{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LXZtrkHg2SoP9udHZ9abWv","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Feature Definition of Done Checklist\n2\t\n3\t**Purpose**: Feature-completion gate for Keystone work. A feature is not done until all applicable items below are complete or explicitly waived with a documented reason, owner, and follow-up date.\n4\t\n5\t---\n6\t\n7\t## Change Information\n8\t\n9\t| Field | Value |\n10\t|-------|-------|\n11\t| Feature / workflow | |\n12\t| Domain | |\n13\t| Change owner | |\n14\t| Date reviewed | |\n15\t| Related scorecard | |\n16\t| Related architecture doc | |\n17\t| Related functional doc | |\n18\t| Related manual doc | |\n19\t\n20\t---\n21\t\n22\t## Checklist\n23\t\n24\t### Workflow Completion\n25\t\n26\t- [ ] Primary operator workflow works end to end\n27\t- [ ] All intended create, read, update, archive, and transition actions are implemented or explicitly documented as intentionally unavailable\n28\t- [ ] Backend behavior and operator-facing UI are both complete where the workflow is user-visible\n29\t- [ ] Background jobs, automation, webhooks, or integrations required by the workflow are complete\n30\t\n31\t### Failure Handling\n32\t\n33\t- [ ] Validation failures return actionable errors\n34\t- [ ] Permission-denied behavior is implemented and verified\n35\t- [ ] Tenant-boundary failures are implemented and verified where applicable\n36\t- [ ] Not-found, conflict, and dependency failure states are handled truthfully\n37\t- [ ] Partial-failure and retry behavior is defined for async or integration flows\n38\t- [ ] UI shows loading, empty, success, and failure states where applicable\n39\t\n40\t### Security, Tenancy, and Audit\n41\t\n42\t- [ ] Access control is deny-by-default and enforced in the backend\n43\t- [ ] Tenant scoping is enforced on all tenant-owned reads and writes\n44\t- [ ] Destructive, archive, approval, and financially sensitive actions have explicit controls\n45\t- [ ] Meaningful state-changing actions create audit records with actor and target context\n46\t- [ ] Sensitive data and privileged operations are not exposed through convenience shortcuts\n47\t\n48\t### Data Integrity and Workflow Controls\n49\t\n50\t- [ ] Important invariants are enforced in the model or database layer\n51\t- [ ] Constraints, foreign keys, uniqueness rules, and validation exist where they should\n52\t- [ ] Workflow statuses or lifecycle stages use explicit transition rules instead of ad hoc flag combinations\n53\t- [ ] Invalid or terminal-state transitions are blocked and tested\n54\t- [ ] Archive, close, approval, and cancellation behavior is deliberate and documented\n55\t\n56\t### Observability and Recovery\n57\t\n58\t- [ ] Logs, audit records, and surfaced errors provide enough context to debug production failures\n59\t- [ ] Critical async or integration paths are idempotent or otherwise safe under replay\n60\t- [ ] Recovery steps exist for operator-facing failure cases\n61\t- [ ] Rollback, compensation, or retry behavior is defined where partial success is possible\n62\t\n63\t### Performance and Scale\n64\t\n65\t- [ ] The design avoids N+1 query patterns and client-side fan-out for core workflows\n66\t- [ ] Search, filtering, sorting, aggregation, and pagination are server-side where data volume warrants it\n67\t- [ ] The workflow is reasonable for realistic tenant size, concurrency, and queue volume\n68\t- [ ] Known scale limits or cost tradeoffs are documented if they exist\n69\t\n70\t### Documentation and Operator Readiness\n71\t\n72\t- [ ] Architecture documentation updated for structural, model, or subsystem changes\n73\t- [ ] Functional documentation updated for behavior, API, and business-rule changes\n74\t- [ ] Manual documentation updated for operator workflow changes\n75\t- [ ] Operator-facing warnings, confirmations, and troubleshooting notes are documented\n76\t\n77\t### Verification Evidence\n78\t\n79\t- [ ] Unit tests added or updated for local behavior and invariants\n80\t- [ ] Integration tests added or updated for boundary behavior and controls\n81\t- [ ] E2E or acceptance coverage added for major operator workflows where warranted\n82\t- [ ] Relevant automated test commands executed and results captured\n83\t- [ ] Manual verification evidence captured for UI-heavy or operationally sensitive changes\n84\t\n85\t### Explicit Deferrals\n86\t\n87\t- [ ] Any deferred work is documented with reason, owner, and target date\n88\t- [ ] No known production-critical issue remains untreated in the shipped scope\n89\t- [ ] Release or handoff notes clearly call out residual risk\n90\t\n91\t---\n92\t\n93\t## Verification Log\n94\t\n95\t| Evidence Type | Command / Artifact | Result | Notes |\n96\t|---------------|--------------------|--------|-------|\n97\t| Unit tests | | | |\n98\t| Integration tests | | | |\n99\t| E2E / acceptance | | | |\n100\t| Manual verification | | | |\n101\t\n102\t---\n103\t\n104\t## Decision\n105\t\n106\t| Field | Value |\n107\t|-------|-------|\n108\t| Outcome | Done / Conditional / Not Done |\n109\t| Blockers | |\n110\t| Waived items | |\n111\t| Owner sign-off | |\n112\t\n113\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"f5a3ad1d-9f71-4600-bf88-be9dfd8b172a","timestamp":"2026-05-17T02:17:52.180Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md","content":"# Feature Definition of Done Checklist\n\n**Purpose**: Feature-completion gate for Keystone work. A feature is not done until all applicable items below are complete or explicitly waived with a documented reason, owner, and follow-up date.\n\n---\n\n## Change Information\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| Feature / workflow | |\n| Domain | |\n| Change owner | |\n| Date reviewed | |\n| Related scorecard | |\n| Related architecture doc | |\n| Related functional doc | |\n| Related manual doc | |\n\n---\n\n## Checklist\n\n### Workflow Completion\n\n- [ ] Primary operator workflow works end to end\n- [ ] All intended create, read, update, archive, and transition actions are implemented or explicitly documented as intentionally unavailable\n- [ ] Backend behavior and operator-facing UI are both complete where the workflow is user-visible\n- [ ] Background jobs, automation, webhooks, or integrations required by the workflow are complete\n\n### Failure Handling\n\n- [ ] Validation failures return actionable errors\n- [ ] Permission-denied behavior is implemented and verified\n- [ ] Tenant-boundary failures are implemented and verified where applicable\n- [ ] Not-found, conflict, and dependency failure states are handled truthfully\n- [ ] Partial-failure and retry behavior is defined for async or integration flows\n- [ ] UI shows loading, empty, success, and failure states where applicable\n\n### Security, Tenancy, and Audit\n\n- [ ] Access control is deny-by-default and enforced in the backend\n- [ ] Tenant scoping is enforced on all tenant-owned reads and writes\n- [ ] Destructive, archive, approval, and financially sensitive actions have explicit controls\n- [ ] Meaningful state-changing actions create audit records with actor and target context\n- [ ] Sensitive data and privileged operations are not exposed through convenience shortcuts\n\n### Data Integrity and Workflow Controls\n\n- [ ] Important invariants are enforced in the model or database layer\n- [ ] Constraints, foreign keys, uniqueness rules, and validation exist where they should\n- [ ] Workflow statuses or lifecycle stages use explicit transition rules instead of ad hoc flag combinations\n- [ ] Invalid or terminal-state transitions are blocked and tested\n- [ ] Archive, close, approval, and cancellation behavior is deliberate and documented\n\n### Observability and Recovery\n\n- [ ] Logs, audit records, and surfaced errors provide enough context to debug production failures\n- [ ] Critical async or integration paths are idempotent or otherwise safe under replay\n- [ ] Recovery steps exist for operator-facing failure cases\n- [ ] Rollback, compensation, or retry behavior is defined where partial success is possible\n\n### Performance and Scale\n\n- [ ] The design avoids N+1 query patterns and client-side fan-out for core workflows\n- [ ] Search, filtering, sorting, aggregation, and pagination are server-side where data volume warrants it\n- [ ] The workflow is reasonable for realistic tenant size, concurrency, and queue volume\n- [ ] Known scale limits or cost tradeoffs are documented if they exist\n\n### Documentation and Operator Readiness\n\n- [ ] Architecture documentation updated for structural, model, or subsystem changes\n- [ ] Functional documentation updated for behavior, API, and business-rule changes\n- [ ] Manual documentation updated for operator workflow changes\n- [ ] Operator-facing warnings, confirmations, and troubleshooting notes are documented\n\n### Verification Evidence\n\n- [ ] Unit tests added or updated for local behavior and invariants\n- [ ] Integration tests added or updated for boundary behavior and controls\n- [ ] E2E or acceptance coverage added for major operator workflows where warranted\n- [ ] Relevant automated test commands executed and results captured\n- [ ] Manual verification evidence captured for UI-heavy or operationally sensitive changes\n\n### Explicit Deferrals\n\n- [ ] Any deferred work is documented with reason, owner, and target date\n- [ ] No known production-critical issue remains untreated in the shipped scope\n- [ ] Release or handoff notes clearly call out residual risk\n\n---\n\n## Verification Log\n\n| Evidence Type | Command / Artifact | Result | Notes |\n|---------------|--------------------|--------|-------|\n| Unit tests | | | |\n| Integration tests | | | |\n| E2E / acceptance | | | |\n| Manual verification | | | |\n\n---\n\n## Decision\n\n| Field | Value |\n|-------|-------|\n| Outcome | Done / Conditional / Not Done |\n| Blockers | |\n| Waived items | |\n| Owner sign-off | |\n\n","numLines":113,"startLine":1,"totalLines":113}}}
