{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015noTFKqAfrtZXC4hFEnzea","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Storage And Search Backends\n2\t\n3\t## Summary\n4\t\n5\tLattice keeps SQLite as the durable source of truth for the graph and memories, but semantic retrieval no longer does brute-force cosine scans on every hot-path query. The daemon now uses a `VectorIndex` abstraction with scoped retrieval and a richer semantic indexing pipeline:\n6\t\n7\t- `VectorStore` as the compatibility backend: SQLite BLOB storage plus exact cosine search\n8\t- `UsearchVectorIndex` as the preferred backend: persisted USearch ANN graph under `.lattice/vectors.usearch`\n9\t- `VectorScope` to distinguish symbol vectors from file-summary vectors while preserving a compatibility default search path\n10\t\n11\tMemory keyword search now uses SQLite FTS5 instead of ad hoc `LIKE` scans.\n12\t\n13\t## Vector Indexing\n14\t\n15\t- `QueryEngine` depends on `VectorIndex`, not on the SQLite store directly.\n16\t- SQLite remains the durable source of truth for vectors in `.lattice/vectors.db`.\n17\t- `vector_keys` stores stable numeric ANN keys for `(file, name, byte_offset)` triples.\n18\t- `vector_index_meta` stores the configured embedding dimension and a generation counter.\n19\t- `vectors.usearch.meta.json` records the persisted ANN generation so startup can detect drift and rebuild from SQLite when needed.\n20\t- Default `search(...)` stays symbol-scoped for compatibility, while `search_in_scope(...)` can target `Symbol`, `FileSummary`, or `All`.\n21\t- The first multi-granularity slice adds deterministic per-file summary vectors alongside symbol vectors.\n22\t\n23\t## Sync Model\n24\t\n25\t- Cold start: the daemon opens the vector backend, warms from disk if generations match, otherwise rebuilds the ANN file from SQLite.\n26\t- Full graph embedding sync: initial indexing and explicit reindex rebuild the semantic index from the current graph snapshot.\n27\t- Incremental sync: watcher updates delete vectors for changed files, re-embed the current nodes for those files, then flush the ANN file.\n28\t- Embedding payloads now include richer symbol-body anchors such as compact summaries, comments/docstrings, error strings, config keys, and routes before they are written to the vector store.\n29\t- Failure mode: if USearch initialization or warm-up fails, Lattice falls back to the exact SQLite backend without changing MCP schemas.\n30\t\n31\t## Retrieval Pipeline\n32\t\n33\t- The query engine now searches both symbol vectors and file-summary vectors before final ranking.\n34\t- Semantic candidates are re-ranked with deterministic graph, identifier, and query-intent signals before final delivery.\n35\t- Identifier-heavy queries still prefer keyword anchors when they are available, so the richer semantic path does not override exact code-first matches.\n36\t\n37\t## Rollout Observability\n38\t\n39\t- Vector sync now logs structured batch stats for mode, backend, graph size, payload size, elapsed time, and throughput.\n40\t- Watcher-triggered syncs log both vector-sync elapsed time and end-to-end watcher overhead.\n41\t- USearch flushes log index and metadata byte deltas so operators can track on-disk growth during rollout.\n42\t\n43\t## Memory Search\n44\t\n45\t- `memories.db` remains the source of truth for rows and metadata.\n46\t- `memories_fts` stores normalized search text for content, linked symbols, and linked files.\n47\t- Existing databases are migrated on open:\n48\t  - missing schema columns are added\n49\t  - FTS5 is created if absent\n50\t  - FTS content is rebuilt from the current non-invalidated memory rows\n51\t- Store, refresh, promote, invalidate, prune, and clear operations keep FTS rows in sync.\n52\t\n53\t## Contract Notes\n54\t\n55\t- MCP/tool response shapes do not change.\n56\t- Runtime storage gains `.lattice/vectors.usearch` and `.lattice/vectors.usearch.meta.json`.\n57\t- Keyword search semantics stay AND-based, ordered by recency, but are now implemented through FTS5 rather than wildcard table scans.\n58\t- Symbol-only search remains the compatibility default; file-summary vectors are available through the scope-aware retrieval path.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01LgCYkkLu5MSqvwzg2iCDvg","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"a5d7b2dc-3335-4999-b673-df1e397ce9f5","timestamp":"2026-05-17T02:18:28.846Z","subagent_type":"Explore","task_description":"Explore docs and plans"}
