wOutgoingLinks` — docs navigation\n- `lattice.findStaleDocs` — check docs after changes\n- `lattice.openDocsWorkbench` — launch docs graph view\n\n---\n\n### 3. **JSON-RPC Stdio Communication** (daemon.ts)\n\n**Protocol:**\n- Request: `{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\", \"id\":N, \"method\":\"...\", \"params\":{...}}`\n- Response: `{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\", \"id\":N, \"result\":{...}}` or `{\"error\":{...}}`\n- **Newline-delimited** stdio; buffered by DaemonManager\n\n**Core Methods:**\n- `lattice/status` — daemon status snapshot (nodes, files, edges)\n- `lattice/reindex` — explicit workspace reindex\n- `lattice/dependents` — get dependents (daemon-side endpoint)\n- `tools/list` — get available MCP tool schemas\n- `tools/call` — dispatch tool with arguments; returns `McpToolResponse`\n\n**Tool Response Shape:**\n```typescript\ninterface McpToolResponse {\n    content?: Array<{ type?: string; text?: string }>;\n}\n```\nText content is parsed as JSON if valid, else returned as string.\n\n**Daemon Lifecycle:**\n- Binary resolved: extension/bin/lattice → PATH → daemon/target/debug/lattice\n- SHA-256 verification before spawn\n- Restart on crash (max 5 retries with backoff)\n- Process killed on extension deactivation\n\n---\n\n### 4. **UI Surfaces for Memory & Diagnostics**\n\n**Sidebar (sidebar.ts):**\n- Graph stats display: nodes, files, edges (live polling, 3s interval)\n- Delivery mix meter: \"X tiny · Y compact · Z full\" (tracks tool response size strategy)\n- Context handle reuse rate meter\n- Outcome memory reuse counter\n- \"Clear Memory\" button dispatches `lattice/clearMemory` request\n\n**Docs Workbench (docsWorkbench.ts):**\n- Renders backlinks & outgoing links graphs with preview snippets\n- Two-way navigation between docs targets\n- State: ready/loading/error/idle with focused node and link counts\n\n**Output Channel:**\n- Tool results displayed with title + separator\n- Context handle + origin logged when present\n- Results rendered as markdown (string) or JSON\n\n**CodeLens (codelens.ts):**\n- Inline \"Show dependents\" action on each symbol\n- Invokes `lattice.showDependents` command\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Compact vs Full Render Modes**\n\nBoth exposed in tool responses and controllable via `render` parameter:\n\n- `hybrid` (default) — markdown summary + JSON payload in response\n- `markdown` — summary text only\n- `json` — structured data only\n\nTools supporting this: `prepare_change`, `plan_edit`, `get_context_capsule`, `diagnose_failure`, `impact_from_diff`, `trace_scenario`, `get_working_set_context`, `get_repo_playbook`, `summarize_subsystem`.\n\n**Size delivery strategy** (sidebar metric):\n- `tiny` — minimal context for quick recovery\n- `compact` — focused context for edit loops\n- `full` — exhaustive context for deep review\n\nTracked in `SessionMetrics` as `compact_task_count`, `widened_task_count`.\n\n---\n\n### 6. **Context Handle / expand_context Pattern**\n\n**Shape:**\n```json\n{\n  \"context_handle\": \"sha256-hex-...omitted...\",\n  \"context_origin\": \"prepare_change\" | \"get_context_capsule\" | \"impact_from_diff\" | ...\n}\n```\n\n**Where Emitted:**\n- All workflow bundles: `prepare_change`, `plan_edit`, `get_context_capsule`, `diagnose_failure`, `impact_from_diff`, `trace_scenario`, `get_working_set_context`, `get_repo_playbook`, `summarize_subsystem`\n- Cached in `ContextHandleCache` (daemon/src/rpc/context_cache.rs)\n\n**expand_context Resolution (expansion.ts line 349–381):**\n- Extension stores `lastContextHandle` + `lastContextOrigin` after each tool call\n- User selects a focus target: `symbol:X`, `file:path/to/file.rs`, `memory:0`, `test:test_name`\n- `expand_context` with handle + focus narrows prior bundle to next delta\n- Supports `max_tokens` to control output size\n\n**Stable Handle Basis** (2026-04-11-stable-follow-up-handles.md):\n- Graph identity: `SymbolId { file, name, byte_offset }`\n- Deterministic encoding replaces name-only `symbol:<name>` fallback\n- Preferred by `expand_context` for exact resolution; legacy `file:` and `symbol:` forms remain backward compatible\n\n---\n\n### 7. **Architecture Docs** (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/architecture/`)\n\n| File | One-Line Summary |\n|------|------------------|\n| `2026-04-11-structured-memory.md` | Structured assertion layer: verification status, confidence reason, freshness policy, provenance, evidence; legacy memory remains compatible. |\n| `2026-04-11-stable-follow-up-handles.md` | Durable graph identity (file+name+byte_offset) replaces name-only targets; expand_context prefers exact stable handles. |\n| `2026-04-11-patch-oriented-planning.md` | plan_edit bundles candidate spans, affected callers, stale doc signals, tests for direct patching; compact/full modes. |\n| `2026-04-11-scenario-tracing.md` | trace_scenario debugs by behavior description; returns execution paths, guards, side effects, failure branches ranked by confidence. |\n| `2026-04-11-storage-and-search-backends.md` | SQLite durable source + USearch ANN vectors; FTS5 memory keyword search; vector scopes distinguish symbols from file summaries. |\n\n---\n\n**Summary:** Lattice exposes 38 MCP tools across 8 domains. Extension is 7 TypeScript files (~6KB total) with 12 command registrations, sidebar stats/metrics, docs graph workbench, and hover/CodeLens providers. JSON-RPC stdio transports tool calls; responses carry context handles for follow-up expansion. Memory is structured with verification, provenance, and freshness metadata. Render modes (compact/full/hybrid) and handle caching enable efficient reuse across edit loops."}],"totalDurationMs":56589,"totalTokens":62234,"totalToolUseCount":20,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2330,"cache_read_input_tokens":57130,"output_tokens":2767,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2330},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":7,"output_to