{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RDjDdnJFRiz86tbrxskniG","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent. Now let me create a comprehensive summary:\n\n## Lattice Daemon Rust Codebase Exploration Report\n\n### 1. **Crate Structure** (`daemon/crates/`)\n\n**lattice-core** (core library):\n- **graph/** — petgraph `DiGraph<GraphNode, EdgeKind>`; nodes are symbols (function/class/type), edges are `Calls|Imports|Implements|Extends|TypeRef|Contains|LinksTo|Mentions|CoChanges`\n- **parser/** — tree-sitter parsers for TypeScript, Python, Rust, Go, Java, Markdown; extracts symbols (`SymbolKind`), signatures, bodies\n- **indexer/** — incremental file-to-graph indexer; batches parse, caches in HashMap<file, ParsedFile>, rebuilds DAG when files change\n- **query/** — `QueryEngine`: intent detection, semantic + keyword search, graph traversal, ranking, budget allocation; produces `ContextCapsule` with pivot nodes and relationships\n- **storage/** — SQLite: graph persisted in `graph.db` (nodes/edges/file_index tables); file hashes cached to detect changes\n- **memory/** — SQLite-backed `MemoryStore` for observations: 80+ column schema (type, scope, verification_status, confidence, linked_symbols/files, provenance, evidence, freshness_policy, contradictions, supersedence chains)\n- **embeddings/** — ONNX embedding engine (384-dim L2-normalized vectors); loads model + tokenizer from `.lattice/models/`; mean pooling with attention mask\n- **intelligence/** — retrieval & ranking: `prepare_change`, `get_context_capsule`, `expand_context`, `plan_edit`, `trace_scenario`, `diagnose_failure`, `get_docs_capsule`, etc. (see #2)\n- **symbols/** — symbol model; stable file handles; language enum\n- **diff/** — change detection and impact analysis\n- **workspace/** — `WorkspaceManager` for multi-repo mode; detects cross-repo edges\n- **watcher/** — file system observer; ignores .git, node_modules, etc.\n- **security/** — permission filtering (likely for multi-tenant/repo access control)\n\n**lattice-daemon** (RPC server):\n- **main.rs** — entry point; loads/saves graph and memories to `.lattice/`; spawns background indexing task; initializes `QueryEngine`, `Indexer`, embedding engine, memory store; coordinates multi-repo workspace\n- **rpc/mcp.rs** — `McpHandler`: routes JSON-RPC methods to 45+ tools (see #2); manages context handles, session metrics, pruning profiles\n- **rpc/server.rs** — `StdioServer`: JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdin/stdout; async request dispatch with cancellation support; Windows binary mode\n- **rpc/protocol.rs** — JSON-RPC request/response types\n- **rpc/context_cache.rs** — in-memory cache for `ExpandContextSeed` handles to avoid re-computing context between tool calls\n- **rpc/session_metrics.rs** — per-session telemetry: tool counts, payload bytes/tokens, context reuse rates, memory writes, compact/tiny budget usage\n- **vector_sync.rs** — background task to embed file summaries into vector index\n- **watcher.rs** — file change listener; triggers incremental re-indexing\n\n---\n\n### 2. **MCP/RPC Entry Point & Tool Registration**\n\nMain entry: `StdioServer::run()` reads line-delimited JSON-RPC from stdin, delegates to `McpHandler::handle_tools_call()`.\n\n**43 registered tools** (in `mcp.rs::handle_tools_list()`):\n- **Workflow tools** (large bundles with handle-based incremental expansion):\n  - `prepare_change` — fix/add/refactor; suggests edit files, symbols, tests, risks, memory\n  - `plan_edit` — patch-oriented planning (like prepare_change, entry-point agnostic)\n  - `get_context_capsule` — unfamiliar code discovery; pivots, nearby symbols, handle\n  - `expand_context` — incremental drill-down using prior handle\n  - `get_working_set_context` — compress working set (already-open files/symbols)\n  - `trace_scenario` — execution paths, guards, side effects, failure branches\n  - `summarize_subsystem` — domain summary without full source load\n  - `impact_from_diff` — downstream impact + tests for a diff\n  - `diagnose_failure` — stack trace → suspect symbols/files/tests\n  - `record_workflow_outcome` — save successful outcomes to branch/repo memory\n\n- **Docs tools**:\n  - `get_docs_capsule` — markdown docs + linked symbols for a query\n  - `get_backlinks` — inbound references to a symbol/file/doc/section\n  - `get_outgoing_links` — outbound references from a target\n  - `find_stale_docs` — docs mentioning changed symbols/files\n  - `get_repo_playbook` — architecture, conventions, high-signal files, durable patterns\n\n- **Memory tools**:\n  - `save_observation`, `list_observations`, `search_memory`, `update_observation`, `delete_observation`, `promote_observation`, `refresh_memory`\n  - `get_session_context` — memories from current + previous sessions\n  - `list_stale_memories` — memories needing refresh\n\n- **Graph/symbol tools**:\n  - `get_skeleton` — file structure (symbols + kinds, dependent counts)\n  - `search_symbols`, `get_symbol` — by name across project\n  - `get_dependencies`, `get_dependents` — symbol's incoming/outgoing edges\n  - `get_impact_graph` — transitive dependents (N hops)\n  - `search_logic_flow` — call chains from A to B\n  - `submit_lsp_edges` — enrich graph from external LSP\n\n- **Project/workspace tools**:\n  - `get_project_rules` — project-specific conventions\n  - `workspace_setup` — language breakdown, recommended config\n  - `index_status` — indexing progress, graph stats, language breakdown\n\n- **Test tools**:\n  - `find_relevant_tests` — tests for files/symbols/diff\n\n- **Admin tools**:\n  - `get_session_metrics` — payload bytes/tokens, handle reuse, memory writes, budget mode distribution\n  - `lattice` — daemon status, graph stats, file count\n\nSession metrics expose:\n- Tool call counts per method\n- Payload bytes/tokens distribution\n- Context handle creation & reuse rates\n- Automatic memory writes & outcome patterns\n- Compact/tiny/full budget allocation counts\n- Dense wire format usage\n- Semantic fallback occurrences\n- Single-anchor task rates\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Storage Layer**\n\n**SQLite Persistence** (at `.lattice/`):\n\n1. **graph.db** — `GraphStore`\n   - Tables: `nodes` (file, name, byte_offset, kind, signature, body, line, end_line, is_exported, language, edit_count, last_modified)\n   - `edges` (from_file, from_name, from_offset, to_file, to_name, to_offset, kind)\n   - `file_index` (file, content_hash, mtime_ns, size_bytes, parser_version, schema_version, last_indexed_at)\n   - `parsed_files` (file, payload JSON)\n   - Indexes: `idx_nodes_file`, `idx_edges_from`, `idx_edges_to`\n\n2. **memories.db** — `MemoryStore`\n   - Table: `memories` (80+ columns)\n     - Core: id, session_id, content, memory_type, scope, confidence\n     - Metadata: linked_symbols, linked_files, workspace_id, branch, refresh_key, source_query\n     - Assertion shape: assertion_type (observation|decision|exploration|pattern|anti_pattern|workflow_outcome|constraint), verification_status (unverified|in_review|verified|stale|contradicted|superseded)\n     - Verification: confidence_reason, supersedes_memory_id, superseded_by_memory_id, contradicts_memory_ids, contradicted_by_memory_ids\n     - Freshness: freshness_policy (session_scoped|branch_scoped|repo_scoped), freshness_policy_detail\n     - Evidence: provenance_json, evidence_json\n     - Staleness: is_stale, stale_reason, is_invalidated\n     - Timestamps: created_at, last_accessed, access_count\n   - Full-text index: `memories_fts` (memory_id, content, linked_symbols, linked_files, unicode61 tokenizer)\n   - Indexes: by created_at, memory_type, session_id, verification_status, superseded_by\n\n3. **Vector index** — `VectorStore` (usearch-backed)\n   - File paths in `.lattice/vector_index/`\n   - Stores embeddings for symbols + file summaries (384-dim, L2-normalized)\n   - Keyed by stable file handles (hash-based identifiers)\n\n**Schema migrations**: Backward-compatible ALTER TABLE in MemoryStore::initialize() for evolving column additions.\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Memory Implementation**\n\nSQLite-backed with rich schema:\n\n**MemoryType enum**: Observation, Decision, Exploration, Pattern, AntiPattern\n\n**MemoryScope enum**: Session, Branch, Repo (durability scopes)\n\n**MemoryFreshnessPolicy enum**: SessionScoped, BranchScoped, RepoScoped (auto-staleness triggers)\n\n**MemoryVerificationStatus enum**: Unverified → InReview → Verified (terminal) OR Stale, Contradicted, Superseded\n\n**Key features**:\n- Confidence scores (0.0–1.0) with reasons\n- Contradict/supersede chains for conflict/resolution tracking\n- Provenance & evidence JSON blobs (source queries, test results, etc.)\n- Access counts for prioritization\n- FTS5 full-text search on content + symbols + files\n- Multi-session recall via query filters (session_id, scope, created_at)\n\n**Observation tools**:\n- `save_observation` (auto-generate UUID if missing)\n- `search_memory` (FTS5 + filter by scope/type/session)\n- `list_observations`, `list_stale_memories`\n- `update_observation`, `refresh_memory`, `promote_observation` (session → branch → repo)\n- `delete_observation` (soft delete via is_invalidated flag)\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Event/Observation/Telemetry Capture**\n\n**Session-level metrics** (in `session_metrics.rs`):\n- Per-tool call: payload_bytes, approx_tokens, context_handle, delivery_mode, wire_format, semantic_fallback_used, outcome_memory_reuse_count\n- Per-task: tool count, byte/token totals, delivery mode, follow-up avoidance, expand suggestions\n- Session summary: total calls, task count, byte/token aggregates, context handle reuse rate, automatic memory write count, budget distribution\n\n**Tracing**: Uses `tracing` crate; logs to stderr with EnvFilter (RUST_LOG env var); messages include:\n- Background indexing progress (file counts, graph stats)\n- Graph persistence (save/load operations)\n- Embedding engine load status\n- Cross-repo edge detection\n- Incremental indexing results (changed/removed counts)\n\n**No event pipeline or external telemetry**: metrics are in-memory per session, exposed via `get_session_metrics` RPC tool.\n\n---\n\n### 6. **Graph Implementation**\n\n**petgraph-backed**:\n- `CodeGraph` wraps `DiGraph<GraphNode, EdgeKind>` + `HashMap<SymbolId, NodeIndex>` for fast lookups\n- Nodes: `GraphNode` (id, kind, name, signature, body, file, line, end_line, is_exported, language, edit_count, last_modified)\n- Edges: 9 kinds (Calls, Imports, Implements, Extends, TypeRef, Contains, LinksTo, Mentions, CoChanges)\n\n**Parsing**:\n- tree-sitter-based per language (TypeScript, Python, Rust, Go, Java, Markdown)\n- Extracts symbol hierarchy, signatures, and edges based on language semantics\n- Caches parsed ASTs in `ParsedFile` model (file, symbols vec, symbols map)\n\n**Indexing** (`indexer.rs`):\n- `Indexer` holds `graph` + `parsed_files` HashMap\n- Incremental: parse new/changed files, replace in map, call `rebuild_graph()` once\n- `GraphBuilder` reconstructs edges from all parsed files (e.g., imports resolved by looking up imported symbol in parsed files)\n- Supports LSP edge injection via `submit_lsp_edges` to enrich graph with call hierarchy from external tools\n\n**Persistence**:\n- `GraphStore::save_graph()` serializes nodes/edges to SQLite\n- `GraphStore::load_graph()` deserializes back to `CodeGraph` on startup\n- Multi-repo mode: `WorkspaceManager` unifies graphs and detects cross-repo edges via symbol resolution\n\n---\n\n### 7. **Retrieval/Ranking Implementation**\n\nLocated in `intelligence/agent.rs` + `query/engine.rs`:\n\n**`get_context_capsule(query, mode)`**:\n1. Intent detection (keyword analysis: \"debug\"→debugging, \"docs\"→docs-first, etc.)\n2. Semantic search (embedding query, threshold ~0.65) + keyword fallback\n3. Graph traversal (1–3 hops, depending on intent)\n4. Ranking: seed hit score + semantic similarity + relationship type weight + edit recency\n5. Budget allocation: compact/full mode adjusts result counts\n6. Output: `ContextCapsule` with pivots, nearby symbols, memory highlights, suggested expand focus, handle for incremental calls\n\n**`prepare_change(query)`**:\n- `get_context_capsule` + impact graph (what breaks if changed?)\n- Recommends edit files + edit spans\n- Suggests relevant tests + risks\n- Includes linked memories (via symbol/file links)\n\n**`plan_edit(query)`**:\n- Similar to prepare_change but entry-agnostic (no prior file knowledge)\n- Bias toward likely edit files + symbols\n- Return `PlanEditBundle` with recommendations\n\n**`expand_context(handle, focus_target)`**:\n- Reuses prior context handle's index state\n- Drill down to specific file/symbol/test/memory\n- Incremental expansion (avoids recomputing everything)\n\n**`get_working_set_context(files, symbols, query)`**:\n- Compress already-open files/symbols into working set\n- Find relevant tests + nearby symbols + likely next changes\n- Budget-aware compression\n\n**`trace_scenario(scenario_description)`**:\n- \"Why does login fail after refresh?\" → execution paths from `loginUser()` → all reachable callees\n- Identify guards (if conditions), side effects, error branches\n- Return call chains + likely failure points\n\n**`summarize_subsystem(query)`**:\n- Quick overview of unfamiliar subsystem\n- Key files + symbols + tests without loading full source\n- Memory-aware (reuse prior session learnings)\n\n**`impact_from_diff(unified_diff)`**:\n- Parse diff for changed files/symbols\n- Compute transitive dependents (impact graph, N hops)\n- Suggest tests to run\n- Risk assessment (frequently edited symbols = higher risk)\n\n**`diagnose_failure(stack_trace)`**:\n- Parse trace; identify suspect symbols/files\n- Show nearby symbols + dependents (what calls the failed function?)\n- Rank by impact graph (what breaks downstream?)\n\n---\n\n### 8. **Verification Engines / Freshness Logic**\n\n**Memory verification**:\n- `MemoryVerificationStatus` enum: Unverified → InReview → Verified (or Stale/Contradicted/Superseded)\n- `MemoryFreshnessPolicy`: SessionScoped (auto-stale at session end), BranchScoped (cross-branch), RepoScoped (durable)\n- `list_stale_memories()` returns unverified or stale memories\n- `refresh_memory()` updates content + clears stale flag\n\n**Graph freshness**:\n- File index caches content_hash + mtime_ns\n- Background watcher detects file changes; incremental indexer parses + rebuidls graph once\n- Schema version + parser version tracked for detecting stale cached parses\n\n**Outcome pattern memory**:\n- `record_workflow_outcome(task, status, files, symbols, tests)` saves successful fixes/additions to branch/repo scope\n- Later workflows can reuse these patterns (e.g., \"I know how to fix login timeout because I recorded the pattern last week\")\n\n**No explicit freshness check between sessions**: relies on staleness flags + manual `promote_observation` calls to escalate session memories to branch/repo scope.\n\n---\n\n### 9. **Test Layout & Conventions**\n\n**By-module tests** (in-tree `tests.rs`):\n- `storage/tests.rs` — graph persistence, incremental indexing\n- `memory/tests.rs` — memory store CRUD, FTS5, staleness\n- `graph/tests.rs` — petgraph operations, edge kinds\n- `parser/tests.rs` — per-language parsing (Rust, TypeScript, Python, etc.)\n- `query/tests.rs` — intent detection, ranking, capsule generation\n- `indexer/tests.rs` — incremental index, graph rebuild\n- `intelligence/agent_tests.rs` — prepare_change, plan_edit, impact analysis\n- `intelligence/benchmark_tests.rs` — scaling tests (large codebases, many symbols)\n- `embeddings/tests.rs` — ONNX embedding correctness\n- `rpc/tests.rs` — JSON-RPC request/response handling\n\n**Run tests**: `cargo test --workspace` (runs all test suites in parallel)\n\n**Fixtures**: Inline test data in test functions; no external fixture files observed.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\nLattice is a **mature, production-grade Rust codebase** with:\n- **Petgraph DAG** for inter-symbol dependencies with 9 edge types\n- **tree-sitter parsers** for 6 languages + Markdown\n- **SQLite dual-store**: graph persistence + rich memory schema (80+ columns, FTS5, contradictions, supersedence chains)\n- **ONNX embeddings**: 384-dim vectors for semantic search\n- **45 MCP tools**: workflow bundles (with handle-based incremental expansion), docs, memory, graph, tests, metrics\n- **Session telemetry**: payload tracking, budget allocation, context handle reuse, automatic memory writes\n- **Multi-repo support**: workspace manager, cross-repo edge detection\n- **Incremental indexing**: file-change detection, cached parses, graph rebuild\n\n**Recommendation**: This is **extend territory**, not fork. The foundation is complete and extensible (tools, storage schema, RPC protocol are all well-designed). Focus on integration, adding new tools, or enhancing retrieval ranking."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"39b93be1-b697-4b6a-a7fa-b2f982f99dfd","timestamp":"2026-05-17T02:20:02.891Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"Explore the Lattice daemon Rust codebase at /home/pete/cadres/lattice/daemon/. Report:\n\n1. The crate structure under daemon/crates/ — list all modules and their high-level responsibilities (lattice-core and lattice-daemon).\n2. Where the main MCP/RPC server entry point lives and how MCP tools are registered.\n3. The current storage layer — what's in SQLite, how schema migrations work, file paths.\n4. The current memory implementation — schema, retrieval, observation tools.\n5. The current event/observation/telemetry capture (if any) — what's recorded, where.\n6. The current graph implementation — petgraph usage, tree-sitter parsers, indexer.\n7. The current retrieval/ranking implementation — `prepare_change`, `get_context_capsule`, etc.\n8. Verification engines or freshness logic that exist today.\n9. Test layout and conventions (cargo test --workspace, fixtures).\n\nCite file paths and key types. Be precise about what exists vs what doesn't. Report in under 800 words; this is groundwork for a build plan that decides whether to fork or extend.","agentId":"a99faae06255f410a","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent. Now let me create a comprehensive summary:\n\n## Lattice Daemon Rust Codebase Exploration Report\n\n### 1. **Crate Structure** (`daemon/crates/`)\n\n**lattice-core** (core library):\n- **graph/** — petgraph `DiGraph<GraphNode, EdgeKind>`; nodes are symbols (function/class/type), edges are `Calls|Imports|Implements|Extends|TypeRef|Contains|LinksTo|Mentions|CoChanges`\n- **parser/** — tree-sitter parsers for TypeScript, Python, Rust, Go, Java, Markdown; extracts symbols (`SymbolKind`), signatures, bodies\n- **indexer/** — incremental file-to-graph indexer; batches parse, caches in HashMap<file, ParsedFile>, rebuilds DAG when files change\n- **query/** — `QueryEngine`: intent detection, semantic + keyword search, graph traversal, ranking, budget allocation; produces `ContextCapsule` with pivot nodes and relationships\n- **storage/** — SQLite: graph persisted in `graph.db` (nodes/edges/file_index tables); file hashes cached to detect changes\n- **memory/** — SQLite-backed `MemoryStore` for observations: 80+ column schema (type, scope, verification_status, confidence, linked_symbols/files, provenance, evidence, freshness_policy, contradictions, supersedence chains)\n- **embeddings/** — ONNX embedding engine (384-dim L2-normalized vectors); loads model + tokenizer from `.lattice/models/`; mean pooling with attention mask\n- **intelligence/** — retrieval & ranking: `prepare_change`, `get_context_capsule`, `expand_context`, `plan_edit`, `trace_scenario`, `diagnose_failure`, `get_docs_capsule`, etc. (see #2)\n- **symbols/** — symbol model; stable file handles; language enum\n- **diff/** — change detection and impact analysis\n- **workspace/** — `WorkspaceManager` for multi-repo mode; detects cross-repo edges\n- **watcher/** — file system observer; ignores .git, node_modules, etc.\n- **security/** — permission filtering (likely for multi-tenant/repo access control)\n\n**lattice-daemon** (RPC server):\n- **main.rs** — entry point; loads/saves graph and memories to `.lattice/`; spawns background indexing task; initializes `QueryEngine`, `Indexer`, embedding engine, memory store; coordinates multi-repo workspace\n- **rpc/mcp.rs** — `McpHandler`: routes JSON-RPC methods to 45+ tools (see #2); manages context handles, session metrics, pruning profiles\n- **rpc/server.rs** — `StdioServer`: JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdin/stdout; async request dispatch with cancellation support; Windows binary mode\n- **rpc/protocol.rs** — JSON-RPC request/response types\n- **rpc/context_cache.rs** — in-memory cache for `ExpandContextSeed` handles to avoid re-computing context between tool calls\n- **rpc/session_metrics.rs** — per-session telemetry: tool counts, payload bytes/tokens, context reuse rates, memory writes, compact/tiny budget usage\n- **vector_sync.rs** — background task to embed file summaries into vector index\n- **watcher.rs** — file change listener; triggers incremental re-indexing\n\n---\n\n### 2. **MCP/RPC Entry Point & Tool Registration**\n\nMain entry: `StdioServer::run()` reads line-delimited JSON-RPC from stdin, delegates to `McpHandler::handle_tools_call()`.\n\n**43 registered tools** (in `mcp.rs::handle_tools_list()`):\n- **Workflow tools** (large bundles with handle-based incremental expansion):\n  - `prepare_change` — fix/add/refactor; suggests edit files, symbols, tests, risks, memory\n  - `plan_edit` — patch-oriented planning (like prepare_change, entry-point agnostic)\n  - `get_context_capsule` — unfamiliar code discovery; pivots, nearby symbols, handle\n  - `expand_context` — incremental drill-down using prior handle\n  - `get_working_set_context` — compress working set (already-open files/symbols)\n  - `trace_scenario` — execution paths, guards, side effects, failure branches\n  - `summarize_subsystem` — domain summary without full source load\n  - `impact_from_diff` — downstream impact + tests for a diff\n  - `diagnose_failure` — stack trace → suspect symbols/files/tests\n  - `record_workflow_outcome` — save successful outcomes to branch/repo memory\n\n- **Docs tools**:\n  - `get_docs_capsule` — markdown docs + linked symbols for a query\n  - `get_backlinks` — inbound references to a symbol/file/doc/section\n  - `get_outgoing_links` — outbound references from a target\n  - `find_stale_docs` — docs mentioning changed symbols/files\n  - `get_repo_playbook` — architecture, conventions, high-signal files, durable patterns\n\n- **Memory tools**:\n  - `save_observation`, `list_observations`, `search_memory`, `update_observation`, `delete_observation`, `promote_observation`, `refresh_memory`\n  - `get_session_context` — memories from current + previous sessions\n  - `list_stale_memories` — memories needing refresh\n\n- **Graph/symbol tools**:\n  - `get_skeleton` — file structure (symbols + kinds, dependent counts)\n  - `search_symbols`, `get_symbol` — by name across project\n  - `get_dependencies`, `get_dependents` — symbol's incoming/outgoing edges\n  - `get_impact_graph` — transitive dependents (N hops)\n  - `search_logic_flow` — call chains from A to B\n  - `submit_lsp_edges` — enrich graph from external LSP\n\n- **Project/workspace tools**:\n  - `get_project_rules` — project-specific conventions\n  - `workspace_setup` — language breakdown, recommended config\n  - `index_status` — indexing progress, graph stats, language breakdown\n\n- **Test tools**:\n  - `find_relevant_tests` — tests for files/symbols/diff\n\n- **Admin tools**:\n  - `get_session_metrics` — payload bytes/tokens, handle reuse, memory writes, budget mode distribution\n  - `lattice` — daemon status, graph stats, file count\n\nSession metrics expose:\n- Tool call counts per method\n- Payload bytes/tokens distribution\n- Context handle creation & reuse rates\n- Automatic memory writes & outcome patterns\n- Compact/tiny/full budget allocation counts\n- Dense wire format usage\n- Semantic fallback occurrences\n- Single-anchor task rates\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Storage Layer**\n\n**SQLite Persistence** (at `.lattice/`):\n\n1. **graph.db** — `GraphStore`\n   - Tables: `nodes` (file, name, byte_offset, kind, signature, body, line, end_line, is_exported, language, edit_count, last_modified)\n   - `edges` (from_file, from_name, from_offset, to_file, to_name, to_offset, kind)\n   - `file_index` (file, content_hash, mtime_ns, size_bytes, parser_version, schema_version, last_indexed_at)\n   - `parsed_files` (file, payload JSON)\n   - Indexes: `idx_nodes_file`, `idx_edges_from`, `idx_edges_to`\n\n2. **memories.db** — `MemoryStore`\n   - Table: `memories` (80+ columns)\n     - Core: id, session_id, content, memory_type, scope, confidence\n     - Metadata: linked_symbols, linked_files, workspace_id, branch, refresh_key, source_query\n     - Assertion shape: assertion_type (observation|decision|exploration|pattern|anti_pattern|workflow_outcome|constraint), verification_status (unverified|in_review|verified|stale|contradicted|superseded)\n     - Verification: confidence_reason, supersedes_memory_id, superseded_by_memory_id, contradicts_memory_ids, contradicted_by_memory_ids\n     - Freshness: freshness_policy (session_scoped|branch_scoped|repo_scoped), freshness_policy_detail\n     - Evidence: provenance_json, evidence_json\n     - Staleness: is_stale, stale_reason, is_invalidated\n     - Timestamps: created_at, last_accessed, access_count\n   - Full-text index: `memories_fts` (memory_id, content, linked_symbols, linked_files, unicode61 tokenizer)\n   - Indexes: by created_at, memory_type, session_id, verification_status, superseded_by\n\n3. **Vector index** — `VectorStore` (usearch-backed)\n   - File paths in `.lattice/vector_index/`\n   - Stores embeddings for symbols + file summaries (384-dim, L2-normalized)\n   - Keyed by stable file handles (hash-based identifiers)\n\n**Schema migrations**: Backward-compatible ALTER TABLE in MemoryStore::initialize() for evolving column additions.\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Memory Implementation**\n\nSQLite-backed with rich schema:\n\n**MemoryType enum**: Observation, Decision, Exploration, Pattern, AntiPattern\n\n**MemoryScope enum**: Session, Branch, Repo (durability scopes)\n\n**MemoryFreshnessPolicy enum**: SessionScoped, BranchScoped, RepoScoped (auto-staleness triggers)\n\n**MemoryVerificationStatus enum**: Unverified → InReview → Verified (terminal) OR Stale, Contradicted, Superseded\n\n**Key features**:\n- Confidence scores (0.0–1.0) with reasons\n- Contradict/supersede chains for conflict/resolution tracking\n- Provenance & evidence JSON blobs (source queries, test results, etc.)\n- Access counts for prioritization\n- FTS5 full-text search on content + symbols + files\n- Multi-session recall via query filters (session_id, scope, created_at)\n\n**Observation tools**:\n- `save_observation` (auto-generate UUID if missing)\n- `search_memory` (FTS5 + filter by scope/type/session)\n- `list_observations`, `list_stale_memories`\n- `update_observation`, `refresh_memory`, `promote_observation` (session → branch → repo)\n- `delete_observation` (soft delete via is_invalidated flag)\n\n---\n\n### 5. **Event/Observation/Telemetry Capture**\n\n**Session-level metrics** (in `session_metrics.rs`):\n- Per-tool call: payload_bytes, approx_tokens, context_handle, delivery_mode, wire_format, semantic_fallback_used, outcome_memory_reuse_count\n- Per-task: tool count, byte/token totals, delivery mode, follow-up avoidance, expand suggestions\n- Session summary: total calls, task count, byte/token aggregates, context handle reuse rate, automatic memory write count, budget distribution\n\n**Tracing**: Uses `tracing` crate; logs to stderr with EnvFilter (RUST_LOG env var); messages include:\n- Background indexing progress (file counts, graph stats)\n- Graph persistence (save/load operations)\n- Embedding engine load status\n- Cross-repo edge detection\n- Incremental indexing results (changed/removed counts)\n\n**No event pipeline or external telemetry**: metrics are in-memory per session, exposed via `get_session_metrics` RPC tool.\n\n---\n\n### 6. **Graph Implementation**\n\n**petgraph-backed**:\n- `CodeGraph` wraps `DiGraph<GraphNode, EdgeKind>` + `HashMap<SymbolId, NodeIndex>` for fast lookups\n- Nodes: `GraphNode` (id, kind, name, signature, body, file, line, end_line, is_exported, language, edit_count, last_modified)\n- Edges: 9 kinds (Calls, Imports, Implements, Extends, TypeRef, Contains, LinksTo, Mentions, CoChanges)\n\n**Parsing**:\n- tree-sitter-based per language (TypeScript, Python, Rust, Go, Java, Markdown)\n- Extracts symbol hierarchy, signatures, and edges based on language semantics\n- Caches parsed ASTs in `ParsedFile` model (file, symbols vec, symbols map)\n\n**Indexing** (`indexer.rs`):\n- `Indexer` holds `graph` + `parsed_files` HashMap\n- Incremental: parse new/changed files, replace in map, call `rebuild_graph()` once\n- `GraphBuilder` reconstructs edges from all parsed files (e.g., imports resolved by looking up imported symbol in parsed files)\n- Supports LSP edge injection via `submit_lsp_edges` to enrich graph with call hierarchy from external tools\n\n**Persistence**:\n- `GraphStore::save_graph()` serializes nodes/edges to SQLite\n- `GraphStore::load_graph()` deserializes back to `CodeGraph` on startup\n- Multi-repo mode: `WorkspaceManager` unifies graphs and detects cross-repo edges via symbol resolution\n\n---\n\n### 7. **Retrieval/Ranking Implementation**\n\nLocated in `intelligence/agent.rs` + `query/engine.rs`:\n\n**`get_context_capsule(query, mode)`**:\n1. Intent detection (keyword analysis: \"debug\"→debugging, \"docs\"→docs-first, etc.)\n2. Semantic search (embedding query, threshold ~0.65) + keyword fallback\n3. Graph traversal (1–3 hops, depending on intent)\n4. Ranking: seed hit score + semantic similarity + relationship type weight + edit recency\n5. Budget allocation: compact/full mode adjusts result counts\n6. Output: `ContextCapsule` with pivots, nearby symbols, memory highlights, suggested expand focus, handle for incremental calls\n\n**`prepare_change(query)`**:\n- `get_context_capsule` + impact graph (what breaks if changed?)\n- Recommends edit files + edit spans\n- Suggests relevant tests + risks\n- Includes linked memories (via symbol/file links)\n\n**`plan_edit(query)`**:\n- Similar to prepare_change but entry-agnostic (no prior file knowledge)\n- Bias toward likely edit files + symbols\n- Return `PlanEditBundle` with recommendations\n\n**`expand_context(handle, focus_target)`**:\n- Reuses prior context handle's index state\n- Drill down to specific file/symbol/test/memory\n- Incremental expansion (avoids recomputing everything)\n\n**`get_working_set_context(files, symbols, query)`**:\n- Compress already-open files/symbols into working set\n- Find relevant tests + nearby symbols + likely next changes\n- Budget-aware compression\n\n**`trace_scenario(scenario_description)`**:\n- \"Why does login fail after refresh?\" → execution paths from `loginUser()` → all reachable callees\n- Identify guards (if conditions), side effects, error branches\n- Return call chains + likely failure points\n\n**`summarize_subsystem(query)`**:\n- Quick overview of unfamiliar subsystem\n- Key files + symbols + tests without loading full source\n- Memory-aware (reuse prior session learnings)\n\n**`impact_from_diff(unified_diff)`**:\n- Parse diff for changed files/symbols\n- Compute transitive dependents (impact graph, N hops)\n- Suggest tests to run\n- Risk assessment (frequently edited symbols = higher risk)\n\n**`diagnose_failure(stack_trace)`**:\n- Parse trace; identify suspect symbols/files\n- Show nearby symbols + dependents (what calls the failed function?)\n- Rank by impact graph (what breaks downstream?)\n\n---\n\n### 8. **Verification Engines / Freshness Logic**\n\n**Memory verification**:\n- `MemoryVerificationStatus` enum: Unverified → InReview → Verified (or Stale/Contradicted/Superseded)\n- `MemoryFreshnessPolicy`: SessionScoped (auto-stale at session end), BranchScoped (cross-branch), RepoScoped (durable)\n- `list_stale_memories()` returns unverified or stale memories\n- `refresh_memory()` updates content + clears stale flag\n\n**Graph freshness**:\n- File index caches content_hash + mtime_ns\n- Background watcher detects file changes; incremental indexer parses + rebuidls graph once\n- Schema version + parser version tracked for detecting stale cached parses\n\n**Outcome pattern memory**:\n- `record_workflow_outcome(task, status, files, symbols, tests)` saves successful fixes/additions to branch/repo scope\n- Later workflows can reuse these patterns (e.g., \"I know how to fix login timeout because I recorded the pattern last week\")\n\n**No explicit freshness check between sessions**: relies on staleness flags + manual `promote_observation` calls to escalate session memories to branch/repo scope.\n\n---\n\n### 9. **Test Layout & Conventions**\n\n**By-module tests** (in-tree `tests.rs`):\n- `storage/tests.rs` — graph persistence, incremental indexing\n- `memory/tests.rs` — memory store CRUD, FTS5, staleness\n- `graph/tests.rs` — petgraph operations, edge kinds\n- `parser/tests.rs` — per-language parsing (Rust, TypeScript, Python, etc.)\n- `query/tests.rs` — intent detection, ranking, capsule generation\n- `indexer/tests.rs` — incremental index, graph rebuild\n- `intelligence/agent_tests.rs` — prepare_change, plan_edit, impact analysis\n- `intelligence/benchmark_tests.rs` — scaling tests (large codebases, many symbols)\n- `embeddings/tests.rs` — ONNX embedding correctness\n- `rpc/tests.rs` — JSON-RPC request/response handling\n\n**Run tests**: `cargo test --workspace` (runs all test suites in parallel)\n\n**Fixtures**: Inline test data in test functions; no external fixture files observed.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\nLattice is a **mature, production-grade Rust codebase** with:\n- **Petgraph DAG** for inter-symbol dependencies with 9 edge types\n- **tree-sitter parsers** for 6 languages + Markdown\n- **SQLite dual-store**: graph persistence + rich memory schema (80+ columns, FTS5, contradictions, supersedence chains)\n- **ONNX embeddings**: 384-dim vectors for semantic search\n- **45 MCP tools**: workflow bundles (with handle-based incremental expansion), docs, memory, graph, tests, metrics\n- **Session telemetry**: payload tracking, budget allocation, context handle reuse, automatic memory writes\n- **Multi-repo support**: workspace manager, cross-repo edge detection\n- **Incremental indexing**: file-change detection, cached parses, graph rebuild\n\n**Recommendation**: This is **extend territory**, not fork. The foundation is complete and extensible (tools, storage schema, RPC protocol are all well-designed). Focus on integration, adding new tools, or enhancing retrieval ranking."}],"totalDurationMs":113815,"totalTokens":69153,"totalToolUseCount":38,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1295,"cache_read_input_tokens":63206,"output_tokens":4652,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1295},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":4652,"cache_read_input_tokens":63206,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1295,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1295,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"toolStats":{"readCount":20,"searchCount":0,"bashCount":18,"editFileCount":0,"linesAdded":0,"linesRemoved":0,"otherToolCount":0}}}
