{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01JraPN454XQxqXddhC3Pid5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017pUgKMNHs9AuKm96kkQfas","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/plan.md","content":"# Build Plan — Cognitive Workspace Fork\n\n**Spec:** [`../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md`](../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md)\n**Context:** [`context.md`](context.md)\n**Harness contract:** [`tasks.json`](tasks.json)\n**Tasks directory:** [`tasks/`](tasks/)\n**Reviews directory:** `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/` (created by review tasks during execution)\n**Total tasks:** 89 (66 work tasks + 18 reviews + 5 contract/gate reviews) — see [`tasks.json`](tasks.json)\n**Date assembled:** 2026-05-16\n\n---\n\n## 1. Reading order\n\nIf you are an executor picking up this plan cold, read in this order:\n\n1. The spec — [`../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md`](../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md). Don't summarize it; read it.\n2. The context file — [`context.md`](context.md). Carry-forward inventory, gap inventory, fork-or-extend evidence, verification discipline.\n3. This plan — for sequencing and review boundaries.\n4. The first unexecuted task file under [`tasks/`](tasks/).\n5. [`tasks.json`](tasks.json) only as the machine-readable contract for the harness, not as documentation.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Phase-by-phase sequencing\n\nThe eleven spec phases drive the task ordering. Every phase ends in a review (`Rxx`). Contract-gate reviews sit at boundaries where multiple substrates interlock.\n\n| Phase | Spec § | Task IDs | Closing review | Why this order |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 — Fork Foundation | §Phase 0 | T01 → T04 | **R05** | Fork-or-extend decision must precede any structural code change; baseline benchmarks must exist before retrieval changes have anything to regress against. |\n| 1 — Identity | §Phase 1 | T06 → T09 | **R10** | Identity precedes events (events that reference unstable names cannot be replayed) and precedes memory (memory links target stable IDs). |\n| 2 — Event Log | §Phase 2 | T11 → T17 | **R18** | The event log is the substrate that makes consolidation and usefulness measurement possible. Built once identity is stable. |\n| 3 — Memory Graph | §Phase 3 | T19 → T24 | **R25** | First-class memory links, evidence, accesses, scores. Migration from existing `memories` rows happens here. |\n| **Contract Gate** | cross-layer | — | **R26** | Identity ↔ Event Log ↔ Memory round-trip contracts; identity must serialize cleanly through events into memory references. |\n| 4 — Retrieval V1 | §Phase 4 | T27 → T32 | **R33** | Intent classifier, anchor extractor, hybrid candidates, explainable scoring. Forward-compatible with Phase 5 working memory per spec §Phase 4 scope constraint. |\n| 5 — Working Memory | §Phase 5 | T34 → T37 | **R38** | Explicit per-task state replaces implicit prompt accumulation. Built on retrieval. |\n| 6 — Consolidation | §Phase 6 | T39 → T46 | **R47** | Deterministic + LLM-driven jobs. Honors spec §Phase 6 \"LLM-driven consolidation\" constraints: proposal-only, provenance, queue bounds, budgets. |\n| 7 — Verification + Freshness | §Phase 7 | T48 → T53 | **R54** | Keeps memory honest. Stale-label discipline + scope-leak prevention. |\n| **Contract Gate** | cross-layer | — | **R55** | Memory ↔ Verification ↔ Retrieval round-trip: stale memory never returned as trusted, contradictions surface, scope filters enforced. |\n| 8 — Workflow Engine V2 | §Phase 8 | T56 → T62 | **R63** | Redesigned workflow tools + 10 new memory tools, audited per spec §Phase 8 \"Tool surface discipline\". |\n| **Contract Gate** | cross-layer | — | **R64** | MCP schema regression: every old tool either preserved, deprecated with shim, or removed-with-migration-note; every new tool has compact/full/diagnostic mode coverage. |\n| 9 — Metrics + Evaluation | §Phase 9 | T65 → T69 | **R70** | Metric collection, golden benchmark suite, regression dashboard. Targets all numeric goals from spec §Measurable Success Criteria. |\n| 10 — Human Review UI | §Phase 10 | T71 → T77 | **R78** | Extension-side review panel for memory inbox, queues, event/retrieval views. UI-specification compliance verified here. |\n| **Contract Gate** | cross-layer | — | **R79** | Extension ↔ Daemon JSON-RPC for review-UI tools; full round-trip evidence captured. |\n| 11 — Hardening | §Phase 11 | T80 → T86 | **R87** | Large-repo perf, concurrency, recovery, corruption, partial-index, workspace-boundary, migration, MCP compat; plus the full documentation suite. |\n| **DoD gate** | shared standard | — | **R88** | Definition-of-done checklist applied to the whole fork; no item left unchecked or silently waived. |\n| **Final** | end-to-end | — | **R89** | Spec coverage matrix, measurable-success evidence, risk-control evidence, full build + test + extension run. |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Dependency principles\n\n- **Reviews block downstream work.** No backend task in a phase starts until the previous phase's review is closed.\n- **Contract gates block downstream phases.** R26, R55, R64, R79 each block the phases that depend on the contract they certify.\n- **Documentation tasks (T02, T03, T16, T22, T43, T61, T85, T86) ship in the same logical group as their code.** Doc updates do not wait for the final hardening phase.\n- **Tests inside a phase run after the substrate they cover.** A phase's closing tests task (e.g. T17, T24, T32, T37, T46, T53) depends on all the implementation tasks for that phase.\n- **The final readiness review (R89) depends on every other review.** That guarantees no review was silently skipped.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Cross-cutting standards enforcement\n\nEvery phase obeys, and every closing review certifies, these standards:\n\n| Standard | Where it is enforced |\n|---|---|\n| Cadres coding standard (`shared/templates/coding.md`) — hard limits, single source of truth, naming, error handling, no broken windows | Every backend/frontend task body lists \"Coding-standard checks\" with file/function/nesting limits and the dup-detect grep. Every review template has a `## Coding-standard alignment` section. |\n| UI specification (`shared/templates/ui-specification.md`) | All Phase 10 tasks (T71–T77) plus R78 verify: `<dialog>` not `window.confirm`, i18n via `i18n.t(...)`, `SearchableSelect` for ID fields, parseApiError + toast on mutations. |\n| Definition-of-done checklist (`shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md`) | R88 walks the full checklist explicitly. Earlier reviews check the subset relevant to their phase. |\n| Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`) | Every doc task adds Markdown-heading references when documenting authoritative behavior. Every backend task respects backward compatibility per AGENTS.md. The deploy sequence (`pkill -f lattice && cp …`) is referenced in T86 recovery playbook. |\n| Execution philosophy (`/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md`) | No task says \"TODO\" or \"future work\". Every phase ships in full inside this build. |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Verification discipline (summary)\n\nVerification commands in [`tasks.json`](tasks.json) are real shell commands runnable from the repo root. Categories:\n\n- `cd daemon && cargo build --release` — proves the workspace still compiles after each backend change.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p <crate> --lib <module>::<test>` — scoped unit/integration tests; failures map cleanly to a single task.\n- `cd daemon && cargo bench --bench <name> -- --warm-up-time 1 --measurement-time 3` — quick benches that catch P99 regressions on hot paths.\n- `cd extension && npm run compile && npm run lint && npm test` — extension TypeScript compile, lint, and runner.\n- `test -f <path>` + `grep -q '## Heading' <path>` — doc-producing tasks confirm structural completeness.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib contract_tests::<x>` — contract-gate tasks have their own dedicated test module.\n\nThe final readiness review (R89) runs the full `cargo test --workspace`, full extension compile/lint/test, and asserts every prior review file exists and is closed.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Out-of-scope (per spec audit)\n\nThe spec lists nothing out of scope. This plan plans all of it. The \"First Implementation Slice\" steps in the spec (event log → memory graph → retrieval V1 → consolidation → verification) appear first inside their phases, but every later phase still ships in this build per the execution philosophy.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Files this plan produces (summary)\n\nThe complete file inventory for the build is the union of every `files_expected` array in [`tasks.json`](tasks.json). Major groupings:\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/**` — Phase 1.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/**` — Phase 2.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/**` — Phase 3.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/**` — Phase 4.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/**` — Phase 5.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/**` — Phase 6.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/**` — Phase 7.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/**` — Phase 9.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/**` — Phase 11.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/contract_tests/**` — cross-layer gates.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/**` and `rpc/memory_v2/**` — Phase 8.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/event_capture.rs`, `working_memory_tool.rs`, `metrics_surface.rs`, `mcp_schema_tests.rs`, `mcp_compat_tests.rs` — instrumentation + contract tests.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/bin/lattice_report.rs` — CLI regression report.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/benches/**` — baseline + benchmark suites.\n- `extension/src/review/**` — Phase 10 review UI.\n- `extension/src/test/**` — extension UI smoke + contract tests.\n- `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-*.md` — design notes per phase.\n- `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-*.md` — operator + migration + benchmark + UI guides + runbook + recovery playbook.\n- `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R*.md` — all review outputs.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Where the per-task briefs live\n\nEvery task (`Txx`) and every review (`Rxx`) has a markdown file under [`tasks/`](tasks/) with: goal, prerequisites, inputs, steps, files-expected, verification commands, coding-standard checks, and definition-of-done for that task. Executors should open the next pending task's file before touching code.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":203,"cache_read_input_tokens":124691,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":203},"output_tokens":51,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"2a58cc9d-5fba-4ac2-b3c9-8689fcc4109e","request_id":"req_011Cb7MRFkmnNxAVd4hxWkaT"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017pUgKMNHs9AuKm96kkQfas","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/plan.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"516bab7b-a81b-49dd-b7dd-2e3b45e927a8","timestamp":"2026-05-17T02:29:57.556Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/plan.md","content":"# Build Plan — Cognitive Workspace Fork\n\n**Spec:** [`../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md`](../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md)\n**Context:** [`context.md`](context.md)\n**Harness contract:** [`tasks.json`](tasks.json)\n**Tasks directory:** [`tasks/`](tasks/)\n**Reviews directory:** `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/` (created by review tasks during execution)\n**Total tasks:** 89 (66 work tasks + 18 reviews + 5 contract/gate reviews) — see [`tasks.json`](tasks.json)\n**Date assembled:** 2026-05-16\n\n---\n\n## 1. Reading order\n\nIf you are an executor picking up this plan cold, read in this order:\n\n1. The spec — [`../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md`](../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md). Don't summarize it; read it.\n2. The context file — [`context.md`](context.md). Carry-forward inventory, gap inventory, fork-or-extend evidence, verification discipline.\n3. This plan — for sequencing and review boundaries.\n4. The first unexecuted task file under [`tasks/`](tasks/).\n5. [`tasks.json`](tasks.json) only as the machine-readable contract for the harness, not as documentation.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Phase-by-phase sequencing\n\nThe eleven spec phases drive the task ordering. Every phase ends in a review (`Rxx`). Contract-gate reviews sit at boundaries where multiple substrates interlock.\n\n| Phase | Spec § | Task IDs | Closing review | Why this order |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 0 — Fork Foundation | §Phase 0 | T01 → T04 | **R05** | Fork-or-extend decision must precede any structural code change; baseline benchmarks must exist before retrieval changes have anything to regress against. |\n| 1 — Identity | §Phase 1 | T06 → T09 | **R10** | Identity precedes events (events that reference unstable names cannot be replayed) and precedes memory (memory links target stable IDs). |\n| 2 — Event Log | §Phase 2 | T11 → T17 | **R18** | The event log is the substrate that makes consolidation and usefulness measurement possible. Built once identity is stable. |\n| 3 — Memory Graph | §Phase 3 | T19 → T24 | **R25** | First-class memory links, evidence, accesses, scores. Migration from existing `memories` rows happens here. |\n| **Contract Gate** | cross-layer | — | **R26** | Identity ↔ Event Log ↔ Memory round-trip contracts; identity must serialize cleanly through events into memory references. |\n| 4 — Retrieval V1 | §Phase 4 | T27 → T32 | **R33** | Intent classifier, anchor extractor, hybrid candidates, explainable scoring. Forward-compatible with Phase 5 working memory per spec §Phase 4 scope constraint. |\n| 5 — Working Memory | §Phase 5 | T34 → T37 | **R38** | Explicit per-task state replaces implicit prompt accumulation. Built on retrieval. |\n| 6 — Consolidation | §Phase 6 | T39 → T46 | **R47** | Deterministic + LLM-driven jobs. Honors spec §Phase 6 \"LLM-driven consolidation\" constraints: proposal-only, provenance, queue bounds, budgets. |\n| 7 — Verification + Freshness | §Phase 7 | T48 → T53 | **R54** | Keeps memory honest. Stale-label discipline + scope-leak prevention. |\n| **Contract Gate** | cross-layer | — | **R55** | Memory ↔ Verification ↔ Retrieval round-trip: stale memory never returned as trusted, contradictions surface, scope filters enforced. |\n| 8 — Workflow Engine V2 | §Phase 8 | T56 → T62 | **R63** | Redesigned workflow tools + 10 new memory tools, audited per spec §Phase 8 \"Tool surface discipline\". |\n| **Contract Gate** | cross-layer | — | **R64** | MCP schema regression: every old tool either preserved, deprecated with shim, or removed-with-migration-note; every new tool has compact/full/diagnostic mode coverage. |\n| 9 — Metrics + Evaluation | §Phase 9 | T65 → T69 | **R70** | Metric collection, golden benchmark suite, regression dashboard. Targets all numeric goals from spec §Measurable Success Criteria. |\n| 10 — Human Review UI | §Phase 10 | T71 → T77 | **R78** | Extension-side review panel for memory inbox, queues, event/retrieval views. UI-specification compliance verified here. |\n| **Contract Gate** | cross-layer | — | **R79** | Extension ↔ Daemon JSON-RPC for review-UI tools; full round-trip evidence captured. |\n| 11 — Hardening | §Phase 11 | T80 → T86 | **R87** | Large-repo perf, concurrency, recovery, corruption, partial-index, workspace-boundary, migration, MCP compat; plus the full documentation suite. |\n| **DoD gate** | shared standard | — | **R88** | Definition-of-done checklist applied to the whole fork; no item left unchecked or silently waived. |\n| **Final** | end-to-end | — | **R89** | Spec coverage matrix, measurable-success evidence, risk-control evidence, full build + test + extension run. |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Dependency principles\n\n- **Reviews block downstream work.** No backend task in a phase starts until the previous phase's review is closed.\n- **Contract gates block downstream phases.** R26, R55, R64, R79 each block the phases that depend on the contract they certify.\n- **Documentation tasks (T02, T03, T16, T22, T43, T61, T85, T86) ship in the same logical group as their code.** Doc updates do not wait for the final hardening phase.\n- **Tests inside a phase run after the substrate they cover.** A phase's closing tests task (e.g. T17, T24, T32, T37, T46, T53) depends on all the implementation tasks for that phase.\n- **The final readiness review (R89) depends on every other review.** That guarantees no review was silently skipped.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Cross-cutting standards enforcement\n\nEvery phase obeys, and every closing review certifies, these standards:\n\n| Standard | Where it is enforced |\n|---|---|\n| Cadres coding standard (`shared/templates/coding.md`) — hard limits, single source of truth, naming, error handling, no broken windows | Every backend/frontend task body lists \"Coding-standard checks\" with file/function/nesting limits and the dup-detect grep. Every review template has a `## Coding-standard alignment` section. |\n| UI specification (`shared/templates/ui-specification.md`) | All Phase 10 tasks (T71–T77) plus R78 verify: `<dialog>` not `window.confirm`, i18n via `i18n.t(...)`, `SearchableSelect` for ID fields, parseApiError + toast on mutations. |\n| Definition-of-done checklist (`shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md`) | R88 walks the full checklist explicitly. Earlier reviews check the subset relevant to their phase. |\n| Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`) | Every doc task adds Markdown-heading references when documenting authoritative behavior. Every backend task respects backward compatibility per AGENTS.md. The deploy sequence (`pkill -f lattice && cp …`) is referenced in T86 recovery playbook. |\n| Execution philosophy (`/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md`) | No task says \"TODO\" or \"future work\". Every phase ships in full inside this build. |\n\n---\n\n## 5. Verification discipline (summary)\n\nVerification commands in [`tasks.json`](tasks.json) are real shell commands runnable from the repo root. Categories:\n\n- `cd daemon && cargo build --release` — proves the workspace still compiles after each backend change.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p <crate> --lib <module>::<test>` — scoped unit/integration tests; failures map cleanly to a single task.\n- `cd daemon && cargo bench --bench <name> -- --warm-up-time 1 --measurement-time 3` — quick benches that catch P99 regressions on hot paths.\n- `cd extension && npm run compile && npm run lint && npm test` — extension TypeScript compile, lint, and runner.\n- `test -f <path>` + `grep -q '## Heading' <path>` — doc-producing tasks confirm structural completeness.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib contract_tests::<x>` — contract-gate tasks have their own dedicated test module.\n\nThe final readiness review (R89) runs the full `cargo test --workspace`, full extension compile/lint/test, and asserts every prior review file exists and is closed.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Out-of-scope (per spec audit)\n\nThe spec lists nothing out of scope. This plan plans all of it. The \"First Implementation Slice\" steps in the spec (event log → memory graph → retrieval V1 → consolidation → verification) appear first inside their phases, but every later phase still ships in this build per the execution philosophy.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Files this plan produces (summary)\n\nThe complete file inventory for the build is the union of every `files_expected` array in [`tasks.json`](tasks.json). Major groupings:\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/**` — Phase 1.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/**` — Phase 2.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/**` — Phase 3.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/**` — Phase 4.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/**` — Phase 5.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/**` — Phase 6.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/**` — Phase 7.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/**` — Phase 9.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/**` — Phase 11.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/contract_tests/**` — cross-layer gates.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/workflow_v2/**` and `rpc/memory_v2/**` — Phase 8.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/event_capture.rs`, `working_memory_tool.rs`, `metrics_surface.rs`, `mcp_schema_tests.rs`, `mcp_compat_tests.rs` — instrumentation + contract tests.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/bin/lattice_report.rs` — CLI regression report.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/benches/**` — baseline + benchmark suites.\n- `extension/src/review/**` — Phase 10 review UI.\n- `extension/src/test/**` — extension UI smoke + contract tests.\n- `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-*.md` — design notes per phase.\n- `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-*.md` — operator + migration + benchmark + UI guides + runbook + recovery playbook.\n- `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R*.md` — all review outputs.\n\n---\n\n## 8. Where the per-task briefs live\n\nEvery task (`Txx`) and every review (`Rxx`) has a markdown file under [`tasks/`](tasks/) with: goal, prerequisites, inputs, steps, files-expected, verification commands, coding-standard checks, and definition-of-done for that task. Executors should open the next pending task's file before touching code.\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false}}
