{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013ZXuTanJH7X6D7LHKK4aiQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YB5hoQD42WUiscsyfBonC7","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T03.md","content":"# T03 — Phase 0 — Crate/module boundary plan + storage migration policy\n\n**Phase:** 0\n**Type:** foundation\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** T01, T02\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 0: Fork Foundation](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-0-fork-foundation)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task fixes the crate layout and storage migration ordering before any Phase 1+ backend task writes code. It names the new crates (`lattice-identity`, `lattice-events`, `lattice-memory`, `lattice-retrieval`, `lattice-working-memory`, `lattice-consolidation`, `lattice-verification`) that will live under `daemon/crates/` (or documents the case for keeping each as a module inside `lattice-core` instead) and specifies the binding storage migration order plus rollback steps for every schema introduction in Phases 2 through 7. Without this contract, individual phase tasks would re-litigate boundaries and order, and migrations would be added in inconsistent ways.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 0 Deliverables: ... crate/module boundary plan; storage migration policy; compatibility policy for existing MCP tools.\"\n\n> \"Use SQLite as the durable local store unless proven insufficient. Split logical tables cleanly.\"\n\n> \"Event log compaction: ... compaction must be a daemon-managed background operation, not a user-initiated manual step.\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs:\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-fork-or-extend-decision.md` from T01 (decides repo target).\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-architecture.md` and `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md` from T02 (defines substrate boundaries the crates encapsulate).\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/Cargo.toml` (workspace)\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/Cargo.toml` and `src/lib.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/Cargo.toml`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` (current schema introduction and migration patterns)\n- Standards files to honor: `coding.md` (file ≤800 lines, single source of truth, no broken windows); `AGENTS.md` (backward compatibility).\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read T01 and T02 outputs and re-read the spec sections §Storage Design and §Fork Strategy.\n2. For each of the seven new substrates (identity, events, memory, retrieval, working-memory, consolidation, verification), pick one of two layouts: a separate crate under `daemon/crates/` named `lattice-<substrate>`, or a module inside `lattice-core`. Record the choice and the rationale (compile-time boundary, dependency cycles avoided, public-API stability).\n3. In `2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md`, write one section per crate or module with: name, purpose, public API surface, allowed dependencies (other lattice crates only), and the spec sections it implements.\n4. Add a `## Dependency graph` section showing the directed acyclic dependency relationship between the new crates and `lattice-core` / `lattice-daemon`. No cycles permitted.\n5. Add a `## Test boundary` section stating that each crate carries its own `tests.rs` modules under `src/` per Lattice convention (see `context.md` §2 \"Tests\").\n6. In `2026-05-16-storage-migration-policy.md`, write a `## Migration order` section that enumerates every schema introduction in chronological phase order: Phase 1 identity tables, Phase 2 `events` + `event_payloads`, Phase 3 `memory_links` + `memory_evidence` + `memory_accesses` + `memory_scores`, Phase 5 `working_memory_checkpoints` + `context_handles`, Phase 6 `consolidation_jobs`, Phase 7 `verification_jobs`.\n7. Add a `## Rollback` section that names, for every migration, the inverse operation, the data-loss class (none, archived, destructive), and the operator command to invoke rollback. Migrations that cannot be safely rolled back must be flagged explicitly.\n8. Add a `## Compaction snapshot policy` subsection covering the daemon-managed background compaction described in spec §Storage Design (versioned format, independently readable, no manual trigger).\n9. Cross-reference the architecture overview from T02 and the fork-or-extend decision from T01 at the top of both docs.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md` — binding crate/module layout for every Phase 1+ backend task; names `lattice-identity`, `lattice-events`, `lattice-memory`, `lattice-retrieval`, `lattice-working-memory`, `lattice-consolidation`, `lattice-verification` or documents the in-`lattice-core` alternative per substrate.\n- `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-storage-migration-policy.md` — migration order across phases plus rollback per migration plus compaction snapshot policy.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md` — confirms the crate boundary plan exists.\n- `test -f docs/architecture/2026-05-16-storage-migration-policy.md` — confirms the migration policy exists.\n- `grep -q 'lattice-identity' docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md` — confirms the identity substrate is named explicitly.\n- `grep -q 'lattice-events' docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md` — confirms the events substrate is named explicitly.\n- `grep -q 'lattice-memory' docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md` — confirms the memory substrate is named explicitly.\n- `grep -q '## Migration order' docs/architecture/2026-05-16-storage-migration-policy.md` — confirms migration order is its own section, not buried in prose.\n- `grep -q '## Rollback' docs/architecture/2026-05-16-storage-migration-policy.md` — confirms rollback is explicitly documented per migration.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file (verify with `wc -l docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md docs/architecture/2026-05-16-storage-migration-policy.md`).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10 — not applicable (docs task).\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code.\n- No unjustified `// allow(...)` or suppressions.\n- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming — applies to any crate or module names introduced.\n- For schema changes: schema parity rules are stated as policy here; actual schema changes happen in later phases.\n- Doc citation: cite the exact `## Storage Design` and `## Fork Strategy` headings from the spec, and reference `docs/architecture/2026-04-11-storage-and-search-backends.md` headings rather than duplicating.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: no item from spec §Phase 0 punted to a later phase.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed and the architecture doc was updated in the same task.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":615,"cache_read_input_tokens":49571,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":615,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016juPk15H1M5x3FpzubRVsP","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"60aa9842-388e-4ea6-aa67-465c151b1ae1","request_id":"req_011Cb7Mcwaxi2NndD8b7oC78","subagent_type":"genera