{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MwMpQjCfQEHZyv4nKvEQiq","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# T11 — Phase 2 — Event model types (all 20 event kinds + envelope)\n2\t\n3\t**Phase:** 2\n4\t**Type:** backend\n5\t**Model class:** balanced\n6\t**Depends on:** R10\n7\t**Spec anchor:** [§Event Log](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#3-event-log)\n8\t**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules.\n9\t\n10\t## Goal\n11\t\n12\tThis task introduces the Rust type system for the append-only event log substrate. It defines the `EventKind` enum covering all 20 spec event types, the shared `EventEnvelope` struct carrying workspace id, branch, session id, task id, actor, timestamp, stable references, payload hash, compact summary, and optional full payload location, plus the typed payload structs for each kind. Without these types, Phase 2 storage, writer, reader, and capture work has nothing to serialize. Every later phase (memory consolidation, verification, retrieval, metrics) depends on these typed records, so getting the model right now prevents downstream churn.\n13\t\n14\t## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n15\t\n16\t> \"Required event types: `AssistantTaskStarted`, `ToolCalled`, `ToolResult`, `ContextBundleReturned`, `MemoryRetrieved`, `MemoryExpanded`, `PlanCreated`, `FileRead`, `PatchApplied`, `TestRunStarted`, `TestRunCompleted`, `DiagnosticObserved`, `UserCorrection`, `UserPreferenceObserved`, `WorkflowSucceeded`, `WorkflowFailed`, `MemoryCreated`, `MemoryUpdated`, `MemoryInvalidated`, `MemoryConsolidated`.\"\n17\t\n18\t> \"Events should carry: workspace id, branch, session id, task id, actor, timestamp, stable references to files, symbols, docs, events, and memories, payload hash, compact payload summary, optional full payload location.\"\n19\t\n20\t> \"The full event stream should not be injected into prompts. It exists for retrieval, audit, replay, metrics, and consolidation.\"\n21\t\n22\t## Inputs\n23\t\n24\t- Dependency outputs: R10 (Phase 1 unified-identity review) — events MUST reference files, symbols, docs, and prior events through the stable identity types defined in Phase 1, not through transient names.\n25\t- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n26\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/store.rs` — current serde patterns for memory records.\n27\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` — current serde + chrono conventions for SQLite timestamps.\n28\t  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/` — current `ContextBundle`, `WorkflowOutcome` shapes that some event payloads will summarize.\n29\t  - Phase 1 identity crate (`lattice-identity` or `identity` module per T03 decision) — the source of `FileId`, `SymbolId`, `DocSectionId`, `EventId`, `MemoryId`, `ContextHandleId`.\n30\t- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Hard limits, §Naming, §Schema / model parity, §No broken windows; Lattice rules on Markdown heading references for spec-bound behavior.\n31\t\n32\t## Steps\n33\t\n34\t1. Read spec §Event Log in full and copy the 20 event-kind list verbatim into a doc comment on `EventKind` so the enum is self-documenting.\n35\t2. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/mod.rs` exporting the module surface (`kinds`, `envelope`) and a top-level doc comment that points to `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md` §Event Log.\n36\t3. In `events/kinds.rs`, define `pub enum EventKind` with the 20 variants in spec order: `AssistantTaskStarted`, `ToolCalled`, `ToolResult`, `ContextBundleReturned`, `MemoryRetrieved`, `MemoryExpanded`, `PlanCreated`, `FileRead`, `PatchApplied`, `TestRunStarted`, `TestRunCompleted`, `DiagnosticObserved`, `UserCorrection`, `UserPreferenceObserved`, `WorkflowSucceeded`, `WorkflowFailed`, `MemoryCreated`, `MemoryUpdated`, `MemoryInvalidated`, `MemoryConsolidated`. Derive `Serialize`, `Deserialize`, `Clone`, `Copy`, `Debug`, `PartialEq`, `Eq`, `Hash`. Implement `EventKind::as_str()` returning the canonical snake_case wire name used in storage.\n37\t4. In `events/kinds.rs`, define one typed payload struct per variant (e.g. `AssistantTaskStartedPayload`, `ToolCalledPayload`, `ToolResultPayload`, `ContextBundleReturnedPayload`, `MemoryRetrievedPayload` …). Each payload references prior identity types (`FileId`, `SymbolId`, `DocSectionId`, `EventId`, `MemoryId`, `ContextHandleId`) — never raw paths or names.\n38\t5. Define `pub enum EventPayload` wrapping all 20 payload structs so the envelope can carry any kind without dynamic dispatch.\n39\t6. In `events/envelope.rs`, define `pub struct EventEnvelope` with the spec-required fields: `event_id: EventId`, `workspace_id: WorkspaceId`, `branch: BranchRef`, `session_id: SessionId`, `task_id: Option<TaskId>`, `actor: Actor`, `timestamp: chrono::DateTime<Utc>`, `kind: EventKind`, `references: Vec<StableRef>`, `payload_hash: PayloadHash`, `summary: CompactSummary`, `payload_location: PayloadLocation`. Derive `Serialize`, `Deserialize`, `Clone`, `Debug`.\n40\t7. Define `StableRef` as an enum over `FileRef(FileId)`, `SymbolRef(SymbolId)`, `DocSectionRef(DocSectionId)`, `EventRef(EventId)`, `MemoryRef(MemoryId)`, `ContextHandleRef(ContextHandleId)` so every reference is identity-typed.\n41\t8. Define `PayloadLocation` as `Inline { bytes_len: u32 }` or `Spilled { row_id: i64 }` so T12 can decide spillover policy without changing the envelope.\n42\t9. Define `Actor` as `enum { Assistant { model: String }, User, Tool { name: String }, Daemon }`. Define `CompactSummary` as a newtype around `String` with a hard ceiling (e.g. 512 bytes) enforced at construction.\n43\t10. In `events/tests.rs`, write tests that round-trip each `EventKind` through serde, assert canonical wire names, and verify every payload struct serializes deterministically (sorted JSON keys) so payload hashing in T13 is stable.\n44\t\n45\t## Files expected\n46\t\n47\t- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/mod.rs` — module root; re-exports `EventEnvelope`, `EventKind`, `EventPayload`, `StableRef`, `Actor`, `CompactSummary`, `PayloadHash`, `PayloadLocation`; doc comment cites spec §Event Log.\n48\t- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/kinds.rs` — `EventKind` enum with all 20 variants, per-kind typed payload structs, `EventPayload` wrapper, serde derives.\n49\t- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/envelope.rs` — `EventEnvelope` plus supporting types (`Actor`, `StableRef`, `PayloadLocation`, `CompactSummary`, `PayloadHash`).\n50\t- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/tests.rs` — unit tests for serde round-trip per kind, canonical wire names, summary ceiling, deterministic key ordering.\n51\t\n52\t## Verification\n53\t\n54\t- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/mod.rs` — file exists at the path the harness expects.\n55\t- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/kinds.rs` — file exists at the path the harness expects.\n56\t- `cd daemon && cargo build -p lattice-core` — the new module compiles cleanly with the rest of the crate.\n57\t- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib events::tests` — every event-model unit test passes.\n58\t\n59\t## Coding-standard checks\n60\t\n61\t- File length ≤800 lines per file (split `kinds.rs` if it grows beyond, e.g. one sub-module per kind family).\n62\t- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10.\n63\t- Schema parity: every variant has a typed payload struct with serde derives; every non-private field has an explicit type and doc comment.\n64\t- No silent error handling — `Result` returned from `CompactSummary::new` is checked at every call site or annotated.\n65\t- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, commented-out code.\n66\t- For SQLite: not applicable here (T12 owns SQL); ensure no schema bytes leak into this task.\n67\t- Use `tracing` only where construction failure must be observable; types themselves are passive.\n68\t\n69\t## Definition of done\n70\t\n71\t- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content.\n72\t- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n73\t- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n74\t- [ ] No deferred work: all 20 event kinds defined with payloads in this task; storage, writer, reader, capture, snapshot, and tests are sibling Phase 2 tasks (T12–T17), not deferrals.\n75\t- [ ] Architecture doc updated in the same task if behavior is publicly observable — covered by T16's `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-event-log-compaction.md` for compaction; this task adds the doc-comment heading reference to the spec §Event Log on `mod.rs` and `EventKind`.\n76\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XjrTa6YAS1dmMW989ZPauZ","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"14acb78e-77fe-427c-b89e-b0a0d6d79714","timestamp":"2026-05-17T02:33:36.324Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 10+11+Final task briefs"}
