{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_012dWuByvFthfkPZ5xS5UtsP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013h33HXF8JPQmJW1Fsfdbgi","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T27.md","content":"# T27 — Phase 4 — Task intent classifier\n\n**Phase:** 4\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** R26\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 4: Retrieval V1](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-4-retrieval-v1), [§Retrieval Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#7-retrieval-engine), [§Ranking Complexity](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#ranking-complexity)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task delivers the first stage of the Phase 4 retrieval pipeline: a deterministic, feature-based classifier that reads a user task statement and assigns it one or more intent labels (debug, refactor, explain, add-feature, test, docs, migration, performance, review, etc.). The classifier is the input to every later retrieval stage — anchor extraction biases toward intent-relevant token shapes, candidate retrieval weights source mix by intent, and the scorer applies a `task-type compatibility` signal that requires this label to exist. Per spec §Ranking Complexity, the classifier must stay feature-based and inspectable before any learned policy is layered on top, so that ranking remains explainable for the lifetime of Phase 4.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Pipeline: 1. Parse user task and classify intent.\" (spec §7. Retrieval Engine)\n\n> \"Ranking signals: task-type compatibility, graph proximity to anchors, exact identifier match, semantic similarity, verification status, freshness, scope, evidence strength, contradiction/supersession state, past usefulness, recent successful reuse, user preference compatibility, token cost.\" (spec §7. Retrieval Engine)\n\n> \"Phase 4: Retrieval V1 — Deliverables: task intent classifier; anchor extractor and resolver; hybrid candidate retrieval from graph, docs, memories, and events; scoring model with graph proximity, semantic similarity, freshness, scope, verification, and usefulness; compact response shaper; diagnostic response mode with ranking reasons; benchmark suite for realistic assistant tasks.\" (spec §Phase 4: Retrieval V1)\n\n> \"Risk: ranking becomes hard to reason about. Control: keep ranker feature-based and inspectable before any learned policy. Expose diagnostic scores.\" (spec §Ranking Complexity)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: R26 (Phase 3 memory-graph review verdict) — ensures retrieval can rely on typed memory streams, link tables, and verification status fields existing as designed.\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/` — current workflow tools that today perform implicit intent inference inline; T27 lifts that into a dedicated module.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/query/engine.rs` — current heuristic intent detection in the query path; behaviour to preserve and extend.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/lib.rs` — module registry that must expose the new `retrieval_v1` namespace.\n- Standards files to honor: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (file ≤800 lines, function ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, single source of truth — no parallel intent inference helpers); `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md` (Markdown heading references in code comments where behaviour is doc-anchored).\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md` §Retrieval Engine pipeline step 1, §Phase 4 deliverables, and §Ranking Complexity in full so the inspectability constraint is internalized verbatim.\n2. Enumerate the intent labels the classifier must emit, drawn from spec language and current workflow tool coverage: `debug`, `refactor`, `explain`, `add_feature`, `modify_feature`, `add_test`, `update_docs`, `migration`, `performance`, `review`, `unknown`. Document each label with a short doc comment naming the workflow tools that depend on it.\n3. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/mod.rs` (new directory) that re-exports the classifier API and registers the module with `lib.rs`.\n4. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/intent.rs`: a pure-function classifier `classify_intent(task_text: &str) -> IntentClassification` that returns a primary label, optional secondary labels, per-feature scores, and the literal features that fired (lemma matches, imperative-verb hits, error-keyword hits, file/symbol token shapes, question-form hits). Features must be a finite, documented list — no learned weights, no opaque model — so the result is fully inspectable per §Ranking Complexity.\n5. Surface a `diagnostics()` view on `IntentClassification` that returns `(label, contributing_features, score)` tuples for use by the diagnostic mode of T30 and the working-memory inspector of T36; this is the contract that lets the ranker explain why a label was chosen.\n6. Migrate the existing heuristic intent inference in `query/engine.rs` to call the new classifier instead of duplicating logic; remove the old inline heuristic in the same commit per \"single source of truth\" in `coding.md`.\n7. Add `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/intent_tests.rs` covering: every label appears for at least one canonical task statement; ambiguous tasks return multiple labels with documented tie-break; empty/whitespace input returns `unknown` without panic; long input is truncated at a documented boundary without losing the leading verb; diagnostics output round-trips through serde.\n8. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release` and the verification test command; fix any clippy warnings in the new module before stopping.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/intent.rs` — feature-based intent classifier with documented label set and diagnostics view.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/intent_tests.rs` — in-tree tests for label coverage, ambiguity handling, edge inputs, diagnostics serialization.\n\n(Implicitly required to make the module compile: `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/mod.rs` with module declarations, registered from `lib.rs`.)\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/intent.rs` — confirms the classifier file exists at the expected path.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib retrieval_v1::intent_tests` — runs the in-tree tests and asserts every documented label and edge case is covered.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file (`wc -l daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/intent.rs daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/intent_tests.rs`).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. The classifier must use early returns and table-driven feature evaluation; no nested match pyramids.\n- Schema parity: not applicable (no SQL in this task).\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Single source of truth: the legacy heuristic intent inference in `query/engine.rs` is removed in this commit; no parallel classifier remains.\n- No broken windows: dead imports removed, every public name expresses intent.\n- Doc citation: where the classifier comments explain a behaviour mandated by `## Ranking Complexity` in the plan doc, the comment cites that exact heading per `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md` \"Markdown Heading References\".\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: no item from spec §Phase 4 deliverable \"task intent classifier\" punted to a later phase.\n- [ ] Legacy inline intent heuristic in `query/engine.rs` migrated to the new module in the same commit (single source of truth).\n- [ ] Diagnostics view is exported and exercised by a test, ready to be consumed by T30 (scoring) and T36 (working-memory inspector).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":187,"cache_read_input_tokens":45959,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":187,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019RjXwCuf57BAKn88mWkE24","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"7b3a9aaf-37d5-4241-8bbe-3572b8a62729","request_id":"req_011Cb7MkGmZvqNoB2E9TvBXh","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 4+5 task briefs"}
