{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Uas3euKq46W6C9zwd3iTNw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AizBE4euwFSDBxZ5E42DbU","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T12.md","content":"# T12 — Phase 2 — Append-only SQLite event tables + payload spillover + indexes\n\n**Phase:** 2\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** T11\n**Spec anchor:** [§Storage Design](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#storage-design)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules.\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task creates the durable, append-only SQLite tables that back the event log: `events` for envelope rows and `event_payloads` for spilled payloads larger than the inline ceiling. It defines the migration runner that creates the schema on a fresh `.lattice/events.db`, and the indexes that make task, session, workspace, and branch scoped reads bounded. The spec requires the event log to be append-only and replayable; this task is where that invariant is encoded in the schema (no UPDATE/DELETE triggers, monotonic event_id PK). Without these tables, T13 (writer) and T14 (reader) have nowhere to land.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Use SQLite as the durable local store unless proven insufficient. Split logical tables cleanly. Core tables: … `events`, `event_payloads`, …\"\n\n> \"The event log should be append-only. Derived graph and memory state can be rebuilt from source files and events.\"\n\n> \"Indexes: … event task/session indexes …\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: T11 — `EventEnvelope`, `EventKind`, `EventPayload`, `PayloadLocation` types are the row shapes the schema must accommodate.\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` — current SQLite connection setup, WAL mode configuration, migration patterns. Reuse the existing `Migration` trait if one exists; otherwise mirror the structure of `graph.db` and `memories.db` setup.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/store.rs` — reference for `rusqlite::params!` usage and prepared-statement patterns.\n  - Phase 0 storage migration policy (`docs/architecture/2026-05-16-storage-migration-policy.md` from T03).\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Schema / model parity, §No broken windows (no string-formatted SQL); Lattice rule that raw SQL must be wrapped via `rusqlite::params!` or equivalent parameter binding.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. In `events/schema.sql`, define the schema as a single migration file the runner can execute idempotently. Tables:\n   - `events` columns: `event_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT`, `event_uuid TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE`, `workspace_id TEXT NOT NULL`, `branch TEXT NOT NULL`, `session_id TEXT NOT NULL`, `task_id TEXT NULL`, `actor_kind TEXT NOT NULL`, `actor_detail TEXT NULL`, `kind TEXT NOT NULL`, `ts_unix_micros INTEGER NOT NULL`, `payload_hash BLOB NOT NULL`, `summary TEXT NOT NULL`, `payload_inline BLOB NULL`, `payload_spill_id INTEGER NULL`, `references_json TEXT NOT NULL`, `schema_version INTEGER NOT NULL`. Foreign key: `payload_spill_id REFERENCES event_payloads(row_id)`.\n   - `event_payloads` columns: `row_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT`, `payload_hash BLOB NOT NULL UNIQUE`, `bytes BLOB NOT NULL`, `bytes_len INTEGER NOT NULL`, `created_ts_unix_micros INTEGER NOT NULL`. Content-addressed by hash so duplicate payloads dedupe naturally.\n   - `event_schema_version` table for the migration runner (`version INTEGER PRIMARY KEY`, `applied_ts_unix_micros INTEGER NOT NULL`).\n2. Add a deny-write trigger on `events` for UPDATE and DELETE so the table is append-only at the engine level, not only by convention: `CREATE TRIGGER events_no_update BEFORE UPDATE ON events BEGIN SELECT RAISE(ABORT, 'events table is append-only'); END;` (same for DELETE).\n3. Add indexes:\n   - `idx_events_task` on `(task_id, ts_unix_micros)` for task-scoped reads.\n   - `idx_events_session` on `(session_id, ts_unix_micros)`.\n   - `idx_events_workspace_branch` on `(workspace_id, branch, ts_unix_micros)`.\n   - `idx_events_kind_ts` on `(kind, ts_unix_micros)` for kind-filtered scans.\n   - `idx_event_payloads_hash` is the implicit UNIQUE on `payload_hash`.\n4. In `events/migrations.rs`, define `pub fn run_migrations(conn: &mut rusqlite::Connection) -> Result<(), EventStoreError>` that creates the `event_schema_version` table, reads the current version, and applies `schema.sql` if version is below the target. Embed `schema.sql` via `include_str!`.\n5. In `events/store.rs`, define `pub struct EventStore { conn: Mutex<rusqlite::Connection>, ... }` with `EventStore::open(path: &Path) -> Result<Self, EventStoreError>`. Configure WAL mode and `synchronous = NORMAL` consistent with the Phase 0 storage policy; document any deviation.\n6. In `events/store.rs`, define low-level row APIs that T13 writer and T14 reader will sit on top of: `insert_envelope_row(...)`, `insert_or_get_payload(...)`, `query_events_by_task(...)`, `query_events_by_session(...)`, `query_events_by_workspace_branch(...)`. Every SQL string uses `rusqlite::params!`; no `format!` of SQL.\n7. Define `EventStoreError` as a typed error enum (`Io`, `Sqlite`, `MigrationFailed`, `PayloadTooLarge`, `EnvelopeInvalid`) — never `anyhow::Error` at module boundaries.\n8. In `events/store_tests.rs`, write tests against an in-memory or temp-file DB: schema applies on fresh DB; migration is idempotent on re-open; UPDATE/DELETE triggers reject writes with the expected error; payload spillover row-IDs round-trip; content-addressed dedupe collapses identical payloads to one row; indexes exist (`PRAGMA index_list`).\n9. Confirm the table layout matches the migration policy doc from T03; if T03 prescribed different column names, update this task's schema to match before merge — never diverge.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/store.rs` — `EventStore` struct, connection setup, low-level row APIs, error type.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/schema.sql` — declarative DDL for `events`, `event_payloads`, append-only triggers, indexes.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/migrations.rs` — versioned migration runner with `include_str!` of `schema.sql`.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/store_tests.rs` — migration idempotence, append-only trigger enforcement, spillover round-trip, dedupe, index presence.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/store.rs` — schema/storage file exists at expected path.\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/schema.sql` — DDL artifact exists for review and golden-schema diffing.\n- `cd daemon && cargo build -p lattice-core` — store + schema compile cleanly inside the crate.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib events::store_tests` — every storage test passes against a temp DB.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10.\n- Schema parity: every column in `schema.sql` maps to a field on the T11 envelope/payload types; nullability matches `Option<T>`/`T` exactly.\n- No silent error handling — every `rusqlite::Result` propagated as `EventStoreError`.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, commented-out code.\n- For SQLite: every statement uses `rusqlite::params!`; no `format!`/`+`/`{}` interpolation of SQL strings; raw SQL lives in `schema.sql` not Rust source.\n- Use `tracing::debug!` / `warn!` for migration steps, schema mismatches, and trigger rejections so operators can diagnose without reproduction.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content.\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: append-only triggers, indexes, spillover table, and migration runner all in this task; the writer (T13), reader (T14), and snapshot (T16) are sibling tasks.\n- [ ] Architecture doc updated in the same task if behavior is publicly observable — the storage migration policy doc from T03 is the authoritative reference; if this task discovered a schema fact not covered there, update T03's doc in the same change rather than recording it only in code.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2746,"cache_read_input_tokens":55995,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2746,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01KTEqX34f6x4nqNqXUnhApL","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"d61c6c30-0d57-48f2-9329-9800151d5534","request_id":"req_011Cb7MhDToeu8q12KdN2sQ5","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 2+3+Gate task briefs"}
