{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012rYY2es9JTL5G4URr2Ybfg","type":"tool_result","content":"531\t## 7. Modals & Dialogs\n532\t\n533\t### 7.1 Standard Modal — use `ResponsiveModal`\n534\t\n535\t**Every modal in every Cadres product is built with the `ResponsiveModal` wrapper** (`components/common/ResponsiveModal.tsx`). Raw DaisyUI `<dialog className=\"modal modal-open\">` usage is forbidden — the wrapper owns responsive sizing (§13.6), focus management (§3.3), Esc handling, backdrop click-to-close, and ARIA role wiring, and centralizing those concerns is the only way they stay correct as the codebase grows.\n536\t\n537\t```tsx\n538\timport ResponsiveModal from 'components/common/ResponsiveModal';\n539\t\n540\t{showEditor && (\n541\t  <ResponsiveModal onClose={() => setShowEditor(false)} maxWidth=\"lg\">\n542\t    <h3 className=\"font-bold text-lg\">Edit user</h3>\n543\t    <div className=\"py-4\">{/* body */}</div>\n544\t    <div className=\"modal-action\">\n545\t      <button className=\"btn\" onClick={() => setShowEditor(false)}>Cancel</button>\n546\t      <button className=\"btn btn-primary\" onClick={onSubmit} disabled={saving}>\n547\t        {saving ? <span className=\"loading loading-spinner loading-sm\" /> : 'Save'}\n548\t      </button>\n549\t    </div>\n550\t  </ResponsiveModal>\n551\t)}\n552\t```\n553\t\n554\t**API:**\n555\t\n556\t| Prop | Required | Notes |\n557\t|---|---|---|\n558\t| `onClose` | yes | Called on backdrop click, Esc, and the wrapper's internal close paths. |\n559\t| `maxWidth` | no | `sm` / `md` (default) / `lg` / `xl` / `2xl` / `3xl` / `4xl` — applied at `md:` and above only; below `md:` the modal occupies the full viewport per §13.6. |\n560\t| `labelledBy` | no | `aria-labelledby` hook for when the heading id needs to be explicit. |\n561\t| `className` | no | Extra classes on the `.modal-box` for rare one-off cases. |\n562\t\n563\t**Mount pattern:** wrap with `{state && <ResponsiveModal ...>}`. Don't render ResponsiveModal always-on and toggle classes — conditional mounting is what gives focus-return and body-reset-on-reopen for free.\n564\t\n565\t**Banned modal patterns:**\n566\t\n567\t- `<dialog ref={dialogRef} className=\"modal\">` + `ref.current.showModal()` / `.close()` (imperative native `<dialog>` API). It bypasses ResponsiveModal's focus trap, sizing, and Esc wiring, and it makes the \"is this modal open\" state invisible to React. If the `ResponsiveModal` API doesn't cover your use case, extend it — don't bypass it.\n568\t- `<div className=\"modal modal-open\">` — a `<div>` doesn't provide the native `<dialog>` affordances ResponsiveModal depends on.\n569\t- `<dialog className={\\`modal ${cond ? 'modal-open' : ''}\\`}>` — always-mounted dialog with class-toggled visibility. Use `{cond && <ResponsiveModal>}` instead.\n570\t- `window.confirm` / `window.prompt` / `window.alert` — native browser dialogs (§7.2). The standards gate enforces this.\n571\t\n572\t**Legacy patterns in existing code**, if any, are hot spots — when you're already touching a file with a raw `<dialog>` pattern, convert it to ResponsiveModal in the same change rather than adding to it.\n573\t\n574\t### 7.2 Confirmation Dialogs\n575\t\n576\tDestructive actions (delete, cancel, revoke) MUST show a confirmation dialog:\n577\t- Red/warning styling\n578\t- Clear description of what will be deleted/cancelled\n579\t- Type-to-confirm for high-impact actions (e.g., type resource name)\n580\t- Cancel + Confirm buttons (Confirm in red/warning color)\n581\t\n582\t---\n583\t\n584\t## 8. State Management\n585\t\n586\t### 8.1 API Error Handling\n587\t\n588\t**NEVER use `Promise.all()` for independent API calls.** One failure kills all results.\n589\t\n590\t```tsx\n591\t// WRONG — one fails, all fail\n592\tconst [groups, policies] = await Promise.all([\n593\t  api.getAssignmentGroups(),\n594\t  api.getEscalationPolicies()\n595\t]);\n596\t\n597\t// CORRECT — independent error handling\n598\tlet groups = [], policies = [];\n599\ttry { groups = await api.getAssignmentGroups(); } catch (e) { console.error(e); }\n600\ttry { policies = await api.getEscalationPolicies(); } catch (e) { console.error(e); }\n601\t```\n602\t\n603\t### 8.2 Loading States\n604\t\n605\t- Initial page load: skeleton loader or centered spinner\n606\t- Table reload (filter/page change): subtle overlay spinner, keep existing data visible\n607\t- Form submit: disable submit button, show inline spinner\n608\t- Never show a blank page during loading\n609\t\n610\t### 8.3 Empty States\n611\t\n612\t- Centered icon + message + optional CTA button\n613\t- Different messages for \"no data yet\" vs \"no results matching filter\"\n614\t- Example: \"No assignment groups configured. Create one to start routing incidents.\"\n615\t\n616\t### 8.4 Toast Notifications\n617\t\n618\tAll user-triggered mutations show feedback:\n619\t```tsx\n620\tconst { toast } = useToast();\n621\t\n622\ttry {\n623\t  await api.createAssignmentGroup(data);\n624\t  toast.success('Assignment group created');\n625\t  onClose();\n626\t  refresh();\n627\t} catch (err) {\n628\t  toast.error(parseApiError(err));\n629\t}\n630\t```\n631\t\n632\t### 8.4.1 Plan Limit Errors (HTTP 429)\n633\t\n634\tHTTP 429 responses from plan-based resource limits should be displayed as a clear toast message:\n635\t\n636\t```\n637\t\"You've reached the maximum [resource] for your plan. Upgrade to add more.\"\n638\t```\n639\t\n640\tWhere `[resource]` is \"hosts\", \"scripts\", \"workflows\", or \"storage\". If the response body includes `limit` and `current` fields, include them: `\"You've reached the maximum scripts for your plan (50/50). Upgrade to add more.\"`\n641\t\n642\tOptionally include an upgrade link/button that navigates to the subscription management page.\n643\t\n644\t### 8.5 Error Display on API Failure (MANDATORY)\n645\t\n646\tEvery API call that mutates data (POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE) MUST display an error to the user on failure. Silent failures are never acceptable.\n647\t\n648\t**Rules:**\n649\t1. Every mutation API call must have a `catch` block that shows a `toast.error()` with a meaningful message\n650\t2. Pydantic validation errors (`422` with `detail` array) must be parsed into human-readable field-level messages\n651\t3. Never show a blank screen, spinner-forever, or swallowed error on API failure\n652\t4. For form submissions: display field-level errors inline below the relevant fields when possible\n653\t5. For non-form mutations: show a toast with the error detail\n654\t\n655\t**Standard error parsing helper** (`src/utils/errors.ts`):\n656\t```typescript\n657\timport { parseApiError } from '../../utils/errors';\n658\t\n659\t// In catch blocks:\n660\tcatch (error: any) {\n661\t  toast.error(parseApiError(error));\n662\t}\n663\t```\n664\t\n665\t`parseApiError()` handles all three error shapes:\n666\t- Pydantic 422 arrays: `[{loc: [\"body\", \"field\"], msg: \"...\"}]` -> `\"field: msg, field2: msg2\"`\n667\t- FastAPI string detail: `{detail: \"message\"}` -> `\"message\"`\n668\t- Generic errors: `error.message` -> fallback string\n669\t\n670\t**Anti-patterns (NEVER do these):**\n671\t```tsx\n672\t// WRONG — swallows error, user sees nothing\n673\tcatch (e) { console.error(e); }\n674\t\n675\t// WRONG — shows \"[object Object]\" for Pydantic 422 errors\n676\ttoast.error(error.response?.data?.detail || 'Failed');\n677\t\n678\t// WRONG — no catch at all, unhandled promise rejection\n679\tawait api.createThing(data);\n680\t```\n681\t\n682\t### 8.6 Error Message Style (Nielsen #9)\n683\t\n684\tErrors are written to be acted on, not just acknowledged. Every user-facing error obeys the rules below.\n685\t\n686\t| Rule | Bad | Good |\n687\t|---|---|---|\n688\t| Plain language, no codes | `ERR_4021: validation_failed` | `Email is already in use. Try signing in or use a different address.` |\n689\t| State the problem AND suggest the fix | `Invalid input.` | `Password must be at least 12 characters. Add 4 more.` |\n690\t| Be specific | `Something went wrong.` | `Could not reach the directory service. Retry in a few seconds.` |\n691\t| Place at the source | Single banner at the top of a long form | Inline error directly under the offending field |\n692\t| Tone matches who's at fault | \"You broke this.\" | \"We can't load this right now — retry?\" for system errors; clear-but-not-shaming for user errors |\n693\t| Never blame the user | `Wrong format.` | `Use YYYY-MM-DD (e.g., 2026-04-14).` |\n694\t| Don't dead-end the user | `Failed.` | `Failed. <a>Reset to defaults</a> or <a>contact support</a>.` |\n695\t\n696\t### 8.7 Success & Confirmation Messages\n697\t\n698\tSuccessful mutations get a brief toast that confirms what happened, in the past tense:\n699\t\n700\t- \"User created.\" (not \"Creating user…\" — that was the in-flight state)\n701\t- \"Webhook deleted.\"\n702\t- \"3 users deactivated.\"\n703\t\n704\tFor high-stakes actions where the user might want to undo: include an Undo action in the toast (see 8.8) for ~5 seconds.\n705\t\n706\tFor low-stakes mutations where the screen visibly updates (table reload, badge change, switch flip), the screen update IS the confirmation — a toast becomes noise. Skip it.\n707\t\n708\t### 8.8 Undo & Optimistic UI\n709\t\n710\tUndo is the antidote to confirm dialogs. Confirm interrupts every action; undo only catches the rare mistake.\n711\t\n712\t**Use undo (no confirm) for:**\n713\t- Reversible actions (archive, mark-complete, mark-read, reorder, snooze).\n714\t- Low-stakes single-row deletes where the row can be restored.\n715\t- Toggle switches.\n716\t\n717\t**Use confirm (no undo) for:**\n718\t- Truly destructive, irreversible actions (delete tenant, delete user with audit history, revoke a service credential) — section 7.2 enforces the confirm-dialog pattern for these.\n719\t- Actions with side effects beyond the current screen (sending email, triggering a deploy, charging a card).\n720\t- Bulk destructive actions where the impact count is large.\n721\t\n722\t**Pattern:**\n723\t\n724\t```tsx\n725\t// Optimistic + undo\n726\tconst original = items;\n727\tsetItems(items.filter(i => i.id !== item.id));            // optimistic remove\n728\tconst result = await toast.actionable(\n729\t  `${item.name} archived.`,\n730\t  { action: 'Undo', timeoutMs: 5000 }"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XjrTa6YAS1dmMW989ZPauZ","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"e1d8a891-a763-45ba-85e2-7a6080ced2c5","timestamp":"2026-05-17T02:34:09.473Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 10+11+Final task briefs"}
