{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013ZXuTanJH7X6D7LHKK4aiQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016cwUC7KSJW4BjPVj93cGrq","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R05.md","content":"# R05 — Foundation review — Phase 0 decisions and baselines\n\n**Phase:** Review for Phase 0\n**Type:** review\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** T01, T02, T03, T04\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 0: Fork Foundation](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-0-fork-foundation)\n**Standards reviewed:** Cadres coding standard, definition-of-done checklist.\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis review certifies that Phase 0 has produced an evidence-backed fork/extend decision, a complete architecture overview, a binding crate boundary plan and migration policy, and a runnable baseline benchmark suite. It is the gate that all Phase 1+ tasks depend on; passing it means later phases can rely on a fixed substrate vocabulary and an objective regression baseline.\n\n## Inputs to read\n\n- Every artifact produced by T01, T02, T03, T04:\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-fork-or-extend-decision.md`\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-architecture.md`\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md`\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md`\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-storage-migration-policy.md`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/benches/baseline_workflows.rs`\n  - `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/baseline_metrics.json`\n  - `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/README.md`\n- Spec sections this phase claims to satisfy: `## Phase 0: Fork Foundation`, `## Design Thesis`, `## System Architecture`, `## Storage Design`, `## Fork Strategy`.\n- Shared standards: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (hard limits, no broken windows, schema parity policy for future phases) and `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md` (every applicable item must be satisfied or explicitly waived).\n\n## Review procedure\n\n1. Open `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-fork-or-extend-decision.md` and verify it evaluates all four spec gate conditions with explicit `met`/`unmet` verdicts citing files and lines; verify a branch or repo name is committed under the `## Branch or repo name` heading.\n2. Open `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-architecture.md` and verify it contains `## Workspace graph`, `## Event log`, and `## Memory graph` sections; spot-check that each enumerates the node/edge/event/memory families from spec §System Architecture rather than paraphrasing.\n3. Open `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md` and verify every existing MCP tool (cross-check against `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` registrations) has a classification of `stable`, `additive`, `redesigned-with-shim`, or `deprecated-with-deadline`. Verify the `## Backward compatibility` section states the binding rule.\n4. Open `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md` and verify all seven new substrates (identity, events, memory, retrieval, working-memory, consolidation, verification) are present by literal grep, each with a layout decision and rationale.\n5. Open `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-storage-migration-policy.md` and verify `## Migration order` enumerates Phase 1 through Phase 7 schema introductions in chronological order, and `## Rollback` lists an inverse operation per migration.\n6. Open `daemon/crates/lattice-core/benches/baseline_workflows.rs` and verify benches exist for `prepare_change`, `get_context_capsule`, `expand_context`, `impact_from_diff`, `diagnose_failure`, `search_symbols`, and `find_relevant_tests`. Run `cd daemon && cargo bench --bench baseline_workflows -- --warm-up-time 1 --measurement-time 3` and confirm `baseline_metrics.json` is regenerated.\n7. Run `wc -l` on every file produced by Phase 0 to confirm none exceeds 800 lines.\n8. Grep all Phase 0 artifacts for `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, and commented-out code blocks; flag any hit as a finding.\n9. Cross-check that doc citations use exact `## Heading` references (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` § Markdown Heading References) and not vague \"see the spec\" prose.\n\n## Required sections in the review output file\n\nThe reviewer writes to `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R05-foundation.md` with these mandatory headings (each must contain real findings, not \"n/a\"):\n\n- `## Spec alignment` — phase-by-phase coverage matrix for Phase 0 deliverables: fork decision, architecture docs, crate/module plan, storage migration policy, compatibility policy, baseline benchmarks. One row per deliverable, evidence column citing the artifact and heading.\n- `## Coding-standard alignment` — line-by-line audit vs. hard limits: file length (`wc -l` results per file), forbidden tokens grep, suppression audit, naming audit on the bench function names.\n- `## Findings` — issues found, severity (`blocker`, `major`, `minor`), suggested follow-up tasks. Follow-up tasks must be opened in this build (do not defer outside).\n- `## Verdict` — `PASS`, `PASS-WITH-FOLLOWUP-TASK-Txx`, or `BLOCK` (with named blockers).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R05-foundation.md` — confirms the review markdown exists where downstream tasks can read it.\n- `grep -q '## Spec alignment' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R05-foundation.md` — confirms spec alignment is a dedicated section, not prose.\n- `grep -q '## Coding-standard alignment' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R05-foundation.md` — confirms standards audit was performed under a dedicated heading.\n- `grep -q '## Findings' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R05-foundation.md` — confirms findings are explicit and not buried.\n- `grep -q '## Verdict' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R05-foundation.md` — confirms the review concludes with a binding verdict.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Review markdown file exists at the path verification commands check.\n- [ ] Every required section above is present with concrete content.\n- [ ] If verdict is BLOCK, the blocking issues are listed and a follow-up task is opened in this build (never deferred to a future session).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":615,"cache_read_input_tokens":49571,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":615,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016juPk15H1M5x3FpzubRVsP","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"0f1bc3de-7993-48de-bd17-e18a2fa6e8b8","request_id":"req_011Cb7Mcwaxi2NndD8b7oC78","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 0+1 task briefs"}
