{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01M8uBUCTUJMj3USgaU3iXWd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CF386hStJ13LMHcfm7LVJ2","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T39.md","content":"# T39 — Phase 6 — Consolidation job runtime + proposal model (no silent writes)\n\n**Phase:** 6\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** R38\n**Spec anchor:** [§Consolidation Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#6-consolidation-engine), [§Phase 6: Consolidation Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-6-consolidation-engine), [§Storage Design](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#storage-design)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task stands up the consolidation engine's runtime kernel and the proposal model on which every later Phase 6 job depends. It introduces the `consolidation_jobs` table from spec §Storage Design, the bounded job queue, and a strict invariant that no consolidation job — deterministic or LLM-driven — writes durable memory directly. Every job emits a `ConsolidationProposal` record that requires explicit `apply` or `reject` before any memory state changes. Without this kernel, the LLM-driven jobs in T42 would be free to silently mutate memory, violating spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties and the §Opaque Memory Mutation risk control.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"No consolidation job may silently rewrite high-scope memory without preserving provenance and prior state.\"\n\n> \"each LLM-driven job produces a proposal record, not a direct write; proposals require explicit apply or reject before altering durable memory\"\n\n> \"consolidation queue depth must be bounded; when the queue is full, new jobs are dropped with a log warning rather than stalling the daemon\"\n\n> \"Every background consolidation pass is recoverable, replayable, and observable.\" (§Non-Negotiable Product Properties)\n\n> Core tables include `consolidation_jobs` (§Storage Design).\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: R38 Phase 5 working-memory review — the consolidation runtime hangs off the same `.lattice/` storage layout and reuses the event-log and memory-graph identity types finalized through Phases 1–5.\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/` — current memory store API; proposals must wrap writes through the existing store rather than bypass it.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` — SQLite connection setup, WAL mode, migration conventions.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/` — `EventEnvelope` (`MemoryConsolidated`, consolidation failure events) emitted by job lifecycle hooks.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/` — `MemoryId`, `EventId`, `WorkspaceId` used inside proposal payloads.\n  - `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/context.md` §1 (proposal-only invariant, bounded queue) and §6 (verification discipline).\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Hard limits, §Error handling, §Schema / model parity, §No broken windows; Lattice rules on Markdown heading references (cite §Consolidation Engine and §Storage Design rather than re-explaining behavior in code comments).\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Consolidation Engine, §Phase 6, and §Storage Design in full; record the proposal-only invariant verbatim in the top-of-module doc comment on `consolidation/mod.rs`.\n2. Add `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/mod.rs` re-exporting `proposal`, `queue`, and the `ConsolidationJobRuntime` entry point. The module doc comment must cite the exact `## 6. Consolidation Engine` and `## Storage Design` headings.\n3. Author `consolidation/schema.sql` defining the `consolidation_jobs` table (columns: `job_id PK`, `workspace_id`, `kind`, `mode` ∈ {`synchronous_post_task`, `background`, `manual_review`, `replay`}, `status` ∈ {`queued`, `running`, `proposed`, `applied`, `rejected`, `failed`, `dropped`}, `enqueued_at`, `started_at`, `finished_at`, `proposal_id NULLABLE`, `error_kind NULLABLE`, indexes on `(workspace_id, status)` and `(kind, status)`) plus a `consolidation_proposals` table (columns: `proposal_id PK`, `job_id FK`, `target_memory_id NULLABLE`, `proposal_kind`, `prior_state JSON`, `proposed_state JSON`, `evidence JSON`, `decided_at NULLABLE`, `decision` ∈ {`pending`, `applied`, `rejected`}, `decided_by NULLABLE`).\n4. In `consolidation/proposal.rs`, define `pub struct ConsolidationProposal { proposal_id, job_id, target: ProposalTarget, prior_state, proposed_state, evidence }`, the `ProposalKind` enum (e.g. `CreateMemory`, `UpdateMemory`, `MarkStale`, `Supersede`, `Demote`, `Refresh`), and the `ProposalDecision` enum. Implement `apply()` and `reject()` methods that mutate `consolidation_proposals.decision`, emit a `MemoryConsolidated` event with prior + proposed state preserved, and only then call the memory store API to materialize the change. `apply` MUST be a no-op if `decision != pending`.\n5. In `consolidation/queue.rs`, implement `BoundedJobQueue` with a configurable `max_depth` (default from `LatticeConfig`, no hard-coded literals). When `enqueue` is called and the queue is full, mark the job as `dropped` in `consolidation_jobs`, emit a `tracing::warn!` log including `workspace_id`, `kind`, and current depth, and return an `EnqueueOutcome::Dropped { reason }` — never block. Expose `depth()`, `pop()`, and `drain_for_shutdown()` for observability.\n6. Implement `ConsolidationJobRuntime` with `submit(job_spec)`, `run_due()` (polled by the daemon's scheduler), `decide(proposal_id, decision)` and `replay_from(event_id)`. The runtime never writes memory; it only writes proposals and dispatches their decisions.\n7. Wire `mod consolidation;` into `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/lib.rs` (alphabetical order) and register `consolidation/schema.sql` in the storage migration runner so the tables are created on daemon start.\n8. In `consolidation/proposal_tests.rs`, write tests that: (a) a deterministic job emits a proposal but does not mutate memory, (b) `apply` materializes the change and writes a `MemoryConsolidated` event with prior + proposed state, (c) `reject` leaves memory unchanged and records the decision, (d) double-apply is a no-op, (e) the queue drops jobs once depth exceeds the bound and emits the warning log (capture via a tracing subscriber fixture), (f) the `consolidation_jobs` schema round-trips under the migration runner against a temp DB.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/mod.rs` — module root; re-exports `ConsolidationJobRuntime`, `ConsolidationProposal`, `ProposalKind`, `ProposalDecision`, `BoundedJobQueue`, `EnqueueOutcome`; doc comment cites spec §Consolidation Engine and §Storage Design.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/proposal.rs` — `ConsolidationProposal` struct, `ProposalKind`/`ProposalDecision` enums, `apply`/`reject` methods, prior-state preservation, event emission.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/queue.rs` — `BoundedJobQueue` with configurable depth, drop-with-warning behavior, observability hooks.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/schema.sql` — `consolidation_jobs` and `consolidation_proposals` tables with the exact columns and indexes the runtime requires.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/proposal_tests.rs` — unit tests for proposal lifecycle, no-silent-writes, bounded-queue drops, schema migration round-trip.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/mod.rs` — confirms the module root exists.\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/proposal.rs` — confirms the proposal module exists.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib consolidation::proposal_tests` — every proposal-runtime unit test passes.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file. Split `proposal.rs` or `queue.rs` if any approaches the ceiling (e.g. extract a `decision.rs` sub-module).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. `BoundedJobQueue::enqueue` and `ConsolidationProposal::apply` are the hot spots — keep them flat with early returns.\n- Single source of truth: proposals MUST route writes through the existing memory store API (`crates/lattice-core/src/memory/`) — do not introduce a parallel write path.\n- Error handling: queue-full and apply-on-non-pending are normal control flow (typed `EnqueueOutcome` / `ApplyOutcome`), not panics. No silent `.ok()` drops on storage results.\n- Naming: `ConsolidationProposal`, `ProposalDecision`, `BoundedJobQueue` — intent over mechanism; no generic `Manager`/`Helper` suffixes.\n- Schema parity: every column on `consolidation_jobs` and `consolidation_proposals` has a typed field on the Rust struct; nullable columns map to `Option<…>`.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Observability: every proposal lifecycle transition emits a `tracing` span carrying `workspace_id`, `job_id`, `proposal_id`, and outcome. Queue drops log at `warn` per spec.\n- Doc citation: top-of-module doc comments cite `## 6. Consolidation Engine` and `## Storage Design` headings; per-method comments reference these headings only where behavior is non-obvious (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` § Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: deterministic jobs (T41), LLM jobs (T42), provenance (T43), manual review (T44), replay (T45), and integration tests (T46) are sibling tasks — but the proposal-only invariant, bounded queue, and `consolidation_jobs` schema all ship in this task.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed and the architecture doc was updated in the same task.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3709,"cache_read_input_tokens":53202,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3709,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015qAoQeXM7HFtFDzBbPkUNq","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"9c71f470-98b9-4480-8f0d-0c8ccdebc756","request_id":"req_011Cb7MmqeXLr2UsR7g5bqCY","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 6+7+Gate task briefs"}
