{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Uas3euKq46W6C9zwd3iTNw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Eegq3pniG384m5gL1nwgzZ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T13.md","content":"# T13 — Phase 2 — Event writer API + payload hashing + workspace scoping\n\n**Phase:** 2\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T12\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 2: Event Log Substrate](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-2-event-log-substrate)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules.\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task implements the public writer that workflow tools, the MCP layer, and the consolidation engine use to append events. It computes the canonical payload hash (deterministic over sorted-key JSON of the typed payload), decides inline vs. spilled payload location based on a configurable size ceiling, enforces workspace scoping at the API boundary (the writer cannot accept envelopes whose workspace_id disagrees with the open store), and meets the spec's hot-path budget of P99 ≤5ms write latency on `prepare_change` and `get_context_capsule` paths. Without the writer, no event ever reaches the store.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"event writer API … event payload hashing and optional payload spillover …\"\n\n> \"event write adds no more than 5ms P99 to hot-path tool calls (`prepare_change`, `get_context_capsule`); large payloads spill to a side table rather than blocking the writer.\"\n\n> \"No silent broad workspace reads that bypass ignore rules or workspace boundaries.\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: T12 — the `EventStore` connection, append-only schema, spillover row API.\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/envelope.rs` (T11) — `EventEnvelope`, `PayloadHash`, `PayloadLocation`, `CompactSummary`.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/kinds.rs` (T11) — `EventPayload` wrapper.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` — existing connection pooling and `WorkspaceId` conventions.\n  - Identity crate / module from Phase 1 — `WorkspaceId`, `SessionId`, `TaskId`, `BranchRef`.\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Hard limits, §Error handling (no silent catches), §Observability (tracing on hot path); Lattice rule that hot-path tools record bounded telemetry.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. In `events/hashing.rs`, define `pub struct PayloadHash([u8; 32])` (BLAKE3 or SHA-256 — match whichever the rest of the crate uses; document the choice) and `pub fn hash_payload(payload: &EventPayload) -> PayloadHash`. The hash is computed over `serde_json::to_vec` of the payload with a deterministic key ordering (use `serde_json::ser::PrettyFormatter` is wrong here — use a canonical-JSON helper that sorts keys; if none exists, write one and unit-test it).\n2. In `events/writer.rs`, define `pub struct EventWriter { store: Arc<EventStore>, workspace_id: WorkspaceId, inline_ceiling_bytes: usize }` and `pub fn EventWriter::new(store: Arc<EventStore>, workspace_id: WorkspaceId, inline_ceiling_bytes: usize) -> Self`. Default `inline_ceiling_bytes` to 4096 (documented in module doc with rationale).\n3. Define the primary entry point: `pub fn EventWriter::append(&self, envelope: PartialEnvelope) -> Result<EventId, EventWriteError>`. `PartialEnvelope` contains the caller-supplied fields (kind, references, payload, summary, optional task_id, session_id, actor); the writer fills in `event_id`, `timestamp` (UTC monotonic via `chrono::Utc::now()` plus a per-session monotonic tiebreaker), `payload_hash`, and `payload_location`.\n4. Enforce workspace scoping: if `PartialEnvelope::workspace_id` is set and differs from `self.workspace_id`, return `EventWriteError::WorkspaceMismatch` — do not silently coerce.\n5. Decide payload location: serialize the payload, hash it, and if `bytes.len() <= inline_ceiling_bytes` set `PayloadLocation::Inline { bytes_len }` and insert payload bytes directly into the `events.payload_inline` column. Otherwise call `EventStore::insert_or_get_payload(hash, bytes)` and set `PayloadLocation::Spilled { row_id }`. Content-addressed dedupe is handled by T12's UNIQUE index on payload_hash.\n6. Use a prepared-statement cache on the writer so repeated appends do not re-prepare the INSERT; document that the cache is per-writer, not global.\n7. Instrument `append` with `tracing::trace_span!(\"event_writer.append\", kind = ?envelope.kind)` and emit a `tracing::debug!` on every spill so operators can see hot-path payload-size pressure.\n8. Add a synchronous-flush option for tests: `EventWriter::with_flush_policy(FlushPolicy::Sync | FlushPolicy::Batched { interval_ms })`. Default to `Sync` in tests, `Batched` in daemon use (configurable later in T15).\n9. Define `EventWriteError` as a typed enum: `WorkspaceMismatch`, `PayloadTooLarge { ceiling: usize, actual: usize }` (if a hard cap is exceeded), `Storage(EventStoreError)`, `Serde(serde_json::Error)`, `Identity(IdentityError)`.\n10. In `events/writer_tests.rs`, write tests covering: deterministic hash for equivalent payloads with key-order variation; identical payloads dedupe to one `event_payloads` row; inline vs. spill threshold honored exactly at the boundary; workspace mismatch returns `WorkspaceMismatch`; concurrent appends from two threads preserve monotonic `event_id`; sync flush returns only after the row is durable in WAL.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/writer.rs` — `EventWriter`, `PartialEnvelope`, `FlushPolicy`, `EventWriteError`.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/hashing.rs` — `PayloadHash` newtype, canonical-JSON serialization helper, `hash_payload` function.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/writer_tests.rs` — hash determinism, dedupe, spill threshold, workspace scoping, concurrent monotonicity, sync flush durability.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/writer.rs` — writer file exists at expected path.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib events::writer_tests` — every writer test passes; T17 covers the dedicated P99 budget test under `events::budget_tests`.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10.\n- Schema parity: writer never invents fields not in `events`/`event_payloads`; every envelope field has a matching DB column.\n- No silent error handling — every `Result` returned or annotated; no `.ok()` discards on the write path.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, commented-out code.\n- For SQLite: prepared statements only, `rusqlite::params!` everywhere; no SQL string interpolation.\n- Use `tracing::trace_span!` on `append`, `tracing::debug!` on spillover, `tracing::warn!` on workspace mismatch.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content.\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: hashing, spillover, workspace scoping, batched + sync flush policies, and concurrent-safety all in this task; the P99 budget test is a sibling task (T17) per the build plan.\n- [ ] Architecture doc updated in the same task if behavior is publicly observable — `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-event-log-compaction.md` (T16) is the authoritative event-log doc; if this task introduces a writer-visible behavior not covered there (e.g. batched flush semantics), update T16's doc in the same change.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2746,"cache_read_input_tokens":55995,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2746,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01KTEqX34f6x4nqNqXUnhApL","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"4c4dd2e0-99d5-425f-973d-333a35d99dca","request_id":"req_011Cb7MhDToeu8q12KdN2sQ5","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 2+3+Gate task briefs"}
