{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013ZXuTanJH7X6D7LHKK4aiQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RsNa6ebsnWVeUhpsNvGQen","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T06.md","content":"# T06 — Phase 1 — Identity type system (File, Symbol, Doc, Section, Event, Memory, Handle)\n\n**Phase:** 1\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** R05\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 1: Unified Identity Model](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-1-unified-identity-model)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task introduces the unified identity type system that every later substrate (event log, memory graph, working memory, retrieval, verification) depends on. Spec §Phase 1 states \"Identity must precede the event log. An event that references a file, symbol, or doc by unstable name cannot be reliably replayed or used for consolidation.\" The task delivers stable, encodable, decodable, hashable id types for each of the seven identity kinds plus the encoding/decoding rules that make them compact in MCP payloads. The existing `SymbolId { file, name, byte_offset }` is generalized into a common identity model.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 1 Deliverables: stable ids for files, symbols, docs, sections, events, memories, and context handles; identity resolver for paths, symbols, headings, tests, and event refs; explicit identity serialization in MCP payloads; compatibility support for legacy name-based references; tests for duplicate symbol names, renamed files, moved sections, and branch changes.\"\n\n> \"Definition of done: every workflow output can be expanded through a stable identity; ambiguous names return ambiguity diagnostics instead of arbitrary matches; identity resolution adds no more than 2ms P99 to hot-path tool calls.\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: R05 review (validates Phase 0 artifacts) and the layout decisions in `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md` (decides whether identity is a `lattice-identity` crate or a `lattice-core::identity` module).\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/graph/` (current node identifier types)\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/` (current `SymbolId` usage in `expand_context`)\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-04-11-stable-follow-up-handles.md` (existing handle conventions to honor and generalize)\n- Standards files to honor: `coding.md` hard limits (file ≤800 lines, function ≤50, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10), naming (intent over mechanism), single source of truth (replace ad-hoc id strings, do not fork them); `AGENTS.md` backward-compatibility (legacy `SymbolId` callers must keep compiling via a re-export or `From` impl).\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read the crate boundary plan from T03 to confirm whether identity lives in `daemon/crates/lattice-identity/` or `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/`. The files_expected list assumes the in-`lattice-core` module layout; if T03 chose a separate crate, mirror the file structure under that crate and update the workspace `Cargo.toml`.\n2. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/mod.rs` declaring the `kinds`, `encoding`, and `tests` submodules and re-exporting the public identity types.\n3. In `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/kinds.rs`, define one struct per identity kind with the exact fields required by the spec node/event/memory model:\n   - `FileId { workspace_id, repo_relative_path, content_hash }`\n   - `SymbolId { file: FileId, qualified_name, byte_offset, kind }` (generalizing the existing `SymbolId`)\n   - `DocId { workspace_id, repo_relative_path, content_hash }`\n   - `SectionId { doc: DocId, heading_path: Vec<String>, byte_offset }`\n   - `EventId { workspace_id, ulid }` (ULID for monotonic ordering)\n   - `MemoryId { workspace_id, ulid }`\n   - `ContextHandleId { workspace_id, session_id, ulid }`\n4. Each id type derives `Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, Hash, serde::Serialize, serde::Deserialize`. Implement `Display` to produce the compact MCP wire form.\n5. Define a common `IdentityKind` enum and an `Identity` enum that wraps the seven kinds so any subsystem can hold a heterogeneous identity reference.\n6. In `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/encoding.rs`, implement compact wire encoding rules: a stable string form (`file:<workspace>/<path>@<hash>`, `symbol:<file>#<qname>@<offset>`, `event:<workspace>/<ulid>`, etc.) and a decoder that round-trips. Reject malformed strings with a typed `IdentityDecodeError`.\n7. Provide `From<old_SymbolId> for SymbolId` and a re-export under the prior path so existing callers continue compiling.\n8. In `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/tests.rs`, write unit tests for: round-trip encoding for every kind; equality semantics; hash stability across process restarts (deterministic for same inputs); `IdentityDecodeError` cases (empty, missing prefix, malformed hash); `From<old_SymbolId>` migration.\n9. Add the module to `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/lib.rs` with `pub mod identity;` and document the substrate in a module-level doc comment that cites the spec heading.\n10. Run `cd daemon && cargo build -p lattice-core` and `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib identity::tests` to confirm green.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/mod.rs` — module entrypoint, re-exports, module docs citing spec §Phase 1.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/kinds.rs` — the seven id structs, `Identity` enum, `IdentityKind` enum.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/encoding.rs` — compact wire form encode/decode with `IdentityDecodeError`.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/tests.rs` — unit tests covering round-trip, equality, hashing, decode errors, and the legacy `SymbolId` migration shim.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/mod.rs` — confirms the module file exists.\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/kinds.rs` — confirms the kinds file exists.\n- `cd daemon && cargo build -p lattice-core` — confirms the crate compiles with the new module integrated.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib identity::tests` — confirms all identity unit tests pass.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines (verify with `wc -l daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/*.rs`).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10 — applies to every encode/decode helper.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code.\n- No unjustified `// allow(...)` or suppressions; if `#[allow(clippy::...)]` is required, justify on the same line.\n- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming (`FileId`, `SymbolId`, `IdentityDecodeError`).\n- For schema changes: not applicable (no SQL schema in this task); type-level schema parity is asserted via the `Identity` enum covering all seven kinds with no orphan fields.\n- Doc citation: cite the exact `## Phase 1: Unified Identity Model` heading from the spec in `mod.rs`; reference `docs/architecture/2026-04-11-stable-follow-up-handles.md` headings rather than duplicating prior handle behavior (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` § Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: no item from spec §Phase 1 punted to a later phase.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed and the architecture doc was updated in the same task.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":615,"cache_read_input_tokens":49571,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":615,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016juPk15H1M5x3FpzubRVsP","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"36cefa05-6830-4681-aa11-def156e8cd29","request_id":"req_011Cb7Mcwaxi2NndD8b7oC78","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 0+1 task briefs"}
