{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01M8uBUCTUJMj3USgaU3iXWd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Dy9HX5RWGcivLrDTBFxn1v","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T40.md","content":"# T40 — Phase 6 — Synchronous session consolidation (episode summaries)\n\n**Phase:** 6\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T39\n**Spec anchor:** [§Consolidation Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#6-consolidation-engine), [§Phase 6: Consolidation Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-6-consolidation-engine)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task adds the `synchronous post-task consolidation` mode from spec §Consolidation Engine. It runs only on small task traces immediately after a workflow concludes, producing an episode-summary proposal that links the task's event slice to a new or updated episode memory. It must NOT run on the hot path: spec §Phase 2 DoD pins event writes at ≤5ms P99 on `prepare_change` / `get_context_capsule`, and the consolidation engine §LLM-driven block forbids LLM inference on the synchronous post-task hot path. The session consolidator therefore uses the deterministic episode template only; LLM-driven episode generation lives in T42.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Consolidation modes: synchronous post-task consolidation for small task traces; background scheduled consolidation for larger histories; manual review mode for high-impact repo or organization memories; replay mode for rebuilding memory state from the event log.\"\n\n> \"Consolidation jobs: create episode summaries from completed tasks ...\"\n\n> \"LLM-driven jobs run only in background or manual review modes, never on the synchronous post-task hot path.\"\n\n> Phase 2 DoD: \"event write ≤5ms P99 on `prepare_change` / `get_context_capsule`\" — synchronous consolidation must respect the same hot-path discipline.\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: T39 — proposals, queue, and `consolidation_jobs` schema. Session consolidation enqueues a job and emits a proposal through the T39 runtime; it never writes memory directly.\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/` — the event reader to scan the small task slice (`AssistantTaskStarted` → `WorkflowSucceeded`/`WorkflowFailed`).\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/` — `EpisodeMemory` class shape and store API.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/` — `TaskId`, `SessionId`, `EventId`, `MemoryId`.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/` — `WorkflowOutcome` carries the trigger for post-task consolidation.\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Hard limits (≤5ms P99 budget is non-negotiable), §Error handling, §No broken windows; Lattice rules on doc-heading citation for hot-path behavior.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Consolidation Engine \"Consolidation modes\" and §Phase 6 DoD. Copy the synchronous-mode definition into the top-of-file doc comment on `session.rs`.\n2. In `consolidation/episode.rs`, define `EpisodeTemplate` — the deterministic shape of an episode summary: `task_id`, `session_id`, `outcome` (success/failure/abandoned), `event_window: Range<EventId>`, `salient_anchors: Vec<StableRef>` (files, symbols, docs touched), `tools_used: Vec<ToolName>`, `summary_text` (deterministic template like `\"Task {task_id}: {n} tools, {n} files, outcome={outcome}\"`). No LLM call. Implement `EpisodeTemplate::from_task_slice(events: &[EventEnvelope]) -> Result<EpisodeTemplate, EpisodeError>`.\n3. In `consolidation/session.rs`, implement `SessionConsolidator::on_task_complete(workspace_id, task_id, outcome)`. Steps: (a) fetch the task's event slice via the event reader using `task_id`-indexed lookup, (b) reject slices over the `synchronous_max_events` ceiling (configurable, default 200) by enqueuing the work into `background` mode instead, (c) build an `EpisodeTemplate`, (d) construct a `CreateMemory` or `UpdateMemory` proposal through the T39 runtime carrying the template's fields as `proposed_state`, (e) return immediately — apply/reject is the operator's call.\n4. Enforce the hot-path budget: wrap `on_task_complete` in a `tracing::info_span!` with elapsed-time recording and a `debug_assert!` for ≤5ms P99 in tests. The body must short-circuit if the slice exceeds the ceiling so the operation cannot grow unbounded.\n5. Wire `SessionConsolidator` into the workflow-outcome path (the daemon's existing `record_workflow_outcome` handler) so it fires once per completed task — but never blocks the response.\n6. Forbid LLM imports: this module must not depend on any `consolidation::llm::*` symbol. Add a crate-level compile assertion (a `#[cfg(test)]` test that uses `cargo metadata` or a string-grep guard test against this file's source) so future edits cannot silently introduce an LLM call here.\n7. In `consolidation/session_tests.rs`, write tests that: (a) a 3-event task slice produces a `CreateMemory` proposal with a deterministic summary, (b) a slice of 250 events is redirected to background mode rather than processed synchronously, (c) the runtime never mutates `memories` directly (assert via store telemetry), (d) elapsed time per call stays well under the 5ms budget on a benchmark fixture, (e) the LLM-forbid guard test fails if a `consolidation::llm` symbol is referenced from this module.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/session.rs` — `SessionConsolidator` synchronous entry point, ceiling check, proposal emission through T39, hot-path span, LLM-forbid guard.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/episode.rs` — `EpisodeTemplate` deterministic shape and `from_task_slice` constructor (no LLM).\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/session_tests.rs` — unit tests for synchronous behavior, ceiling redirect, no-mutation invariant, budget guard, LLM-forbid guard.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/session.rs` — confirms the synchronous module exists.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib consolidation::session_tests` — every session-consolidation unit test passes.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. `on_task_complete` is a flat sequence: guard, fetch, template, propose, return.\n- Single source of truth: episode shape lives in `episode.rs`; do not redefine the template in `session.rs`. Reuse the T39 proposal API; do not duplicate the `ConsolidationProposal` write path.\n- Error handling: `EpisodeError` is a typed enum (missing task slice, ceiling exceeded, store unavailable). No bare `unwrap`; no swallowed `Result`s. Ceiling exceedance is normal control flow (returns a `Redirected` outcome) not an error.\n- Naming: `SessionConsolidator`, `EpisodeTemplate`, `on_task_complete`, `synchronous_max_events`. No `Helper` / `Manager` / generic `data`.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Observability: `tracing::info_span!(\"session_consolidation\", workspace_id, task_id, slice_len)` around every call; elapsed time recorded on span exit.\n- Doc citation: file-top doc comments cite `## 6. Consolidation Engine` \"Consolidation modes\" and `## Phase 2: Event Log Substrate` DoD for the hot-path budget (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` § Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content.\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: LLM-driven episode generation is T42 by spec design; this task ships the full deterministic synchronous path and the LLM-forbid guard.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed and the architecture doc was updated in the same task.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3709,"cache_read_input_tokens":53202,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3709,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015qAoQeXM7HFtFDzBbPkUNq","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"f63339c6-78dc-430e-ad5f-857415ad1d3d","request_id":"req_011Cb7MmqeXLr2UsR7g5bqCY","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 6+7+Gate task briefs"}
