{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_013ZXuTanJH7X6D7LHKK4aiQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016wpFR2N3dUb7fdjiDggmL3","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T08.md","content":"# T08 — Phase 1 — Identity serialization in MCP payloads + legacy name compatibility shim\n\n**Phase:** 1\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T07\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 1: Unified Identity Model](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-1-unified-identity-model)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task wires the new `Identity` types into the MCP JSON-RPC surface so every workflow tool response carries stable identities the client can expand later, while preserving legacy name-based fields so existing clients continue to function. Spec §Phase 1 deliverables include \"explicit identity serialization in MCP payloads\" and \"compatibility support for legacy name-based references\". The compatibility shim is the binding mechanism by which T02's MCP compatibility policy is honored for Phase 1.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 1 Deliverables: ... explicit identity serialization in MCP payloads; compatibility support for legacy name-based references.\"\n\n> \"Definition of done: every workflow output can be expanded through a stable identity.\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs:\n  - T06 identity types (`daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/kinds.rs`, `encoding.rs`).\n  - T07 resolver and ambiguity modules (`resolver.rs`, `ambiguity.rs`).\n  - T02 compatibility policy (`docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md`) — binding for which tools must add additive identity fields vs. shimmed legacy fields.\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` (current MCP dispatch and payload shapes)\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/server.rs` (JSON-RPC server)\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/context_cache.rs` (handle cache that must store new `ContextHandleId`)\n- Standards files to honor: `coding.md` (no broken windows, single source of truth, schema parity), `AGENTS.md` (binding compatibility shim — every legacy field stays populated for one phase cycle).\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/serialization.rs` with serde helpers that emit the compact wire form defined in T06 `encoding.rs` and accept either compact form or structured object form on deserialize.\n2. Define a `pub struct IdentityPayload` containing both the compact `id` string and a structured `fields` object, plus an optional `legacy_name` field for backward compatibility. Serialization round-trips through both forms.\n3. Add `pub fn serialize_outcome<T: Into<Identity>>(outcome: ResolveOutcome<T>) -> IdentityPayloadOrAmbiguity` that converts the resolver outcome to the wire shape, preserving `Ambiguous` as a structured diagnostic instead of an arbitrary pick.\n4. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/identity_payload.rs` with the MCP wiring: a wrapper that decorates every workflow tool response (or its top-level pivot list) with `IdentityPayload` values and preserves the legacy name field listed in the T02 compatibility policy for each tool.\n5. Wire one representative tool (`get_context_capsule` or `prepare_change`) end-to-end through the new serialization wrapper as a proof of integration; full Phase 8 redesign of every tool is owned later, but Phase 1 must demonstrate the integration path works without regressing existing clients.\n6. Add tests under `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/serialization.rs` (`#[cfg(test)] mod tests`) covering: compact-form round-trip, structured-form acceptance, legacy-name preservation, ambiguity payload shape.\n7. Add tests under `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/identity_payload.rs` covering: a full tool response that includes both identity payloads and legacy fields, and a response where the resolver returned `Ambiguous` (the response must surface the ambiguity diagnostic rather than silently picking).\n8. Update the workflow tool that was wired in step 5 to emit identity payloads alongside its prior fields; document the change in `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md` under the per-tool classification.\n9. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release`, `cd daemon && cargo test --workspace -- identity::serialization`, and `cd daemon && cargo test --workspace -- rpc::identity_payload` to confirm green.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/serialization.rs` — `IdentityPayload`, serde helpers, `serialize_outcome`, inline tests.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/identity_payload.rs` — MCP wrapper that decorates workflow responses with identity payloads and preserves legacy name fields.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/serialization.rs` — confirms the serialization module exists.\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/identity_payload.rs` — confirms the RPC integration module exists.\n- `cd daemon && cargo build --release` — confirms the full workspace builds in release profile with the new modules wired in.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test --workspace -- identity::serialization` — confirms the serialization tests pass.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test --workspace -- rpc::identity_payload` — confirms the RPC integration tests pass.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines (verify with `wc -l daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/serialization.rs daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/identity_payload.rs`).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10 — applies to every serde helper and wrapper.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code.\n- No unjustified `// allow(...)` or suppressions.\n- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming (`IdentityPayload`, `serialize_outcome`, not `IdData` or `to_json`).\n- For schema changes: not applicable (no SQL schema added); JSON schema parity is asserted by tests covering both legacy and new fields.\n- Doc citation: cite the exact `## Phase 1: Unified Identity Model` heading from the spec and the per-tool classification heading from `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md` for every additive field introduced (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` § Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: no item from spec §Phase 1 punted to a later phase.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed and the architecture doc was updated in the same task.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":615,"cache_read_input_tokens":49571,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":615,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016juPk15H1M5x3FpzubRVsP","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"f2172cba-383d-413f-b510-a7ed9826dfd5","request_id":"req_011Cb7Mcwaxi2NndD8b7oC78","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 0+1 task briefs"}
