{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01CqnMhG1wN36C2yteTWR1rZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FtML53V5rSKF5hu5wzzt4s","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T58.md","content":"# T58 — Phase 8 — New memory tools: get_task_memory + save_memory + propose_memory_evolution(action=apply|reject)\n\n**Phase:** 8\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** R55\n**Spec anchor:** [§MCP Surface](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#9-mcp-surface)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task introduces three new memory-facing MCP tools required by spec §MCP Surface: `get_task_memory` (read working memory + relevant durable memory for the current task), `save_memory` (create a new durable memory record with evidence and validity conditions), and `propose_memory_evolution` (the unified successor to the spec's `propose_memory_evolution` + `apply_memory_evolution` pair, collapsed per spec §MCP Surface \"Tool surface discipline\" into a single tool with an `action` parameter accepting `propose | apply | reject`). The collapse is binding: spec §MCP Surface explicitly says \"audit whether `propose_memory_evolution` + `apply_memory_evolution` can collapse into a single tool with an `action` parameter, and whether `verify_memory` + `explain_memory` can be unified. The goal is the smallest surface that covers all assistant workflows.\" Without the unified `propose_memory_evolution`, the new memory surface ships ten tools instead of the audited eight, increasing client cognitive load for no gain.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"New or redesigned memory tools: `get_task_memory`, `save_memory`, `propose_memory_evolution`, `apply_memory_evolution`, `verify_memory`, `explain_memory`, `list_memory_conflicts`, `consolidate_session`, `get_memory_metrics`, `get_event_trace`.\"\n\n> \"Tool surface discipline: ten new memory tools is a meaningful cognitive load for clients. Before shipping Phase 8, audit whether `propose_memory_evolution` + `apply_memory_evolution` can collapse into a single tool with an `action` parameter, and whether `verify_memory` + `explain_memory` can be unified. The goal is the smallest surface that covers all assistant workflows. Consolidate before stabilizing the MCP contract.\" (spec §MCP Surface)\n\n> \"Each memory record requires: stable id, content, memory class, assertion type, scope, verification status, confidence and confidence reason, freshness policy, validity conditions, invalidation triggers, provenance events, evidence references, linked files, linked symbols, linked docs, linked tests, linked memories, contradiction links, supersession links, access history, usefulness scores, last verified state.\" (spec §Memory Graph)\n\n> \"Adopt the structure and link evolution. Do not adopt silent uncontrolled mutation. In this system, memory evolution should produce auditable proposals or transactional updates with provenance.\" (spec §A-Mem)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: R55 (Phase 7 verification engine review) — every memory returned by `get_task_memory` must carry its current verification status; `save_memory` must default to `unverified` and trigger a verification job per spec §Phase 7.\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/` — Phase 3 memory store, links, evidence, accesses, scores.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/working_memory/` — Phase 5 working-memory operations.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/` — Phase 2 event writer (emits `MemoryCreated`, `MemoryUpdated`, `MemoryRetrieved`, `MemoryInvalidated`).\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` — MCP tool registration.\n  - Phase 4 retrieval pipeline (used by `get_task_memory` for typed-stream candidate retrieval).\n  - T02 MCP compatibility policy (`docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md`).\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Hard limits, §Single source of truth, §No broken windows, §Schema parity, §Observability; Lattice rules on Markdown heading references; `AGENTS.md` backward-compatibility discipline.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §MCP Surface and §Memory Graph in full. Quote the \"Tool surface discipline\" paragraph verbatim into a doc comment on `memory_v2/mod.rs` so the rationale for collapsing `propose_memory_evolution` + `apply_memory_evolution` is preserved at the call site.\n2. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/mod.rs` exporting the three tools and the shared request/response types (`TaskMemoryBundle`, `MemoryRecord`, `EvolutionProposal`, `EvolutionAction`).\n3. Implement `get_task_memory` in `memory_v2/get_task_memory.rs`: take `task_id` (resolved through Phase 1 identity) plus optional `intent_hint` and `budget_tokens`; query the Phase 5 working-memory checkpoint for active context; query Phase 3 typed memory streams (`Observation`, `Decision`, `Constraint`, `Pattern`, `AntiPattern`, `WorkflowOutcome`, `FailurePattern`, `Procedure`, `Preference`, `ArchitectureInvariant`, `DocsContract`, `OpenQuestion`, `CounterMemory`) for relevant durable claims; rank via the Phase 4 scorer; return a compact `TaskMemoryBundle` where each entry carries inclusion reason, evidence strength, verification status, freshness status, contradiction/supersession state, scope, and an expansion handle per spec §MCP Tool Contract Principles \"Every memory-bearing response should identify…\".\n4. Implement `save_memory` in `memory_v2/save_memory.rs`: accept all spec-required memory fields (`content`, `memory_class`, `assertion_type`, `scope`, `confidence`, `confidence_reason`, `freshness_policy`, `validity_conditions`, `invalidation_triggers`, evidence event refs, linked files/symbols/docs/tests). Validate scope-aware filters (spec §Risks \"Scope Leakage\"), default `verification_status = unverified`, persist via Phase 3 store, emit a `MemoryCreated` event via Phase 2 writer, enqueue a verification job per Phase 7, and return the created `MemoryId` plus the resulting `MemoryRecord`.\n5. Implement `propose_memory_evolution` in `memory_v2/propose_memory_evolution.rs` as the unified tool with an `action: \"propose\" | \"apply\" | \"reject\"` parameter (collapsed per spec §MCP Surface \"Tool surface discipline\"). On `propose`, persist a proposal record referencing the source memory and the proposed delta (content change, link addition, supersession, invalidation) without altering durable memory; on `apply`, apply the proposal transactionally, emit `MemoryUpdated`/`MemoryConsolidated` events, and preserve prior state in `memory_evidence` per spec §Memory Graph \"Memory evolution should produce auditable proposals or transactional updates with provenance\"; on `reject`, mark the proposal rejected and emit a consolidation outcome event.\n6. Every tool must emit the appropriate Phase 2 events (`MemoryRetrieved`, `MemoryCreated`, `MemoryUpdated`, `MemoryConsolidated`, `MemoryInvalidated`) and stay within the hot-path budget for the tools that participate in the hot path.\n7. Register the three new tools in `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`. Per the T02 compatibility policy, the spec's nominal `apply_memory_evolution` name continues to respond as a deprecation shim that internally calls `propose_memory_evolution` with `action: \"apply\"`; the shim emits a deprecation warning in the response.\n8. Scope-leak controls: every store query must include `scope` filters at the store layer (spec §Risks \"Scope Leakage\" requires \"scope-aware queries, enforced filters in store APIs, and negative tests\"). Reject any cross-scope leak with a typed error rather than silently returning empty.\n9. In `memory_v2/memory_tools_tests.rs`, write tests that: (a) round-trip each tool's request/response through serde; (b) assert `get_task_memory` surfaces inclusion reason + verification status for every returned memory; (c) assert `save_memory` defaults `verification_status = unverified`, persists every spec field, emits a `MemoryCreated` event, and enqueues a verification job; (d) assert `propose_memory_evolution` with `action = propose` does NOT alter durable memory, `apply` updates transactionally with provenance preserved, `reject` records rejection; (e) assert scope-leak negative tests (a session-scoped query cannot return a branch-scoped memory created in a different branch); (f) assert the `apply_memory_evolution` shim continues to respond and forwards correctly.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_task_memory.rs` — `get_task_memory` tool returning compact, ranked, fully-annotated task memory bundles.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/save_memory.rs` — `save_memory` tool persisting new memory with all spec-required fields, defaulting to `unverified`, and enqueueing verification.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/propose_memory_evolution.rs` — unified `propose_memory_evolution` tool with `action: propose | apply | reject`, collapsing the spec's two-tool API per §MCP Surface tool-surface discipline.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/memory_tools_tests.rs` — unit + scope-leak negative tests covering schema, default values, event emission, verification enqueue, transactional apply, and the shim path.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_task_memory.rs` — confirms the `get_task_memory` file exists at the harness path.\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/save_memory.rs` — confirms the `save_memory` file exists at the harness path.\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/propose_memory_evolution.rs` — confirms the unified `propose_memory_evolution` file exists at the harness path.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::memory_v2::memory_tools_tests` — every memory-tool test passes (schema, defaults, event emission, transactional apply, scope-leak negatives, shim forwarding).\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file (split per-tool when needed).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10.\n- Schema parity: every request/response struct derives `Serialize`, `Deserialize`, `Debug`, `Clone`; every public field has a doc comment; the `EvolutionAction` enum is `Serialize`/`Deserialize` with snake_case wire names.\n- No silent error handling — every store/event-writer failure returns a typed error; scope-leak rejections are explicit errors, not empty results.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code; no unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming (`EvolutionAction::Apply`, not `EvolutionAction::Do`).\n- For SQLite: all writes go through Phase 3 store APIs; no raw SQL in the RPC layer; transactional apply uses the Phase 3 transaction primitive.\n- Observability: each tool emits `tracing::info!` spans with `tool`, `task_id`, `session_id`, `scope`, `memory_count` fields.\n- Doc citation: cite spec headings `## MCP Surface` (including the \"Tool surface discipline\" paragraph) and `## Memory Graph` in module doc comments.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: the unified `propose_memory_evolution` is shipped in this task; the spec's two-tool API is collapsed before MCP contract stabilization per §MCP Surface \"Consolidate before stabilizing the MCP contract.\"\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed; the `apply_memory_evolution` deprecation shim continues to respond per the T02 compatibility policy.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4253,"cache_read_input_tokens":64195,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4253,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012n7S8LWZzY1cvitTHPzudV","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"94b8eb29-8d6d-4ba6-bb27-e58f56b043db","request_id":"req_011Cb7MvNok52tFCLxfFdHF5","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 8+9+Gate task briefs"}
