{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01M8uBUCTUJMj3USgaU3iXWd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014zNDdXZx4dBGs3FpiMxAG8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T42.md","content":"# T42 — Phase 6 — LLM-driven jobs: episode summary, procedure extraction, contradiction detection, failure-pattern extraction\n\n**Phase:** 6\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** T39, T40, T41\n**Spec anchor:** [§Consolidation Engine — LLM-driven consolidation](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#6-consolidation-engine), [§Phase 6: Consolidation Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-6-consolidation-engine)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task implements the four LLM-driven consolidation jobs the spec calls out as inherently non-deterministic: episode-summary generation (richer than T40's deterministic template), procedure extraction from repeated successful workflows, contradiction detection across memories, and failure-pattern extraction from repeated diagnostics. The spec is explicit that these jobs MUST run only in background or manual-review modes, NEVER on the synchronous post-task hot path, and MUST emit proposals (never silent writes). This task ships the four job implementations and the LLM-driver abstraction; T43 layers provenance and budgets on top, T44 adds the manual-review queue for high-scope outputs, T45 makes the work replay-safe.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Several consolidation jobs (episode summary generation, procedure extraction, contradiction detection, failure-pattern extraction) cannot be implemented deterministically and require LLM inference.\"\n\n> \"LLM-driven jobs run only in background or manual review modes, never on the synchronous post-task hot path.\"\n\n> \"each LLM-driven job produces a proposal record, not a direct write; proposals require explicit apply or reject before altering durable memory\"\n\n> \"failed or malformed LLM responses must leave the prior memory state unchanged and emit a consolidation failure event\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: T39 (proposal runtime, queue, schema), T40 (synchronous session consolidator — these LLM jobs are its background counterpart for richer summaries), T41 (deterministic scanners — these LLM jobs may consume their proposals as hints).\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/` — task slices and tool-call traces consumed by episode and procedure extraction.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/` — `EpisodeMemory`, `ProcedureMemory`, `ContradictionMemory`, `FailurePatternMemory` classes from Phase 3.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/` — `WorkflowOutcome` aggregator that signals which workflows succeeded repeatedly.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/proposal.rs` — `ConsolidationProposal` / `ProposalKind` defined in T39.\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Hard limits, §Error handling (failed LLM responses are control flow), §No broken windows; Lattice rules on doc-heading citation; spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties on no silent writes.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Consolidation Engine \"LLM-driven consolidation\" subsection in full; copy the six constraint bullets into the top-of-file doc comment on `llm/mod.rs`.\n2. In `consolidation/llm/mod.rs`, define `pub trait LlmDriver { fn complete(&self, request: LlmRequest) -> Result<LlmResponse, LlmDriverError>; fn name(&self) -> &str; }` plus a `pub struct LlmJobContext { workspace_id, mode: ConsolidationMode, budget: LlmBudget }`. Enforce a runtime guard: every LLM job entry point asserts `ctx.mode != ConsolidationMode::SynchronousPostTask` and returns `Err(LlmJobError::ForbiddenOnHotPath)` otherwise.\n3. In `consolidation/llm/episode.rs`, implement `EpisodeSummaryJob::run(ctx, task_slice)` — fetch the event slice for a completed task, build a structured prompt requesting an episode summary, call the `LlmDriver`, parse the response into an `EpisodeMemory` candidate, and emit a `CreateMemory` or `UpdateMemory` proposal through the T39 runtime. On malformed JSON or driver error, emit a `ConsolidationFailed` event (new event-kind handler, reusing the Phase 2 event log) carrying `job_id`, `kind`, `error_kind`, leave any prior memory untouched, and return early.\n4. In `consolidation/llm/procedure.rs`, implement `ProcedureExtractionJob::run(ctx, workflow_id, occurrences)` — gather N≥3 successful traces of the same workflow shape, prompt the driver to extract the procedure (steps, preconditions, postconditions, tools used), and emit a `CreateMemory` proposal for a `ProcedureMemory`. Same malformed-response handling as episode.\n5. In `consolidation/llm/contradiction.rs`, implement `ContradictionDetectionJob::run(ctx, candidate_pair)` — given two memories the deterministic pass flagged as overlapping with conflicting assertions, prompt the driver to confirm contradiction and explain why. Emit an `UpdateMemory` proposal that flips one to `contradicted` and links it to the contradicting memory via `memory_links`. Same malformed handling.\n6. In `consolidation/llm/failure_pattern.rs`, implement `FailurePatternJob::run(ctx, diagnostic_cluster)` — given N≥2 `DiagnosticObserved` events with similar shape, prompt the driver to summarize the failure pattern and propose a `FailurePatternMemory`. Same malformed handling.\n7. Every job's malformed-response branch emits the consolidation failure event before returning. Add a `ConsolidationFailedPayload` to `events::kinds` if Phase 2 did not already include it (cite T11's event-kind list); otherwise reuse the existing payload.\n8. Register all four jobs in `consolidation/llm/mod.rs` so the runtime can dispatch by `ConsolidationJobKind`. Forbid synchronous mode at the dispatch layer in addition to the per-job guard (defense in depth).\n9. In `consolidation/llm/llm_tests.rs`, write tests with a fake `LlmDriver` that: (a) returns a well-formed response → a proposal is enqueued and prior memory is unchanged until apply, (b) returns malformed JSON → a `ConsolidationFailed` event is emitted and no proposal is enqueued, (c) the driver returns an error → same as malformed, (d) every job called with `ConsolidationMode::SynchronousPostTask` returns `ForbiddenOnHotPath` and the driver was never called, (e) per-job structured output round-trips (episode, procedure, contradiction, failure-pattern) into their respective memory classes.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/llm/mod.rs` — `LlmDriver` trait, `LlmJobContext`, mode guard, job dispatch registry; cites the six spec constraint bullets.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/llm/episode.rs` — `EpisodeSummaryJob` (LLM-rich variant of T40's deterministic template).\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/llm/procedure.rs` — `ProcedureExtractionJob` driven by repeated successful workflow shapes.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/llm/contradiction.rs` — `ContradictionDetectionJob` consuming deterministic-overlap candidates.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/llm/failure_pattern.rs` — `FailurePatternJob` driven by `DiagnosticObserved` clusters.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/llm/llm_tests.rs` — fake-driver-backed tests covering well-formed, malformed, error, and forbidden-mode paths per job.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/llm/mod.rs` — confirms the LLM job module root exists.\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/llm/contradiction.rs` — confirms the contradiction-detection job exists.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib consolidation::llm::llm_tests` — every LLM-job unit test passes.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. Each `run` method is a short pipeline: guard → prompt → call → parse → propose-or-fail.\n- Single source of truth: every proposal goes through T39; every event emission goes through the existing Phase 2 event writer; no parallel write paths.\n- Error handling: typed `LlmJobError` covers `ForbiddenOnHotPath`, `DriverError(LlmDriverError)`, `MalformedResponse(String)`, `BudgetExceeded`. Malformed/error branches MUST emit a `ConsolidationFailed` event before returning. No silent failure paths.\n- Naming: `EpisodeSummaryJob`, `ProcedureExtractionJob`, `ContradictionDetectionJob`, `FailurePatternJob`, `LlmDriver`. No generic `LlmHelper`/`Runner`.\n- Schema parity: every job's proposed-state JSON deserializes cleanly into the matching `MemoryClass` struct from Phase 3 (verify in tests).\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Observability: every job emits a `tracing::info_span!(\"llm_consolidation\", job_kind, workspace_id, mode, model_name)`; failure path also emits a `tracing::warn!` mirroring the `ConsolidationFailed` event payload.\n- Doc citation: each job file cites the exact `## 6. Consolidation Engine` \"LLM-driven consolidation\" bullet it implements and the `## Phase 6: Consolidation Engine` DoD (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` § Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content.\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: provenance (T43), high-scope review queue (T44), replay (T45), and integration tests (T46) are sibling tasks — but the four LLM jobs, the mode guard, the proposal-only invariant, and the malformed-response → failure-event behavior all ship in this task.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed and the architecture doc was updated in the same task.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3709,"cache_read_input_tokens":53202,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3709,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015qAoQeXM7HFtFDzBbPkUNq","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"bf92073c-b5f3-47f0-a475-b9537aa9c047","request_id":"req_011Cb7MmqeXLr2UsR7g5bqCY","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 6+7+Gate task briefs"}
