{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01VnVHrBqUuRyoA3FBgpwZ83","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01F3DH5Fpg8roxDtQWKpDiPK","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T73.md","content":"# T73 — Phase 10 — Promotion queue + contradiction queue with accept/reject (dialog modals)\n\n**Phase:** 10\n**Type:** frontend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T71\n**Spec anchor:** [§10. Human Review Surface](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#10-human-review-surface), [§6. Consolidation Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#6-consolidation-engine), [§Opaque Memory Mutation](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#opaque-memory-mutation)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); UI specification (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/ui-specification.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task delivers two of the most consequential operator surfaces in Phase 10: the promotion queue (proposed promotions awaiting accept/reject) and the contradiction queue (memory pairs the consolidation engine flagged as conflicting, awaiting a human verdict). Per spec §Opaque Memory Mutation, \"automatic consolidation corrupts durable repo knowledge\" is a named risk whose control is \"event-backed proposals, reversible updates, provenance, review queue for high-scope changes, and replay.\" This task implements the human side of that control: the queue UIs and the proposal-confirm dialogs that turn a proposed memory evolution into an applied write only when an operator explicitly clicks accept. Dialogs are native `<dialog>` elements per the UI specification — never `window.confirm`.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Required operator views: ... proposed promotions; proposed contradictions; ... one-click accept/reject for memory evolution proposals.\" (spec §10, §Phase 10 deliverables)\n\n> \"Each LLM-driven job produces a proposal record, not a direct write; proposals require explicit apply or reject before altering durable memory.\" (spec §6 — binds the accept/reject contract.)\n\n> \"Risk: automatic consolidation corrupts durable repo knowledge. Control: event-backed proposals, reversible updates, provenance, review queue for high-scope changes, and replay.\" (spec §Opaque Memory Mutation)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: T71 (review panel scaffolding) — supplies `ReviewPanelProvider`, `ReviewRpcBridge`, the i18n catalog, and the base modal primitive (native `<dialog>` mounted into the webview).\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `extension/src/review/reviewPanel.ts` — host the two queue subviews mount into.\n  - `extension/src/review/rpcBridge.ts` — typed methods this task consumes: `listPromotionProposals`, `applyPromotion`, `rejectPromotion`, `listContradictions`, `applyContradictionResolution`, `rejectContradictionResolution`.\n  - `extension/src/review/components/StatusBadge.ts` (from T72) — reused for proposal status badges (`pending`, `applied`, `rejected`, `expired`).\n- Standards files to honor: `coding.md` (no `window.confirm`, error handling, single source of truth, schema parity); `ui-specification.md` §7 (modals are native `<dialog>`, never `window.confirm/prompt/alert`), §7.2 (destructive-action confirms), §8.4 (toast feedback on mutations), §8.7 (success message phrasing), §8.5 (mandatory error display), §14 (i18n catalog).\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §6 Consolidation Engine, the \"LLM-driven consolidation\" subsection, §10 Human Review Surface, and §Opaque Memory Mutation risk control in full so the proposal-only-then-apply contract is grounded in the spec.\n2. Create `extension/src/review/promotionQueue.ts` exporting `mountPromotionQueue(host, bridge, i18n)`. The function lists pending promotion proposals (memory candidates the consolidation engine wants to elevate, e.g. session → branch, branch → repo) with columns: `Proposed Class`, `Current Scope`, `Target Scope`, `Confidence`, `Evidence Count`, `Created At`, `Status` badge, `Actions` (Review, Accept, Reject).\n3. Create `extension/src/review/contradictionQueue.ts` exporting `mountContradictionQueue(host, bridge, i18n)`. The function lists pending contradiction pairs with columns: `Memory A`, `Memory B`, `Link Type` (`contradicts`/`supersedes` candidate), `Detected By` (rule or LLM proposal provenance), `Created At`, `Status` badge, `Actions` (Review, Accept Resolution, Reject Resolution).\n4. Create `extension/src/review/components/ProposalDialog.ts` exporting `openProposalDialog({ proposal, onApply, onReject }, i18n)`. The dialog uses a native `<dialog>` element mounted into the webview (never `window.confirm`). The dialog renders: proposal summary, evidence list with file/symbol/event links, model + prompt-hash + response-hash provenance (per spec §6 LLM-driven consolidation), expected effect on durable memory, and a `Diff preview` panel showing the memory record before/after. Footer: `Cancel`, `Reject (with reason)`, `Accept and apply`.\n5. The dialog enforces typed-confirm for high-scope proposals (per `ui-specification.md` §7.2): if the target scope is `repo`, `user`, or `organization`, the operator must type the memory class name (e.g. `ArchitectureInvariant`) before the Accept button enables. Below `repo` scope, single-click accept is sufficient.\n6. The `onApply` handler calls `bridge.applyPromotion(proposalId)` (or `bridge.applyContradictionResolution(...)` for the contradiction dialog). Wrap in `try/catch`; on success post a `vscode.window.showInformationMessage('Promotion applied.')` and refresh the queue. On failure, render an inline error inside the dialog and call `vscode.window.showErrorMessage(err.message)` (per `ui-specification.md` §8.5).\n7. The `onReject` handler requires a reason string (rendered as a `<textarea>` inside the dialog, required to be non-empty). Calls `bridge.rejectPromotion(proposalId, reason)`. Reasons are persisted by the daemon as event-log evidence so rejected proposals are auditable per spec §Opaque Memory Mutation control.\n8. Add queue-specific i18n keys to `en.json` under `promotionQueue` and `contradictionQueue` namespaces: column headers, action labels, dialog title, dialog body strings, typed-confirm prompt, success/error toast strings. Status-badge labels reused from T71.\n9. Wrap every bridge call in `try/catch`. On read failure render the inline error banner; on mutation failure render inline + `vscode.window.showErrorMessage(err.message)`.\n10. Run `cd extension && npm run compile && npm run lint` and fix every error/warning before stopping.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `extension/src/review/promotionQueue.ts` — `mountPromotionQueue` subview controller listing pending promotions and routing actions through `ProposalDialog`.\n- `extension/src/review/contradictionQueue.ts` — `mountContradictionQueue` subview controller listing pending contradictions and routing actions through `ProposalDialog`.\n- `extension/src/review/components/ProposalDialog.ts` — single shared native `<dialog>` modal used by both queues, with typed-confirm gating for high-scope proposals.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f extension/src/review/promotionQueue.ts` — confirms the promotion queue file exists at the path the harness expects.\n- `test -f extension/src/review/contradictionQueue.ts` — confirms the contradiction queue file exists at the path the harness expects.\n- `test -f extension/src/review/components/ProposalDialog.ts` — confirms the dialog component exists at the path the harness expects.\n- `cd extension && npm run compile` — TypeScript compile succeeds with no errors.\n- `cd extension && npm run lint` — lint passes with zero warnings introduced by this task.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. Dialog state machine is a discriminated union, not nested booleans.\n- Single source of truth: `ProposalDialog.ts` is the only modal used by both queues; promotion and contradiction queues parameterize it via props rather than forking.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `// eslint-disable`.\n- No silent error handling — every bridge call surfaces failure to the dialog and to `vscode.window.showErrorMessage`.\n- Doc citation: comments cite `## 6. Consolidation Engine` for the proposal-only-then-apply contract and `## Opaque Memory Mutation` for the audit-trail requirement (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Markdown Heading References).\n\n### UI specification\n\n- All user-facing strings via `i18n.t(...)` from the `promotionQueue`, `contradictionQueue`, and `proposalDialog` namespaces; no inline literals in any of the three files.\n- All modals via native `<dialog>` (per `ui-specification.md` §7) — `ProposalDialog.ts` mounts an actual `<dialog>` element in the webview and uses `dialog.showModal()` / `dialog.close()`. No `window.confirm`, no `window.prompt`, no `window.alert`, no DaisyUI `modal modal-open` `<div>` pattern. Typed-confirm for high-scope (repo / user / organization) per `ui-specification.md` §7.2.\n- All mutation handlers (`onApply`, `onReject`) use `try/catch` with `vscode.window.showErrorMessage(err.message)` (`parseApiError + toast.error` is the Cadres web equivalent; for the VS Code extension this is the analogue per the build harness rule).\n- All ID inputs use `SearchableSelect` (webview) or `vscode.window.showQuickPick` (tree-view) — proposal selection inside the dialog uses `<dialog>` content, not a separate ID picker; if cross-references to other memories or events are picked, use `showQuickPick`, never raw `<select>` or `prompt`.\n- Sortable tables use `SortableHeader` + `useTableSort` equivalents on both queue tables. Sortable on `Confidence`, `Evidence Count`, `Created At`, and `Status`.\n- Status badges + loading + empty + error states for every interactive surface: badge for proposal status, loading skeleton on first load, distinct empty states (\"No pending promotions.\" vs \"No pending contradictions.\"), error banner on read failure, inline dialog error on apply/reject failure plus VS Code error toast.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] UI specification checks satisfied: native `<dialog>`, no `window.confirm`, typed-confirm for high-scope proposals, error handling on every mutation, reason required on every reject.\n- [ ] No deferred work: both queues + the shared dialog ship in this task; stale view (T74), event trace (T75), and graph/index health (T76) are sibling tasks, not deferrals.\n- [ ] After build, deploy per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy procedure.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6111,"cache_read_input_tokens":77427,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6111,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XjrTa6YAS1dmMW989ZPauZ","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"fcc99437-4fc6-4d24-96fb-320f9dce7740","request_id":"req_011Cb7MqWKneiRTEnKhFBPcy","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 10+11+Final task briefs"}
