standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: no item from spec §<this phase> punted to a later phase.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed and the architecture doc was updated in the same task.\n```\n\n**For review files (R05, R10), use this template instead:**\n\n```\n# <REVIEW_ID> — <Title from tasks.json>\n\n**Phase:** Review for Phase <N>\n**Type:** review\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** <list>\n**Spec anchor:** [§<phase section>](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#<anchor>)\n**Standards reviewed:** Cadres coding standard, definition-of-done checklist.\n\n## Purpose\n\nWhat this review certifies. 2-3 sentences.\n\n## Inputs to read\n\n- Every artifact produced by the listed dependency tasks.\n- Spec sections this phase claims to satisfy.\n- Shared standards: coding.md and definition-of-done-checklist.md sections relevant to this phase.\n\n## Review procedure\n\n1. ... step\n2. ... step\n... be specific about what to grep for, what tests to re-run, what schema columns to spot-check.\n\n## Required sections in the review output file\n\nThe reviewer writes to `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/<REVIEW_ID>-<slug>.md` with these mandatory headings (each must contain real findings, not \"n/a\"):\n\n- `## Spec alignment` — phase-by-phase coverage matrix.\n- `## Coding-standard alignment` — line-by-line audit vs. hard limits.\n- `## P99 budget evidence` (only for phases that have a P99 SLA in the spec).\n- `## Findings` — issues found, severity, suggested follow-up tasks (do NOT defer outside this build).\n- `## Verdict` — `PASS`, `PASS-WITH-FOLLOWUP-TASK-Txx`, or `BLOCK` (with named blockers).\n\n## Verification\n\nList each command from tasks.json verbatim with a sentence explaining what passing means.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Review markdown file exists at the path verification commands check.\n- [ ] Every required section above is present with concrete content.\n- [ ] If verdict is BLOCK, the blocking issues are listed and a follow-up task is opened in this build (never deferred to a future session).\n```\n\n**Task-specific content guidance:**\n\n- T01 produces `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-fork-or-extend-decision.md`. The decision considers the four gate conditions in spec §Phase 0 (breaking memories table changes, identity primary-key changes, event log requiring incompatible WAL changes, two-or-more of the above). The decision MUST document evidence and a branch-or-repo name.\n- T02 produces architecture overview (workspace graph, event log, memory graph sections required) + MCP compatibility policy (backward compatibility required).\n- T03 names new crates `lattice-identity`, `lattice-events`, `lattice-memory`, `lattice-retrieval`, `lattice-working-memory`, `lattice-consolidation`, `lattice-verification` (live under daemon/crates/) OR documents why they're modules in `lattice-core` instead. Storage migration policy must include migration order and rollback.\n- T04 captures baseline benchmarks of EXISTING workflows so Phase 4/9 has something to regress against. Bench file uses criterion conventions.\n- T06–T09 implement the unified identity model from spec §Phase 1: stable IDs for files, symbols, docs, sections, events, memories, context handles; identity resolver with ambiguity diagnostics; serialization in MCP payloads; legacy name compat. P99 budget ≤2ms.\n- R05 reviews Phase 0; R10 reviews Phase 1 (must include \"P99 budget evidence\" section).\n\nRead the spec yourself for the exact spec section text and quote it. Cite spec headings precisely.\n\nWrite all 11 files. Then report a one-line confirmation per file with `ls -la` style output. Do NOT modify tasks.json. Do NOT modify context.md or plan.md. Do NOT implement any code in daemon/ or extension/.","agentId":"aede099a0ec974b60","agentType":"general-purpose","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 11