{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01KfbHujQgTf2xL6BHMDNHxQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JaUehHfMda4juEMcTBkWUD","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T43.md","content":"# T43 — Phase 6 — LLM provenance (model + prompt hash + response hash) + queue bounds + cost budgets\n\n**Phase:** 6\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** T42\n**Spec anchor:** [§Consolidation Engine — LLM-driven consolidation](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#6-consolidation-engine), [§Phase 6: Consolidation Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-6-consolidation-engine)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task makes every LLM-driven consolidation proposal from T42 auditable, reproducible, and bounded. It adds the provenance record (model name + prompt hash + response hash attached to each proposal), enforces the spec's bounded-queue-with-warning behavior at the LLM-job submission point, encodes per-job-type cost and latency budgets, and publishes the budget rationale as an architecture doc the operator can consult. It also nails down the malformed/failed-response contract: prior memory MUST remain unchanged and a `ConsolidationFailed` event MUST be emitted. Without this task, T42's LLM jobs would be reproducible only by luck and budget overruns would propagate silently.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"each job records its model, prompt hash, and response hash as part of the proposal provenance so outputs are auditable and reproducible\"\n\n> \"consolidation queue depth must be bounded; when the queue is full, new jobs are dropped with a log warning rather than stalling the daemon\"\n\n> \"cost and latency budgets for LLM consolidation should be documented per job type before Phase 6 begins; jobs exceeding budget must fall back to deterministic approximations or skip with a stale flag\"\n\n> \"failed or malformed LLM responses must leave the prior memory state unchanged and emit a consolidation failure event\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: T42 — `LlmDriver`, `LlmJobContext`, the four LLM jobs. Provenance attaches to the proposals they emit; budgets gate their `run` calls.\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/proposal.rs` (T39) — `ConsolidationProposal` gains an `LlmProvenance` optional field.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/queue.rs` (T39) — bounded depth + drop-warning behavior; this task adds per-LLM-kind sub-quotas.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/` — `ConsolidationFailed` event from T42.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` — SQLite migration runner; `consolidation_proposals` gains provenance columns.\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Hard limits, §Error handling, §Observability, §No broken windows; Lattice rules on Markdown heading references for budget-bound behavior.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Consolidation Engine \"LLM-driven consolidation\" bullets 4, 5, and 6 verbatim and copy into the top-of-file doc comment on `llm/provenance.rs` and `llm/budget.rs`.\n2. In `consolidation/llm/provenance.rs`, define `pub struct LlmProvenance { model: String, prompt_sha256: [u8; 32], response_sha256: [u8; 32], prompt_token_count: u32, response_token_count: u32, latency_ms: u32, called_at: DateTime<Utc> }`. Implement `LlmProvenance::record(driver_name, prompt_bytes, response_bytes, prompt_tokens, response_tokens, latency)` that hashes both blobs with SHA-256 (using the existing `sha2` crate or workspace-pinned equivalent).\n3. Extend `ConsolidationProposal` with `provenance: Option<LlmProvenance>` (deterministic proposals leave it `None`; LLM jobs set it). Add a migration adding `provenance_json TEXT NULL` to `consolidation_proposals`.\n4. In `consolidation/llm/budget.rs`, define `pub struct LlmBudget { max_prompt_tokens: u32, max_response_tokens: u32, max_latency_ms: u32, max_cost_micro_usd: u32 }` and `pub enum BudgetOutcome { Within, ExceededFallback(DeterministicFallback), ExceededSkipWithStale }`. Per spec: exceeding budget either falls back to a deterministic approximation (episode → T40 deterministic template; procedure → no-op; contradiction → deterministic supersession candidate from T41) or skips and flags affected memory as `stale`.\n5. Provide a per-job-kind `BudgetCatalog::for_kind(kind) -> LlmBudget` returning the budgets documented in step 8 below. The catalog reads from `LatticeConfig` so operators can override; defaults are pinned in code AND mirrored verbatim in the architecture doc.\n6. Extend the `BoundedJobQueue` from T39 with per-kind sub-quotas: when an LLM job's queue slice is full, drop the new job with a `tracing::warn!` carrying `kind`, `current_depth`, `max_depth`, `workspace_id`. Emit a `ConsolidationFailed` event with `error_kind = QueueFull` so the failure is auditable in the event log, not just the tracing stream.\n7. Wire provenance into every LLM job's success path (`EpisodeSummaryJob`, `ProcedureExtractionJob`, `ContradictionDetectionJob`, `FailurePatternJob` — defined in T42): on a well-formed response, construct `LlmProvenance::record(...)` and attach it to the proposal before enqueuing. On a malformed/failed/budget-exceeded path, leave prior memory state unchanged and emit `ConsolidationFailed` with the right `error_kind`.\n8. Write `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-llm-budgets.md` with the mandatory headings and content: `## Scope`, `## Per-job budgets` (a table: job_kind | max_prompt_tokens | max_response_tokens | max_latency_ms | max_cost_micro_usd | fallback_strategy), `## Bounded queue depth`, `## Failure handling` (malformed → ConsolidationFailed, prior state unchanged), `## Provenance record` (fields + hash algorithm + reproducibility guarantee), `## Operator overrides` (config keys), `## Spec citation` (link to `## 6. Consolidation Engine` \"LLM-driven consolidation\").\n9. In `consolidation/llm/provenance_tests.rs`, write tests that: (a) successful job attaches `LlmProvenance` with deterministic SHA-256 hashes computed from prompt + response bytes, (b) re-running the same prompt and response yields the same hashes (reproducibility), (c) a budget overrun triggers `ExceededFallback` for episode/contradiction and `ExceededSkipWithStale` for procedure/failure-pattern per the catalog, (d) per-kind queue overflow drops the job, emits the warn log, and writes a `ConsolidationFailed` event, (e) the architecture doc exists and contains the required headings (sanity-grep from the test harness using `include_str!`).\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/llm/provenance.rs` — `LlmProvenance` struct, SHA-256 hashing, attachment to proposals.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/llm/budget.rs` — `LlmBudget`, `BudgetOutcome`, `BudgetCatalog`, fallback dispatch.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/llm/provenance_tests.rs` — provenance reproducibility, budget overruns, per-kind queue drops, failure-event emission.\n- `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-llm-budgets.md` — per-job-type cost and latency budgets, queue bounds, failure handling, provenance record format, operator overrides, spec citation.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/llm/provenance.rs` — confirms the provenance module exists.\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/llm/budget.rs` — confirms the budget module exists.\n- `test -f docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-llm-budgets.md` — confirms the architecture doc exists at the canonical path.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib consolidation::llm::provenance_tests` — every provenance + budget unit test passes.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file (`budget.rs` should stay compact; split per-kind fallback strategies into helpers if it grows).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. `LlmProvenance::record` and `BudgetCatalog::for_kind` are straight-line.\n- Single source of truth: budgets live in `BudgetCatalog`; the architecture doc mirrors the values but the catalog is canonical (note this in the doc).\n- Error handling: typed `BudgetError`, `ProvenanceError`. Malformed-response, budget-exceeded, and queue-full are normal control-flow outcomes — each emits a `ConsolidationFailed` event before returning.\n- Naming: `LlmProvenance::record`, `BudgetOutcome::ExceededFallback`, `BudgetCatalog::for_kind`. No `Helper`/`Manager`.\n- Schema parity: `provenance_json` column maps to `Option<LlmProvenance>` via serde; migration covers both up and (no-op) down direction.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Observability: every drop and budget overrun emits a `tracing::warn!` carrying `workspace_id`, `kind`, `current_depth`, `max_depth` (drops) or `actual_tokens`, `budget_tokens` (overruns), and writes the matching `ConsolidationFailed` event.\n- Doc citation: code comments cite `## 6. Consolidation Engine` \"LLM-driven consolidation\" bullets 4, 5, 6; the architecture doc links the same heading (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` § Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content, including the architecture budget doc at the canonical path.\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: every spec bullet about provenance, queue bounds, cost budgets, and malformed-response handling is in this task.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed and the architecture doc was updated in the same task.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15541,"cache_read_input_tokens":56911,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":15541,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015qAoQeXM7HFtFDzBbPkUNq","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"927f3d4c-63aa-4e08-ac65-05a177facb83","request_id":"req_011Cb7N1yvFZe4LypqRsfPgL","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 6+7+Gate task briefs"}
