{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01VT8gipuad96TX8SiC5vJU9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JvZswMJm52WEk12Gy4ztFp","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T32.md","content":"# T32 — Phase 4 — Retrieval benchmark suite + golden anchors + ranking tests\n\n**Phase:** 4\n**Type:** tests\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T27, T28, T29, T30, T31\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 4: Retrieval V1](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-4-retrieval-v1), [§Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-9-metrics-and-evaluation), [§Retrieval Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#7-retrieval-engine)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task closes Phase 4 with the benchmark suite, golden anchor fixtures, and ranking regression tests required by spec §Phase 4 deliverables (\"benchmark suite for realistic assistant tasks\") and §Phase 4 Definition of Done (\"irrelevant memory rate is measured and regressed\"). The benchmark must measure end-to-end retrieval against a fixed set of representative tasks, the golden anchor tests must pin the anchor-resolution behaviour against a curated corpus, and ranking regression tests must guard against silent reordering of the ranked output as future signals are tuned. Metrics are written to a baseline JSON file under `docs/plans/.../baselines/` so future runs can diff against it without re-reading the test fixtures.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 4: Retrieval V1 — Deliverables: ... benchmark suite for realistic assistant tasks.\" (spec §Phase 4: Retrieval V1)\n\n> \"Definition of done: ... irrelevant memory rate is measured and regressed.\" (spec §Phase 4: Retrieval V1)\n\n> \"Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation — Deliverables: golden benchmark task set; precision/recall measurement for retrieved memory; usefulness measurement; freshness and staleness metrics; consolidation throughput metrics; CLI for metrics reporting.\" (spec §Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs:\n  - T27 intent classifier, T28 anchor resolver, T29 candidate retrieval, T30 scorer + diagnostics, T31 shaper — the full Phase 4 pipeline is in place before this task runs.\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/benchmark_tests.rs` and `query/benchmark_tests.rs` — convention for benchmark-style tests under `cargo test -- --include-ignored`.\n  - `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/` (created earlier in the build) — directory the baseline metrics JSON is written into.\n- Standards files to honor: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (tests as documentation: one test per behaviour, ≤30 lines per test, named for the behaviour); `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md` (verification is real shell commands).\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Re-read spec §Phase 4 deliverables and Definition of Done, and §Phase 9 metrics list, to fix the metrics the benchmark must emit: top-K precision, top-K recall, irrelevant-memory rate, mean rank of golden result, P50/P95 retrieval latency, candidates per source, dedupe rate, truncation rate.\n2. Curate a golden anchor corpus in `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/golden_tests.rs` covering each anchor type (path, symbol, error string, command, API name, config key) with at least three task statements per type, the expected resolved identities, and the expected top-1 result identity. The corpus is in code (not external fixtures) so the test is hermetic.\n3. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/benchmark.rs` as an `#[ignore]`d test that builds a synthetic workspace (small fixture graph + memories + events), runs the full retrieval pipeline against the golden corpus, computes the metrics list above, asserts against pinned thresholds documented inline, and writes the metric snapshot to `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/retrieval_v1_metrics.json`. The `#[ignore]` lets `cargo test` stay fast while CI runs `cargo test -- --include-ignored`.\n4. Implement ranking regression tests in `golden_tests.rs`: for every golden task, assert that the top-1 result is the expected identity, that the second result is not a stale memory unless the task expects one, and that the inclusion reason for the top result mentions the dominant signal (e.g. an exact-symbol-match task surfaces \"exact identifier match\" in the reason). Tests are ≤30 lines each.\n5. Pin a stale-memory regression: include at least one golden task where a stale memory exists in the fixture and assert that the stale memory ranks below the trusted result, per spec §Stale Memory Leakage control.\n6. Pin a budget regression: include at least one golden task with a deliberately-oversized candidate set and assert that truncation flips `BudgetReport::truncated`, that pinned results survive truncation, and that the bundle still ships within the documented token cap.\n7. Write `retrieval_v1_metrics.json` schema documentation as a doc comment at the top of `benchmark.rs`: every field, its meaning, its threshold, and the rule for tightening it.\n8. Add a CLI hook (small Rust binary entry under the existing benchmark scaffolding, or a `cargo run --example retrieval_v1_metrics`) only if the existing benchmark convention supports it; otherwise the `--include-ignored` test alone satisfies the verification command. Document the convention chosen at the top of `benchmark.rs`.\n9. Run all four verification commands locally; fix any clippy warnings before stopping.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/benchmark.rs` — benchmark harness, metric computation, baseline-JSON writer.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/golden_tests.rs` — golden anchor corpus and ranking regression tests.\n- `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/retrieval_v1_metrics.json` — pinned baseline metrics emitted by the benchmark.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/benchmark.rs` — confirms the benchmark module exists at the expected path.\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/golden_tests.rs` — confirms the golden-test module exists at the expected path.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib retrieval_v1::golden_tests` — runs the golden-anchor and ranking-regression tests.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib retrieval_v1::benchmark -- --include-ignored` — runs the benchmark and emits the baseline metrics JSON.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file. If the golden corpus grows beyond the cap, split into `golden_tests/` submodules grouped by anchor kind.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. Each test ≤30 lines per `coding.md` \"Tests as documentation\".\n- Schema parity: `retrieval_v1_metrics.json` field set mirrors the `BenchmarkMetrics` struct in `benchmark.rs` exactly; both are updated in the same commit.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Single source of truth: thresholds live in `benchmark.rs` as documented constants; they are not duplicated in `golden_tests.rs`.\n- No broken windows: dead imports removed, every test is named for the behaviour it asserts (e.g. `test_exact_symbol_anchor_returns_correct_identity`).\n- Doc citation: thresholds cite `## Phase 4: Retrieval V1` (Definition of Done) and `## Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation` per `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: every metric the spec names (top-K precision/recall, irrelevant-memory rate, latency) is computed by the benchmark; every anchor type has at least one golden test; the stale-memory and truncation regressions are pinned.\n- [ ] `retrieval_v1_metrics.json` is checked in with realistic baseline values produced by an actual benchmark run, not placeholders.\n- [ ] The Phase 4 Definition-of-Done item \"irrelevant memory rate is measured and regressed\" has a single named test that asserts it.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3760,"cache_read_input_tokens":59914,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3760,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":46,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019RjXwCuf57BAKn88mWkE24","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"c811ffb9-e710-45cb-baa8-2368ee072044","request_id":"req_011Cb7N3i9H91jNL98UqmPGP","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 4+5 task briefs"}
