{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01DKqsA9GSR28Z9docHMsRqr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EUFHk1ywsQwkYwKK5eG5uN","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T60.md","content":"# T60 — Phase 8 — New tools: consolidate_session + get_memory_metrics + get_event_trace\n\n**Phase:** 8\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** R55\n**Spec anchor:** [§MCP Surface](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#9-mcp-surface)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task introduces the three remaining new MCP tools from spec §MCP Surface: `consolidate_session` (trigger session-level consolidation producing episode/procedure/failure-pattern proposals), `get_memory_metrics` (return the assistant-usefulness signals required by spec §Phase 9), and `get_event_trace` (return a paginated event-log slice scoped by task/session/workspace for audit and replay). Together these three tools complete the new memory surface and make the underlying substrates inspectable from any MCP client. Without them, Phase 6 consolidation runs only autonomously, Phase 9 metrics surface nothing to assistants, and the Phase 2 event log is invisible — all violations of spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties \"every background consolidation pass is recoverable, replayable, and observable\" and §MCP Tool Contract Principles.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"New or redesigned memory tools: …`consolidate_session`, `get_memory_metrics`, `get_event_trace`.\" (spec §MCP Surface)\n\n> \"Consolidation modes: synchronous post-task consolidation for small task traces; background scheduled consolidation for larger histories; manual review mode for high-impact repo or organization memories; replay mode for rebuilding memory state from the event log.\" (spec §Consolidation Engine)\n\n> \"Required metrics: tool calls per successful task; irrelevant files opened per task; relevant anchor recall; memory inclusion precision; memory later-used rate; stale memory surfaced rate; contradiction missed rate; tests recommended versus tests needed; workflow success after first plan.\" (spec §Phase 9)\n\n> \"The full event stream should not be injected into prompts. It exists for retrieval, audit, replay, metrics, and consolidation.\" (spec §Event Log)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: R55 (Phase 7 verification engine review) — consolidation proposals must respect verification state, and metrics include verification-derived signals (stale memory surfaced rate, contradiction missed rate).\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/` — Phase 6 consolidation engine (deterministic jobs + LLM-driven proposals).\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/` — Phase 2 event reader/query API.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/` — to be created in T65 with the full signal set. T60 wires this module through MCP only after T65 exists; if T65 isn't yet on disk at runtime, `get_memory_metrics` returns the partial set already collected via session_metrics with an `incomplete: true` flag (no fabricated values).\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/session_metrics.rs` — existing per-session telemetry, reused as a fallback source.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` — MCP tool registration.\n  - Phase 1 identity types.\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Hard limits, §Single source of truth, §No broken windows, §Schema parity, §Observability; Lattice rules on Markdown heading references; `AGENTS.md` backward-compatibility discipline.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §MCP Surface, §Consolidation Engine, §Phase 9, and §Event Log in full.\n2. Implement `consolidate_session` in `memory_v2/consolidate_session.rs`. Accept `session_id: SessionId`, `mode: \"post_task\" | \"background\" | \"manual_review\" | \"replay\"` (defaults to `post_task`), and optional `budget_ms` for synchronous mode. Internally enqueue the appropriate Phase 6 consolidation jobs against the session's event slice; return a `ConsolidationReport` enumerating each proposal produced (episode summary, promoted procedure, promoted failure pattern, supersession candidate, duplicate detection) with proposal IDs that can be applied/rejected via the unified `propose_memory_evolution` from T58. Honor spec §Consolidation Engine \"No consolidation job may silently rewrite high-scope memory without preserving provenance and prior state\" — all outputs are proposals, never silent writes.\n3. Implement `get_memory_metrics` in `memory_v2/get_memory_metrics.rs`. Accept optional `scope: session | branch | repo | user | organization`, optional `time_range`, and `signals: Vec<MetricSignal>` (defaults to all). Return the full spec §Phase 9 \"Required metrics\" set: `tool_calls_per_successful_task`, `irrelevant_files_opened_per_task`, `relevant_anchor_recall`, `memory_inclusion_precision`, `memory_later_used_rate`, `stale_memory_surfaced_rate`, `contradiction_missed_rate`, `tests_recommended_vs_needed`, `workflow_success_after_first_plan`. Source values from the T65 metrics module when present; fall back to `session_metrics` and event-log aggregations with an explicit `source` field on every value so the caller knows where each number came from. Never fabricate missing values — return `null` with a reason instead.\n4. Implement `get_event_trace` in `memory_v2/get_event_trace.rs`. Accept `task_id | session_id | workspace_id` plus optional `kinds: Vec<EventKind>` filter, `since: DateTime<Utc>`, `until: DateTime<Utc>`, and pagination cursor. Return ordered envelopes from the Phase 2 reader, compact-by-default (one-line summary per event) with stable expansion handles for full payload retrieval. Enforce workspace boundary checks per spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties — never return events from a different workspace.\n5. All three tools must support compact + full + diagnostic render modes per spec §MCP Tool Contract Principles. `get_event_trace` diagnostic mode includes payload hashes and any spilled-payload row IDs for replay.\n6. Each tool emits the appropriate Phase 2 events: `consolidate_session` emits `MemoryConsolidated`; `get_memory_metrics` emits a `ToolCalled` + `ToolResult` pair; `get_event_trace` emits `ToolCalled` + `ToolResult` (does not emit a re-entrant event for each returned envelope — that would create a feedback loop).\n7. Register the three tools in `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs`. No deprecation shims needed — these tool names exist only in the new surface.\n8. In `memory_v2/admin_tools_tests.rs`, write tests that: (a) round-trip each tool's request/response through serde; (b) assert `consolidate_session` produces proposals (never direct writes), and assert proposals are addressable via `propose_memory_evolution`; (c) assert `get_memory_metrics` returns every spec-required signal name or an explicit `null` with reason; (d) assert `get_memory_metrics` never fabricates values; (e) assert `get_event_trace` enforces workspace boundary (cross-workspace request returns a typed error); (f) assert pagination cursor stability across calls; (g) assert each tool emits the correct Phase 2 events.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/consolidate_session.rs` — `consolidate_session` triggering Phase 6 jobs and returning proposal IDs.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_memory_metrics.rs` — `get_memory_metrics` returning the full spec §Phase 9 signal set with explicit source per value.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_event_trace.rs` — `get_event_trace` returning paginated, workspace-bounded event slices with compact + diagnostic render modes.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/admin_tools_tests.rs` — unit tests covering schema, proposal-only writes, metric source fidelity, workspace boundary enforcement, pagination stability, and event emission.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/consolidate_session.rs` — confirms the `consolidate_session` file exists at the harness path.\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/get_event_trace.rs` — confirms the `get_event_trace` file exists at the harness path.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::memory_v2::admin_tools_tests` — every admin-tool test passes.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10.\n- Schema parity: `ConsolidationReport`, `MetricSnapshot`, `EventTracePage` derive `Serialize`, `Deserialize`, `Debug`, `Clone`; every public field has a doc comment; the `mode` enum on `consolidate_session` is serde-tagged with snake_case wire names; `MetricSignal` reuses the canonical Phase 9 enum from T65 once present.\n- No silent error handling — workspace-boundary violations are typed errors; missing metrics are explicit `null` with a `reason` field, never zero.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code; no unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming (`MetricSnapshot::source`, not `MetricSnapshot::src`).\n- For SQLite: queries go through Phase 2/3/6 APIs; no raw SQL in the RPC layer.\n- Observability: each tool emits `tracing::info!` spans with `tool`, `scope`, `event_count` or `proposal_count` fields.\n- Doc citation: cite spec headings `## MCP Surface`, `## Consolidation Engine`, `## Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation`, and `## Event Log` in module doc comments.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: all three tools ship with their full request/response surface; consolidation produces proposals only, metrics include the entire spec §Phase 9 signal set or explicit `null` with reason, event trace is workspace-bounded.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3976,"cache_read_input_tokens":73212,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3976,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012n7S8LWZzY1cvitTHPzudV","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"0f1fc265-868c-40b2-97f9-48153a10f0f3","request_id":"req_011Cb7N4DdZErwLbWBNCk8p7","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 8+9+Gate task briefs"}
