{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01KfbHujQgTf2xL6BHMDNHxQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MtC7iTtEeQGC746kjHfP5s","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T44.md","content":"# T44 — Phase 6 — Manual review queue for high-scope memory changes (repo + organization scope)\n\n**Phase:** 6\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T39, T42\n**Spec anchor:** [§Consolidation Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#6-consolidation-engine), [§Phase 6: Consolidation Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-6-consolidation-engine), [§Human Review Surface](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#10-human-review-surface)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task adds the spec-required manual-review queue for high-scope memory changes (repo and organization scope). Proposals targeting workspace-local or session-local memory may be auto-applied by operator policy, but every proposal whose target memory carries scope `repo` or `organization` MUST land in the manual-review queue and stay there until a human operator decides. The queue is the durable backing for the Phase 10 \"memory inbox\" UI surface listed in §Human Review Surface. Without this gate, T42's LLM-driven jobs could silently promote repo-wide claims into trusted state, violating the spec §Opaque Memory Mutation risk control.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Consolidation modes: ... manual review mode for high-impact repo or organization memories ...\"\n\n> \"Deliverables: ... manual review queue for high-scope memory changes ...\"\n\n> \"Required operator views: memory inbox; proposed promotions; proposed contradictions; ... consolidation queue.\" (§Human Review Surface)\n\n> \"No consolidation job may silently rewrite high-scope memory without preserving provenance and prior state.\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: T39 (proposal runtime + `consolidation_proposals` table), T42 (LLM jobs that produce most high-scope proposals).\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/` — `MemoryScope` enum (session / branch / repo / organization) from Phase 3.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/proposal.rs` — `ConsolidationProposal` is what gets queued.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/` — `OperatorId` (or equivalent actor identity) used to record `decided_by`.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/` — `MemoryConsolidated` event (apply path) and `ConsolidationFailed` event (reject is not a failure but is recorded too).\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Hard limits, §Error handling, §Schema / model parity, §Observability; Lattice rules on doc-heading citation; spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Consolidation Engine \"Consolidation modes\" and §Human Review Surface \"Required operator views\" lists. Copy the scope-gating rule into the top-of-file doc comment on `review_queue.rs`.\n2. In `consolidation/review_queue.rs`, define `pub struct ReviewQueue { /* backed by consolidation_proposals where scope ∈ {repo, organization} */ }` with operations: `enqueue(proposal)`, `list_pending(workspace_id, filter) -> Vec<ReviewItem>`, `decide(proposal_id, decision: ProposalDecision, decided_by: OperatorId, reason: Option<String>)`, `inspect(proposal_id) -> ReviewItem` (full prior + proposed state for the UI).\n3. Add a scope-gating hook in the T39 runtime: before enqueuing any proposal for execution, call `ReviewQueue::should_gate(proposal) -> bool` which returns `true` when the target memory's scope is `repo` or `organization`. Gated proposals skip the deterministic auto-apply path and stay `pending` in `consolidation_proposals` until `decide` is called.\n4. Define `pub struct ReviewItem { proposal_id, job_id, kind, scope, target_memory_id, prior_state, proposed_state, evidence, provenance: Option<LlmProvenance>, enqueued_at }`. Implement `From<ConsolidationProposalRow>` so the existing table backs the queue without a parallel store.\n5. Implement `decide`: it routes through the T39 `ConsolidationProposal::apply()` / `reject()` so the same audit path (event emission, prior-state preservation) applies. Record `decided_by` and `reason` in `consolidation_proposals.decision` / a new `decision_reason TEXT NULL` column (migration in this task).\n6. Add `list_pending` filters: `scope`, `kind`, `older_than`, `workspace_id`. Return results ordered by `enqueued_at ASC` so the oldest pending items surface first in the inbox.\n7. Expose a thin internal API on `ReviewQueue` so the Phase 10 review-UI plumbing can call it via JSON-RPC without re-implementing the gating logic. Cite the §Human Review Surface heading in the API doc comment so the boundary is explicit.\n8. In `consolidation/review_queue_tests.rs`, write tests that: (a) a `session`-scope proposal is NOT gated and proceeds to auto-apply, (b) a `branch`-scope proposal is NOT gated, (c) a `repo`-scope proposal IS gated and stays `pending`, (d) an `organization`-scope proposal IS gated and stays `pending`, (e) `decide(apply, operator_id, reason)` routes through `ConsolidationProposal::apply()` and emits `MemoryConsolidated` with the `decided_by` recorded, (f) `decide(reject, operator_id, reason)` leaves memory unchanged and records the rejection, (g) `list_pending` returns items in `enqueued_at ASC` order and honors filters, (h) calling `decide` twice on the same proposal is a no-op on the second call (idempotent), (i) the migration adds `decision_reason` and the schema round-trips.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/review_queue.rs` — `ReviewQueue`, `ReviewItem`, scope-gating hook, `list_pending` / `decide` / `inspect`, `decision_reason` migration registration.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/review_queue_tests.rs` — scope-gating coverage for all four scopes, apply/reject routing, ordering, filters, idempotence, migration round-trip.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/review_queue.rs` — confirms the review-queue module exists.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib consolidation::review_queue_tests` — every review-queue unit test passes.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. `decide` is a guard + dispatch (apply or reject) + record.\n- Single source of truth: gating decision lives in `ReviewQueue::should_gate`; apply/reject route through the T39 `ConsolidationProposal` API. No parallel write paths.\n- Error handling: typed `ReviewQueueError` (proposal not found, already decided, scope mismatch). No bare `unwrap`; no silent `.ok()`. Decision-on-non-pending is a typed `AlreadyDecided` outcome, not an error.\n- Naming: `ReviewQueue`, `ReviewItem`, `should_gate`, `decided_by`. No `Manager`/`Helper`.\n- Schema parity: `decision_reason` column maps to `Option<String>` on `ReviewItem` and `ConsolidationProposal`; migration covers up direction.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Observability: every `decide` call emits a `tracing::info_span!(\"manual_review_decision\", proposal_id, scope, decision, decided_by)` and writes the appropriate event through the existing event writer.\n- Doc citation: file-top doc comment cites `## 6. Consolidation Engine` \"Consolidation modes\" and `## 10. Human Review Surface` \"Required operator views\" (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` § Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content.\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: the review-UI webview is Phase 10 (R70 + downstream tasks), but the JSON-RPC-callable queue API and all gating logic ship here.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed and the architecture doc was updated in the same task.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15541,"cache_read_input_tokens":56911,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":15541,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015qAoQeXM7HFtFDzBbPkUNq","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"d5b729bf-3acd-4983-be95-787917cf1633","request_id":"req_011Cb7N1yvFZe4LypqRsfPgL","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 6+7+Gate task briefs"}
