{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_0139kC52VEu3YD1r5ACQ9dAL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016gvQUZeZmcnYPT16NbkckX","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T61.md","content":"# T61 — Phase 8 — Tool surface audit + final MCP reference doc (collapse overlapping tools per spec §MCP discipline)\n\n**Phase:** 8\n**Type:** docs\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** T56, T57, T58, T59, T60\n**Spec anchor:** [§MCP Surface](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#9-mcp-surface)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task produces the audited final MCP tool surface for the cognitive workspace fork: an audit doc recording which tools were collapsed and why, and the canonical reference doc enumerating every tool the daemon ships, its render modes, expansion handles, budget controls, deprecation status, and shim policy. Spec §MCP Surface \"Tool surface discipline\" makes this audit binding: \"ten new memory tools is a meaningful cognitive load for clients … The goal is the smallest surface that covers all assistant workflows. Consolidate before stabilizing the MCP contract.\" Without this task, the Phase 8 work ships an unaudited surface and Phase 9 metrics regress against the wrong set of tool names.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Tool surface discipline: ten new memory tools is a meaningful cognitive load for clients. Before shipping Phase 8, audit whether `propose_memory_evolution` + `apply_memory_evolution` can collapse into a single tool with an `action` parameter, and whether `verify_memory` + `explain_memory` can be unified. The goal is the smallest surface that covers all assistant workflows. Consolidate before stabilizing the MCP contract.\" (spec §MCP Surface)\n\n> \"Every tool response should support: compact rendering, full structured JSON, context handles, stable expansion targets, budget controls, diagnostic explanations where useful.\" (spec §MCP Surface)\n\n> \"Required workflow tools: `get_context_capsule`, `prepare_change`, `plan_edit`, `trace_scenario`, `diagnose_failure`, `find_relevant_tests`, `impact_from_diff`, `get_docs_capsule`, `get_backlinks`, `expand_context`, `get_working_set_context`, `get_repo_playbook`, `search_symbols`, `search_memory`, `record_workflow_outcome`.\" (spec §MCP Surface)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs:\n  - T56 (`workflow_v2/` edit-planning tools) — final names and request/response schemas.\n  - T57 (`workflow_v2/` discovery tools) — final names and request/response schemas.\n  - T58 (`memory_v2/` get_task_memory + save_memory + unified `propose_memory_evolution`).\n  - T59 (`memory_v2/` unified `verify_explain_memory` + `list_memory_conflicts`).\n  - T60 (`memory_v2/` consolidate_session + get_memory_metrics + get_event_trace).\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md` (from T02) — must be referenced for deprecation policy and shim removal cadence.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` — current registered tool list (43 today); the audit doc must reconcile every entry against the final list.\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Single source of truth, §No broken windows; Lattice rules on Markdown heading references — the reference doc is the authoritative MCP tool listing and must be cited by every subsequent doc.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §MCP Surface in full and quote the \"Tool surface discipline\" paragraph verbatim in `2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md` as the framing for the audit.\n2. In `2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md`, write a `## Audit findings` section that lists every collapse decision made during Phase 8: (a) `propose_memory_evolution` + `apply_memory_evolution` → unified `propose_memory_evolution` with `action` parameter (per T58); (b) `verify_memory` + `explain_memory` → unified `verify_explain_memory` with `mode` parameter (per T59); plus any further collapses identified while reviewing T56–T60. For each collapse, record: rationale, the spec sentence authorizing it, the deprecation shim policy, and the shim-removal deadline.\n3. In `2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md`, write a `## Collapsed tools` section that is a table or bullet list mapping each spec-nominal tool name to its actual implementation: `apply_memory_evolution → propose_memory_evolution(action=\"apply\")`; `verify_memory → verify_explain_memory(mode=\"verify\")`; `explain_memory → verify_explain_memory(mode=\"explain\")`; and any others identified. Each row links to the implementing file under `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/memory_v2/` or `workflow_v2/`.\n4. In `2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md`, write a `## Decisions not to collapse` section documenting any spec-nominal pair that was considered but NOT collapsed (e.g. `get_context_capsule` vs `get_docs_capsule` remain separate because they anchor on distinct identity types), with rationale.\n5. In `2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md`, write a `## Final tool list` section enumerating every tool the daemon ships after Phase 8. For each tool, include: canonical name, one-paragraph description, request schema summary, response schema summary, supported render modes (`compact` / `full` / `diagnostic` / handles), budget controls, emitted Phase 2 events, deprecation status, implementing file path. The list must include every spec §MCP Surface \"Required workflow tools\" and every new memory tool (counting the collapsed names) plus the deprecation shims kept active per the T02 compatibility policy.\n6. In `2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md`, add sections `## Render modes`, `## Expansion handles`, `## Budget controls`, `## Deprecation policy`, each citing the corresponding spec heading.\n7. Cross-link `2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md` ↔ `2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md` and reference back to spec §MCP Surface, §MCP Tool Contract Principles, and the T02 compatibility policy by exact heading.\n8. Confirm no spec §MCP Surface \"Required workflow tools\" entry is missing from the reference. Confirm no implemented tool is missing from the reference. The reference doc is single source of truth.\n9. Confirm both docs respect the Cadres coding standard `## Hard limits` (file ≤800 lines); split into two docs is already mandated by the verification commands.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md` — canonical reference enumerating every shipped MCP tool, render modes, expansion handles, budget controls, deprecation status, and implementing file paths.\n- `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md` — audit findings recording every tool collapse decision per spec §MCP Surface \"Tool surface discipline,\" including the table of collapsed tools and the deprecation shim policy.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md` — confirms the reference doc exists at the harness path.\n- `test -f docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md` — confirms the audit doc exists at the harness path.\n- `grep -q '## Final tool list' docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md` — confirms the reference enumerates the final tool list under a dedicated heading rather than burying it.\n- `grep -q '## Audit findings' docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md` — confirms the audit findings section exists under a dedicated heading.\n- `grep -q '## Collapsed tools' docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md` — confirms the collapsed-tools mapping is recorded under a dedicated heading rather than scattered through prose.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file (verify with `wc -l docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-surface-audit.md`).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10 — not applicable (docs task).\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code.\n- No unjustified `// allow(...)` or suppressions.\n- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming — applies to any tool/schema names mentioned in the docs; they must match the implementations in T56–T60.\n- For schema changes: the reference doc is the single source of truth; every divergence between docs and code is a contract gate failure caught by R64.\n- Doc citation: cite the exact `## MCP Surface`, `## MCP Tool Contract Principles`, and `## Phase 8: Workflow Engine V2` headings from the spec; reference `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md` from T02 for deprecation policy.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: every collapse decision is recorded; every shipped tool is listed; no \"to be added later\" placeholders for tool entries.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed and the T02 compatibility policy was cross-referenced.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4085,"cache_read_input_tokens":77188,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4085,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012n7S8LWZzY1cvitTHPzudV","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"1b19303a-2693-4a8c-9024-c6b34eb8d8d5","request_id":"req_011Cb7N83CrnmzCR4uLXc6tv","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 8+9+Gate task briefs"}
