{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01VnVHrBqUuRyoA3FBgpwZ83","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012qH4jVMW4V9DewbbrQE7KJ","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T76.md","content":"# T76 — Phase 10 — Consolidation queue + indexing health + workspace graph health views\n\n**Phase:** 10\n**Type:** frontend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T71\n**Spec anchor:** [§10. Human Review Surface](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#10-human-review-surface), [§6. Consolidation Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#6-consolidation-engine), [§2. Workspace Graph](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#2-workspace-graph)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); UI specification (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/ui-specification.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task delivers the three operations-focused subviews of the review panel: the consolidation queue (background and manual-review consolidation jobs with depth/state visibility), the indexing health view (ingestion pipeline state, parser failures, vector index freshness), and the workspace graph health view (node/edge counts per family, broken-link detection, stale-edge detection). These views are how operators answer \"is the daemon healthy and is its substrate trustworthy?\" — without them, only the daemon-side logs show whether consolidation is keeping up, whether parsing is failing silently, or whether the graph has degenerated. Spec §10 names all three explicitly; this task delivers the last three of the eleven required operator views, completing the Phase 10 view set before smoke tests (T77).\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Required operator views: ... usefulness metrics; workspace graph health; indexing health; consolidation queue.\" (spec §10)\n\n> \"Consolidation queue depth must be bounded; when the queue is full, new jobs are dropped with a log warning rather than stalling the daemon.\" (spec §6 — drives the queue-depth indicator and dropped-job count.)\n\n> \"The graph must support exact identity lookup, bounded neighborhood traversal, impact queries, doc/code backlinks, and freshness queries.\" (spec §2 — drives the freshness/staleness counters in the graph health view.)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: T71 (review panel scaffolding + RPC bridge + i18n catalog).\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `extension/src/review/reviewPanel.ts` — host the three subviews mount into.\n  - `extension/src/review/rpcBridge.ts` — typed methods this task consumes: `listConsolidationJobs({ status?, kind? })`, `getConsolidationQueueDepth()`, `getIndexingHealth()`, `getWorkspaceGraphHealth()`.\n  - `extension/src/review/components/StatusBadge.ts` (from T72) — reused for job-status badges (`queued`, `running`, `succeeded`, `failed`, `dropped`).\n- Standards files to honor: `coding.md`; `ui-specification.md` §6 (lists & tables, pagination), §8.2–8.5 (loading/empty/error), §11.1 (status badges), §14 (i18n).\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §6 Consolidation Engine (job types, modes, LLM-driven constraints, queue depth rule) and §2 Workspace Graph (node families, edge families, freshness queries) so the column sets are grounded in the spec.\n2. Create `extension/src/review/consolidationQueueView.ts` exporting `mountConsolidationQueueView(host, bridge, i18n)`. Render a sortable, paginated table with columns: `Status` badge, `Kind` (episode summary, procedure extraction, contradiction detection, failure-pattern extraction, duplicate detection, supersession proposal, etc. per spec §6), `Mode` (synchronous / background / manual-review / replay per spec §6 consolidation modes), `Created At`, `Started At`, `Completed At`, `Duration`, `LLM Model` (where applicable), `Result Summary`, `Actions` (Inspect, Retry).\n3. Above the table render a queue-depth indicator showing current depth vs the documented bound, plus a count of jobs `dropped` due to queue full (per spec §6 \"queue depth must be bounded\"). When the dropped count is non-zero, render a warning banner with the count and a link to the event trace view (T75) filtered to `MemoryConsolidated` and consolidation-failure events.\n4. Filter bar: `Status` (multi-select), `Kind` (multi-select), `Mode` (multi-select), all via `vscode.window.showQuickPick`.\n5. Create `extension/src/review/indexingHealthView.ts` exporting `mountIndexingHealthView(host, bridge, i18n)`. Render a panel layout with sections:\n   - Ingestion pipeline status: per-language parser status (count of files parsed, count failed, last error), watcher status, last full-rescan timestamp.\n   - Vector index health: total embeddings, last rebuild timestamp, average freshness, count of stale embeddings.\n   - FTS index health: row count per FTS table, last rebuild, count of orphan rows.\n   - Event log health: events ingested last hour / 24h / 7d, last compaction snapshot timestamp (per spec §Storage Design event-log compaction), event-payload-spillover row count.\n   - Each section ends with a refresh button that calls the relevant bridge method.\n6. Create `extension/src/review/workspaceGraphHealthView.ts` exporting `mountWorkspaceGraphHealthView(host, bridge, i18n)`. Render per-node-family counts and per-edge-family counts (all node and edge families from spec §2) in tables, plus three diagnostic panels: `Broken references` (edges pointing to non-existent identities), `Stale edges` (edges whose `stale_against` flag is set per spec §2 edge families), and `Orphan symbols` (symbols not referenced by any file). Each panel has a `Recompute` button that triggers a re-verification.\n7. Cross-link: clicking a failed consolidation job opens the event trace view (T75) filtered to the related task/session; clicking a broken-reference row opens the file or symbol via `vscode.commands.executeCommand('vscode.open', uri)`; clicking a stale-edge row opens the evidence inspector (T74) for the related memory if one exists.\n8. Add i18n keys under `consolidationQueueView`, `indexingHealthView`, and `workspaceGraphHealthView` namespaces: every column header, status/kind/mode label, panel title, action label, success/error string, loading hint, empty state.\n9. Wrap every bridge call in `try/catch` and surface failure both inline and via `vscode.window.showErrorMessage`.\n10. Run `cd extension && npm run compile && npm run lint` and fix every error/warning before stopping.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `extension/src/review/consolidationQueueView.ts` — `mountConsolidationQueueView` subview with sortable/paginated job table, queue-depth indicator, and dropped-job warning per spec §6.\n- `extension/src/review/indexingHealthView.ts` — `mountIndexingHealthView` panel covering parser, watcher, vector, FTS, and event-log indexing health.\n- `extension/src/review/workspaceGraphHealthView.ts` — `mountWorkspaceGraphHealthView` panel covering per-family counts and three diagnostic panels (broken refs, stale edges, orphan symbols).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f extension/src/review/consolidationQueueView.ts` — confirms the consolidation queue file exists at the path the harness expects.\n- `test -f extension/src/review/indexingHealthView.ts` — confirms the indexing health file exists at the path the harness expects.\n- `test -f extension/src/review/workspaceGraphHealthView.ts` — confirms the graph health file exists at the path the harness expects.\n- `cd extension && npm run compile` — TypeScript compile succeeds with no errors.\n- `cd extension && npm run lint` — lint passes with zero warnings introduced by this task.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file. If a view grows beyond, split per panel.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. Panel renderers are table-driven over the documented node/edge/job-kind sets.\n- Single source of truth: job-status badge from T72; node/edge family enumerations live in one place referenced by both the daemon contract and the i18n catalog.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `// eslint-disable`.\n- No silent error handling — every bridge call surfaces failure inline + via `vscode.window.showErrorMessage`.\n- Doc citation: comments cite `## 6. Consolidation Engine` for the queue-depth and dropped-job rule and `## 2. Workspace Graph` for the node/edge family set (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Markdown Heading References).\n\n### UI specification\n\n- All user-facing strings via `i18n.t(...)` from the three namespaces; no inline literals in any of the three files.\n- All modals via native `<dialog>` — these views are mostly panels; the \"Retry job\" confirmation uses a native `<dialog>` or routes through `vscode.window.showInformationMessage` with explicit actions. Never `window.confirm/prompt/alert`.\n- All mutation handlers (Retry, Recompute, refresh) use `try/catch` with `vscode.window.showErrorMessage(err.message)` (`parseApiError + toast.error` is the Cadres web equivalent; for VS Code, the analogue is the error toast).\n- All ID inputs use `SearchableSelect` (webview) or `vscode.window.showQuickPick` (tree-view) — every filter picker uses `showQuickPick`. Never raw `<select>` or `prompt`-based ID entry.\n- Sortable tables use `SortableHeader` + `useTableSort` equivalents on the consolidation queue (sortable on `Status`, `Kind`, `Mode`, `Created At`, `Duration`), per-family counts in graph health (sortable on `Family`, `Count`), and broken-refs / stale-edges / orphan-symbols panels (sortable on `Identity`, `Reason`). Pagination required on every list per `ui-specification.md` §6.1.\n- Status badges + loading + empty + error states for every interactive surface: badges for every job status; loading skeleton on first load and per-section spinner on refresh; distinct empty states for healthy (\"No queued consolidation jobs.\", \"Indexing pipeline is up to date.\", \"No broken references.\") vs filtered (\"No jobs match the current filters.\"); warning banner when queue-depth bound is hit; error banner inline + VS Code toast on failure.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] UI specification checks satisfied: queue-depth indicator with bound + dropped-job warning per spec §6; per-family counts for all spec §2 node/edge families; cross-navigation to T74/T75 wired through router.\n- [ ] No deferred work: all three views ship in this task; the smoke tests (T77) are a sibling task, not a deferral.\n- [ ] After build, deploy per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy procedure.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6111,"cache_read_input_tokens":77427,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6111,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XjrTa6YAS1dmMW989ZPauZ","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"ce79354a-531c-4b01-8c01-6c9da95c863f","request_id":"req_011Cb7MqWKneiRTEnKhFBPcy","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 10+11+Final task briefs"}
