{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"a163eb6f432e922f5","tool_use_id":"toolu_015qAoQeXM7HFtFDzBbPkUNq","description":"Writing docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T46.md","subagent_type":"general-purpose","usage":{"total_tokens":73207,"tool_uses":27,"duration_ms":439002},"last_tool_name":"Write","uuid":"39a746d5-59b9-486a-a012-17b6d91bacac","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01KfbHujQgTf2xL6BHMDNHxQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019RpBFBk2AigV9E6iHbtaHU","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T46.md","content":"# T46 — Phase 6 — Consolidation tests (proposals, apply/reject, replay, queue bounds, failure events)\n\n**Phase:** 6\n**Type:** tests\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T39, T40, T41, T42, T43, T44, T45\n**Spec anchor:** [§Consolidation Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#6-consolidation-engine), [§Phase 6: Consolidation Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-6-consolidation-engine), [§Testing Requirements](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#testing-requirements)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task ships the cross-job integration test suite that proves Phase 6's invariants hold when all consolidation pieces run together: proposals from every job type land in `consolidation_proposals` without silent writes, apply/reject decisions route through the runtime correctly, replay reconstructs the same memory state, the bounded queue drops with warnings on overflow, malformed LLM responses emit `ConsolidationFailed` events while leaving prior memory unchanged, and high-scope proposals reach the manual-review queue instead of auto-applying. Unit tests in T39–T45 cover each module in isolation; this task wires them end-to-end so the spec's Phase 6 DoD (\"consolidation is auditable, reversible, and test-covered\") is demonstrably met.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> Phase 6 DoD: \"completed tasks produce useful episode memories; repeated successful traces produce procedural memories; consolidation is auditable, reversible, and test-covered.\"\n\n> \"every background consolidation pass is recoverable, replayable, and observable.\"\n\n> \"failed or malformed LLM responses must leave the prior memory state unchanged and emit a consolidation failure event\"\n\n> \"consolidation queue depth must be bounded; when the queue is full, new jobs are dropped with a log warning rather than stalling the daemon\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: T39 (runtime + schema), T40 (synchronous session), T41 (deterministic scanners), T42 (LLM jobs), T43 (provenance + budgets + per-kind queue), T44 (manual-review queue), T45 (replay + reversal).\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/` — the full module shipped by T39–T45.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/` — event reader and writer for assertions on emitted events.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/` — store API used to assert no-silent-write invariants.\n  - Test fixtures from Phase 2 + Phase 3 (seeded workspaces, events, memories).\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Tests as documentation (one test per behavior, named for the behavior), §Hard limits (test length ≤30 lines, factor setup into fixtures); Lattice rules on doc-heading citation.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Phase 6 DoD and §Testing Requirements. Copy the four invariants this suite must demonstrate into the top-of-file doc comment on `integration_tests.rs`.\n2. Build a `ConsolidationHarness` helper at the top of `integration_tests.rs` (or a sibling `integration_test_support.rs` if it grows): seeds a temp SQLite store with the Phase 2/3/6 schemas, registers a fake `LlmDriver` whose responses are scripted per test, wires the T39 runtime, T44 review queue, and T45 replay driver. Tests reuse the harness so each individual test stays ≤30 lines.\n3. Write `test_synchronous_session_consolidation_emits_proposal_not_silent_write` (covers T40 + T39): run a small task slice through `SessionConsolidator::on_task_complete`, assert a `CreateMemory` proposal exists in `consolidation_proposals` with status `pending`, assert the memory store still has zero `EpisodeMemory` rows for that task, then apply the proposal and assert the memory appears AND a `MemoryConsolidated` event is in the event log.\n4. Write `test_deterministic_supersession_proposal_apply_then_reject_round_trip` (covers T41): seed two overlapping memories, run `SupersessionCandidates::scan`, assert one `Supersede` proposal is pending, apply it, assert the older memory's status is `superseded` AND a `memory_links` edge points to the newer, then call `ReplayDriver::reverse(proposal_id)` and assert the status flips back and the link is gone.\n5. Write `test_llm_episode_job_well_formed_response_emits_proposal_with_provenance` (covers T42 + T43): script the fake driver to return a well-formed JSON episode summary, run `EpisodeSummaryJob::run` in `Background` mode, assert a proposal exists with `provenance.is_some()`, `provenance.model == \"fake-llm\"`, and matching `prompt_sha256` / `response_sha256`.\n6. Write `test_llm_malformed_response_leaves_memory_unchanged_and_emits_failure_event` (covers T42 malformed-handling): script the driver to return invalid JSON, assert zero proposals enqueued, zero memory mutations, and exactly one `ConsolidationFailed` event with `error_kind = MalformedResponse`.\n7. Write `test_llm_synchronous_mode_is_forbidden_and_driver_never_called` (covers T42 mode guard): attempt `EpisodeSummaryJob::run(ctx { mode: SynchronousPostTask }, …)`, assert it returns `Err(ForbiddenOnHotPath)`, assert the fake driver's call count is zero.\n8. Write `test_bounded_queue_overflow_drops_jobs_with_warning_event` (covers T39 + T43): set `max_depth = 2`, enqueue 5 jobs of the same LLM kind, assert exactly 3 are dropped, exactly 3 `ConsolidationFailed` events with `error_kind = QueueFull` are emitted, and the `tracing::warn!` log surfaced (capture via a tracing-test subscriber).\n9. Write `test_high_scope_proposal_routes_to_manual_review_queue` (covers T44): seed a `repo`-scope target memory, run a job that produces a proposal for it, assert the proposal is `pending` and visible via `ReviewQueue::list_pending(scope=Repo)`, assert it did NOT auto-apply.\n10. Write `test_replay_from_genesis_reconstructs_memory_state` (covers T45): apply 10 mixed proposals through the runtime, snapshot the memory store hash, reset the memory tables, run `ReplayDriver::replay(FromGenesis)` with the provenance cache, assert the post-replay memory hash equals the snapshot hash AND the live LLM driver was never called.\n11. Wire the suite via `mod integration_tests;` in `consolidation/mod.rs` under `#[cfg(test)]` (or a `tests/` sibling per crate convention — match `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/tests.rs` style).\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/integration_tests.rs` — `ConsolidationHarness` plus the named behavior-per-test functions above covering synchronous, deterministic, LLM well-formed, LLM malformed, mode guard, queue overflow, manual-review routing, and replay reconstruction.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/integration_tests.rs` — confirms the integration test file exists.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib consolidation::integration_tests` — every Phase 6 integration test passes.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file (split harness into `integration_test_support.rs` if approaching the ceiling).\n- Test length ≤30 lines per `#[test]` function; setup factored into the harness.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10 for harness helpers.\n- Single source of truth: tests exercise the real T39–T45 modules via their public APIs; no shadow re-implementation of proposal storage or event emission.\n- Naming: tests follow `test_<behavior_description>` per `coding.md` §Tests as documentation (e.g. `test_llm_malformed_response_leaves_memory_unchanged_and_emits_failure_event`).\n- Error handling: tests assert on typed outcomes (`EnqueueOutcome::Dropped`, `LlmJobError::ForbiddenOnHotPath`) rather than message strings.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Observability: tests capture `tracing::warn!` output via a test subscriber so warn-on-drop is verifiable, not just assumed.\n- Doc citation: file-top doc comment cites the four spec invariants verbatim (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` § Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] `integration_tests.rs` exists with every test from steps 3–10 implemented.\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied (in particular, no individual test exceeds 30 lines).\n- [ ] No deferred work: all four Phase 6 invariants are covered end-to-end in this task; no \"leave for later\" placeholders.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed and the architecture doc was updated in the same task.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15541,"cache_read_input_tokens":56911,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":15541,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015qAoQeXM7HFtFDzBbPkUNq","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"abe467b8-23c3-46c2-8c75-07c0acef06a4","request_id":"req_011Cb7N1yvFZe4LypqRsfPgL","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 6+7+Gate task briefs"}
