{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01VnVHrBqUuRyoA3FBgpwZ83","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LASHxdn2rDrzNDCixBNPTb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T77.md","content":"# T77 — Phase 10 — Extension UI smoke tests (compile + lint + integration runner)\n\n**Phase:** 10\n**Type:** tests\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T71, T72, T73, T74, T75, T76\n**Spec anchor:** [§10. Human Review Surface](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#10-human-review-surface), [§Testing Requirements](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#testing-requirements)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); UI specification (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/ui-specification.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task delivers the VS Code integration smoke tests that prove the Phase 10 review surface activates cleanly inside a real VS Code instance, the review panel registers, and each of the six subviews (memory inbox, promotion queue, contradiction queue, stale view, evidence inspector, event trace, retrieval explanation, consolidation queue, indexing health, workspace graph health) mounts and renders without throwing. Spec §Testing Requirements lists \"extension compile/UI smoke tests\" as a required test family; this task makes that test family green for the Phase 10 deliverables. Without it, regressions in webview wiring would land unnoticed because compile + lint cannot catch runtime mount failures.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Required test families: ... extension compile/UI smoke tests.\" (spec §Testing Requirements)\n\n> \"Definition of done: operators can understand and correct durable memory without reading raw SQLite rows.\" (spec §Phase 10 — the smoke tests must confirm every subview the operator depends on actually renders.)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: T71 (panel scaffolding), T72 (memory inbox), T73 (promotion + contradiction queues), T74 (stale + evidence views), T75 (event trace + retrieval explanation), T76 (consolidation + indexing + graph health) — every subview the smoke tests assert renders.\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `extension/package.json` — existing `npm test` script wired to `node ./out/test/runTest.js` (the VS Code test runner pattern documented in `context.md` §\"Tests\").\n  - `extension/src/extension.ts` — activation function under test.\n  - `extension/src/test/` — existing test scaffolding directory (extended here, not replaced).\n- Standards files to honor: `coding.md` (tests as documentation §Tests, one test per behavior, integration tests prefer real collaborators); `ui-specification.md` §16 (`data-testid` on every interactive element — tests assert against these).\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read `extension/package.json` to confirm the test script `npm test` maps to `node ./out/test/runTest.js`. If the runner entry point does not exist, this task is responsible for creating it.\n2. Create `extension/src/test/runTest.ts` exporting the standard VS Code `@vscode/test-electron` runner entry. It downloads VS Code if needed, launches it with the extension under test loaded, runs the Mocha suite from `extension/src/test/suite/index.ts` (or equivalent index file), and exits with the suite's pass/fail code.\n3. If `extension/src/test/suite/index.ts` does not yet exist (check `extension/src/test/`), add a minimal Mocha entry that registers `review.test.ts` and any pre-existing tests so this task does not regress prior coverage.\n4. Create `extension/src/test/review.test.ts` covering:\n   - **Activation**: `vscode.extensions.getExtension('lattice.lattice')!.activate()` returns successfully; `vscode.commands.getCommands(true)` includes `lattice.openReviewPanel`.\n   - **View registration**: After activation, `vscode.window.registerWebviewViewProvider` has been called for `lattice.reviewPanel` (assert by attempting `vscode.commands.executeCommand('lattice.reviewPanel.focus')` and observing no error).\n   - **Subview render: memory inbox**: Open the review panel, route to the inbox subview, assert the webview HTML contains the inbox container element (queried by `data-testid=\"review-memory-inbox\"` per `ui-specification.md` §16) without throwing.\n   - **Subview render: promotion queue**: Route to the promotion queue, assert `data-testid=\"review-promotion-queue\"` is present.\n   - **Subview render: contradiction queue**: Assert `data-testid=\"review-contradiction-queue\"` is present.\n   - **Subview render: stale view**: Assert `data-testid=\"review-stale-view\"` is present.\n   - **Subview render: evidence inspector**: Open with a mock memory id, assert `data-testid=\"review-evidence-inspector\"` is present.\n   - **Subview render: event trace**: Assert `data-testid=\"review-event-trace\"` is present.\n   - **Subview render: retrieval explanation**: Open with a mock request id, assert `data-testid=\"review-retrieval-explanation\"` is present.\n   - **Subview render: consolidation queue**: Assert `data-testid=\"review-consolidation-queue\"` is present.\n   - **Subview render: indexing health**: Assert `data-testid=\"review-indexing-health\"` is present.\n   - **Subview render: workspace graph health**: Assert `data-testid=\"review-workspace-graph-health\"` is present.\n   - **No throw on missing data**: For every subview, with the RPC bridge stubbed to return an empty array, assert the subview mounts and renders the documented empty-state string (per `ui-specification.md` §8.3) without throwing.\n   - **No throw on bridge error**: For every subview, with the RPC bridge stubbed to reject, assert the subview mounts and renders the error banner without throwing, and that `vscode.window.showErrorMessage` was called (mock or spy).\n5. Use a thin stub of `ReviewRpcBridge` injected via a test-only export from `extension/src/review/reviewPanel.ts` (add a `setBridgeForTests` hook if not already present from T71). Do not mock VS Code's API — use the real `@vscode/test-electron` runner.\n6. Run the suite locally with `cd extension && npm install && npm run compile && npm test`. Resolve every failure before stopping. Capture the suite output and confirm every named test above runs and passes.\n7. Confirm `cd extension && npm run lint` passes with zero new warnings introduced by the test files (lint must include the `src/test` directory).\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `extension/src/test/review.test.ts` — Mocha test file with the smoke coverage enumerated above: activation, view registration, every subview renders, every subview renders cleanly under empty data, every subview renders cleanly under bridge error.\n- `extension/src/test/runTest.ts` — `@vscode/test-electron` runner entry that `npm test` invokes per `extension/package.json`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f extension/src/test/review.test.ts` — confirms the smoke test file exists at the path the harness expects.\n- `test -f extension/src/test/runTest.ts` — confirms the runner entry exists at the path the harness expects.\n- `cd extension && npm run compile` — TypeScript compile succeeds with no errors.\n- `cd extension && npm run lint` — lint passes with zero warnings introduced by this task.\n- `cd extension && npm test` — the VS Code test runner launches, the activation test passes, the view-registration test passes, every subview-render test passes, every empty-data test passes, and every bridge-error test passes.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file.\n- Function length ≤50 lines (each `it(...)` block ≤30 lines per `coding.md` §Hard limits \"Test length\"). Setup factored into beforeEach helpers.\n- One test per behavior, named for the behavior (e.g. `it('mounts the memory inbox without throwing')`), per `coding.md` §Tests as documentation.\n- Integration tests prefer real collaborators — use the real `@vscode/test-electron` runner; mock only the RPC bridge (the process boundary to the daemon).\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `// eslint-disable`.\n- No silent error handling — every `await` either propagates to Mocha's failure path or is wrapped in `try/catch` with an explicit assertion.\n- Doc citation: test comments cite `## Testing Requirements` for the smoke-test family requirement and `## 10. Human Review Surface` for the subview catalog (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] Every subview from T72–T76 has a corresponding \"renders without throwing\" test; every subview has an empty-data test; every subview has a bridge-error test.\n- [ ] `data-testid` attributes referenced by tests exist in the rendered HTML — if they were missing, this task adds them in the same change (no broken windows).\n- [ ] No deferred work: the smoke tests cover every subview registered by T71–T76; deeper interaction tests for accept/reject flows are covered by R79 (contract gate), not deferred to a later session.\n- [ ] After build, deploy per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy procedure.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6111,"cache_read_input_tokens":77427,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6111,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XjrTa6YAS1dmMW989ZPauZ","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"cde47ea5-ed6d-45dc-af76-028da4a4612e","request_id":"req_011Cb7MqWKneiRTEnKhFBPcy","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 10+11+Final task briefs"}
