{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01CUNuwJWz1kjG5DewB82nne","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HJwwSUNMEg7MoxjMkEhEQy","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T35.md","content":"# T35 — Phase 5 — Working memory operations (retrieve, summarize, filter, pin, evict, expand, compress, checkpoint)\n\n**Phase:** 5\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T34\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 5: Working Memory](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-5-working-memory), [§5. Working Memory](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#5-working-memory)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task implements every required operation on `WorkingMemoryState` from spec §5: `retrieve`, `summarize`, `filter`, `pin`, `evict`, `expand`, `compress`, `checkpoint`. Each operation mutates state in a documented, auditable way and pairs with a contract: every operation that drops or skips a memory must record the result in `excluded_memories` with a reason so the working-memory inspector (T36) can show what was intentionally left out. The operations integrate with Phase 4 retrieval (`retrieve` calls into the Phase 4 pipeline, `compress` invokes the shaper's compression policy, `pin` supplies the pin set the shaper honors).\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Required operations: retrieve; summarize; filter; pin; evict; expand; compress; checkpoint. Working memory is not durable by itself. Durable value is extracted through event-backed consolidation.\" (spec §5. Working Memory)\n\n> \"Phase 5: Working Memory — Deliverables: ... operations for retrieve, summarize, filter, pin, evict, expand, compress, and checkpoint ...\" (spec §Phase 5: Working Memory)\n\n> \"Definition of done: workflow tools can show what context is active, why it is active, and what was intentionally excluded; context management is no longer just prompt accumulation.\" (spec §Phase 5: Working Memory)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs:\n  - T34 `WorkingMemoryState`, `ExcludedMemory`, `BudgetDecisions`, checkpoint save/load.\n  - T31 `RetrievalBundle` and `ShaperContext.pins` interface — `pin` and `compress` route through the shaper to keep behaviour consistent with Phase 4.\n  - T30 `RankedCandidate` (for `expand`, which re-runs scoring against a wider candidate set).\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/retrieval_v1/shaper.rs` and `scoring.rs` — invoked by `retrieve`, `compress`, `expand`.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/state.rs` (T34) — every operation takes `&mut WorkingMemoryState`.\n- Standards files to honor: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` (single source of truth — no parallel ranker or shaper in this module); `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Re-read spec §5. Working Memory \"Required operations\" list and §Phase 5 Definition of Done to fix the contract for each operation.\n2. Define an `Operation` trait or `WorkingMemoryOp` enum in `operations.rs` documenting the eight operations with one match arm per operation, so adding a ninth requires a deliberate type-system change.\n3. Implement each operation as a free function `pub fn <op>(state: &mut WorkingMemoryState, args: <Op>Args, ctx: &OpContext) -> Result<<Op>Outcome>`, ≤50 lines each:\n   - `retrieve(state, args, ctx)`: invokes the Phase 4 pipeline (intent → anchors → candidates → scoring → shaper) and merges the returned `RetrievalBundle` into `state.selected_memories`; every dropped candidate during shaper compression is captured in `state.excluded_memories` with its exclusion reason.\n   - `summarize(state, args, ctx)`: returns a compact `WorkingMemorySummary` view (task, intent label, active file count, selected/excluded counts, budget usage, top hypotheses) for MCP display and event capture.\n   - `filter(state, predicate, ctx)`: removes selected memories that fail `predicate`; removed entries move to `excluded_memories` with reason `\"filtered: <predicate description>\"`.\n   - `pin(state, identities, ctx)`: adds identities to `state.budget_decisions.pinned_identities`; documented contract is that subsequent `compress` and shaper-driven trimming must not drop pinned identities.\n   - `evict(state, identities, ctx)`: removes identities from `selected_memories`, records each in `excluded_memories` with reason `\"evicted: <caller reason>\"`; refuses to evict pinned identities unless `force=true`.\n   - `expand(state, target, ctx)`: re-runs Phase 4 scoring against a widened candidate set centred on `target` (a `BundleResult` already in `selected_memories`) using its `expansion_handle`; new high-ranked candidates are appended to `selected_memories`.\n   - `compress(state, budget, ctx)`: reuses the shaper's compression policy on `state.selected_memories`, honoring `pinned_identities`; dropped results move to `excluded_memories` with reason `\"compressed: budget=<n> tokens\"`.\n   - `checkpoint(state, name, ctx)`: calls `state::save_checkpoint(state, name, conn)` and returns the `CheckpointId`.\n4. Make every operation idempotent where the spec implies it: calling `pin` twice on the same identity is a no-op; `evict` on an absent identity returns `Ok` with a documented no-op outcome; `checkpoint` with the same name versions the entry, never silently overwrites.\n5. Wire `OpContext` so it carries the SQLite connection, retrieval profile, identity resolver, and shaper handle once — operations never construct these themselves.\n6. Surface every state mutation through a single internal helper `record_state_mutation(state, op_name, before_hash, after_hash, summary)` so T36's event capture has a single hook to wire `MemoryRetrieved` / `MemoryExpanded` events into.\n7. Add `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/operations_tests.rs` covering: each of the eight operations is exercised; `retrieve` populates both `selected_memories` and `excluded_memories`; `pin` then `compress` proves pinned identities survive; `evict` of a pinned identity without `force` is refused; `filter` records the predicate description; `summarize` returns a non-empty view with the expected fields; `expand` increases the selected-memories count when the candidate pool widens; `checkpoint` returns an id whose `load_checkpoint` byte-matches the state.\n8. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release` and the verification test command; fix any clippy warnings before stopping.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/operations.rs` — eight operations, `OpContext`, internal state-mutation hook.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/operations_tests.rs` — in-tree tests for every operation, pin/evict interaction, summarize, expand, checkpoint round-trip.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/operations.rs`\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib working_memory::operations_tests`\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file. If `operations.rs` approaches the cap, split per-operation modules under `operations/` along operation boundaries.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. Each operation is its own function; the internal mutation hook is shared.\n- Schema parity: any state mutation that needs persistence (only `checkpoint`) goes through T34's `save_checkpoint`; no parallel write path.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Single source of truth: retrieval calls Phase 4 (`retrieval_v1::shaper`, `scoring`); no parallel candidate or scoring code here.\n- No broken windows: dead imports removed, every operation name expresses intent; every drop/skip path writes to `excluded_memories` with a reason.\n- Doc citation: each operation doc comment cites `## 5. Working Memory` per `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: all eight operations implemented; pin/evict/compress interaction enforced; `excluded_memories` populated by every drop/skip path.\n- [ ] Idempotency contracts (pin, evict, checkpoint name versioning) covered by tests.\n- [ ] `record_state_mutation` hook is in place ready for T36 to attach `MemoryRetrieved` / `MemoryExpanded` event emission.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3830,"cache_read_input_tokens":70953,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3830,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"unavailable"}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019RjXwCuf57BAKn88mWkE24","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"1289a950-d62a-4c61-a120-dc64f1b358a7","request_id":"req_011Cb7NEF3AvDWxJijCpc5mc","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 4+5 task briefs"}
