{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01T8NoMY658whtcPyMrX3ZgZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017g8VBmCo7KYVQeAcEafCcT","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R47.md","content":"# R47 — Backend review — Phase 6 consolidation engine\n\n**Phase:** 6\n**Type:** review\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** T39, T40, T41, T42, T43, T44, T45, T46\n**Spec anchor:** [§Consolidation Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#6-consolidation-engine), [§Phase 6: Consolidation Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-6-consolidation-engine), [§Non-Negotiable Product Properties](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#non-negotiable-product-properties)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task is the Phase 6 backend review. It audits T39–T46 against the spec's consolidation contract, the §Non-Negotiable Product Properties bullets that consolidation directly touches (replayability, observability, no silent broad mutation), and the coding standard. The review must produce a verdict on whether Phase 6 is ready to ship and gate Phase 7 (T48 verification engine begins under R47). It records concrete evidence — file paths, function names, test names, log lines — for every claim. A pass/fail decision without cited evidence is not a review.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> Phase 6 DoD: \"completed tasks produce useful episode memories; repeated successful traces produce procedural memories; consolidation is auditable, reversible, and test-covered.\"\n\n> \"No consolidation job may silently rewrite high-scope memory without preserving provenance and prior state.\"\n\n> \"LLM-driven jobs run only in background or manual review modes, never on the synchronous post-task hot path.\"\n\n> \"consolidation queue depth must be bounded; when the queue is full, new jobs are dropped with a log warning rather than stalling the daemon\"\n\n> \"cost and latency budgets for LLM consolidation should be documented per job type before Phase 6 begins\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: T39 (runtime + proposal model), T40 (synchronous session), T41 (deterministic scanners), T42 (LLM jobs), T43 (provenance + budgets + per-kind queue), T44 (manual-review queue), T46 (integration tests). T45 (replay) is also in scope of this review.\n- Existing repo files this task reviews:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/` (all files)\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-llm-budgets.md` (T43 budget doc)\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/` (`MemoryConsolidated`, `ConsolidationFailed` payloads)\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Done means done; Lattice rules on Markdown heading references; spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Run the full Phase 6 test suite from the repo root: `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib consolidation` and capture the count of passing / failing tests per submodule.\n2. Audit `T39.proposal_tests`, `T40.session_tests`, `T41.deterministic_tests`, `T42.llm_tests`, `T43.provenance_tests`, `T44.review_queue_tests`, `T45.replay_tests`, `T46.integration_tests` for behavior coverage; list any spec bullet not exercised by at least one test.\n3. Audit `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/*` for the proposal-only invariant: grep for any direct memory-store write outside `ConsolidationProposal::apply` and `ReplayDriver::reverse`; any hit is a finding.\n4. Verify the hot-path forbid: confirm `LlmJobContext` checks `mode != SynchronousPostTask` in every LLM job's `run` entry point AND that the runtime's dispatch layer enforces the same (defense in depth per T42 step 8).\n5. Verify queue-bound behavior end-to-end: enqueue overflow test exists and exercises both the per-LLM-kind sub-quota (T43) and the top-level cap (T39); both paths emit `tracing::warn!` AND a `ConsolidationFailed` event.\n6. Read `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-llm-budgets.md` and verify: (a) per-job-kind budgets table is present with all four LLM job kinds, (b) fallback behavior is documented per kind, (c) provenance record format matches T43's `LlmProvenance` struct exactly, (d) the spec citation links `## 6. Consolidation Engine` \"LLM-driven consolidation\".\n7. Audit coding-standard adherence across the consolidation module: file lengths via `wc -l`, function-length sampling (any function visibly over 50 lines), nesting depth on `BoundedJobQueue::enqueue`, `ConsolidationProposal::apply`, every `Job::run`. Record exceptions and whether they carry the one-line justification per `coding.md` §Hard limits.\n8. Write the review at `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R47-consolidation.md` with the mandatory headings: `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Proposal discipline`, `## LLM budget evidence`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`. Each section cites concrete evidence (file paths, line ranges, test names, log lines). The `## Verdict` heading states `pass` or `fail` with a one-paragraph justification. Failures list a minimum-fix patch path so a follow-up task can address them.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R47-consolidation.md` — Phase 6 backend review with all six mandatory headings, concrete evidence per section, and a pass/fail verdict.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R47-consolidation.md` — confirms the review file exists.\n- `grep -q '## Spec alignment' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R47-consolidation.md` — `## Spec alignment` heading present.\n- `grep -q '## Proposal discipline' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R47-consolidation.md` — `## Proposal discipline` heading present.\n- `grep -q '## LLM budget evidence' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R47-consolidation.md` — `## LLM budget evidence` heading present.\n- `grep -q '## Verdict' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R47-consolidation.md` — `## Verdict` heading present.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines (review doc unlikely to approach the ceiling; `wc -l` it anyway).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10 — not applicable (review doc).\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code.\n- No unjustified suppressions.\n- Public API naming — not applicable (review doc).\n- Doc citation: every claim cites either a code path (`daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/...`) or a spec heading; vague phrases like \"looks good\" are not evidence.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R47-consolidation.md` exists with all six mandatory headings.\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: every spec bullet under §Consolidation Engine, §Phase 6, and the consolidation-touching §Non-Negotiable Product Properties bullets is addressed in `## Spec alignment` or the verdict explicitly notes it is out of Phase 6 scope (and cites the phase that owns it).\n- [ ] If the verdict is `fail`, the findings section lists the minimum-fix tasks needed before Phase 7 can begin.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14824,"cache_read_input_tokens":72452,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":14824,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015qAoQeXM7HFtFDzBbPkUNq","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"bb9c632f-d4b6-42ac-b363-db85008f9fc1","request_id":"req_011Cb7NFLFEWqZ2jGvDUmCkH","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 6+7+Gate task briefs"}
