{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01T8NoMY658whtcPyMrX3ZgZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UrXaz57g9Ljqrs1JY4WUUp","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T48.md","content":"# T48 — Phase 7 — Verification engine core (file/symbol/doc/test existence checks)\n\n**Phase:** 7\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** R47\n**Spec anchor:** [§Verification Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#8-verification-engine), [§Phase 7: Verification And Freshness](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-7-verification-and-freshness), [§Storage Design](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#storage-design)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task lands the Phase 7 verification engine's core: the existence checks for files, symbols, docs, and tests that every durable memory's evidence cites. It introduces the `verification_jobs` table from spec §Storage Design, the eight-state verification output model (`verified` / `unverified` / `in_review` / `stale` / `contradicted` / `superseded` / `expired` / `invalidated`), and the basic verifier entrypoints that downstream Phase 7 tasks (T49 spans, T50 scope, T51 incremental + expiry, T52 surfacing) layer onto. Without this core, the spec's §Stale Memory Leakage risk control has no mechanism — and memory cannot be safely surfaced as trusted guidance.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Verification checks: linked files still exist; linked symbols still exist; cited docs still exist; linked tests still exist; evidence text still matches when exact spans were captured; implementation still matches memory claim where deterministic checks are possible; contradicted/superseded states remain coherent; branch-scoped memory is not leaking into unrelated branches; time-bound memory has expired.\"\n\n> \"Verification outputs: `verified`; `unverified`; `in_review`; `stale`; `contradicted`; `superseded`; `expired`; `invalidated`.\"\n\n> \"Verification must be incremental and tied to workspace changes. Large repos cannot tolerate full rescans for every memory.\"\n\n> Core tables include `verification_jobs` (§Storage Design).\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: R47 — Phase 6 consolidation review must pass before verification work begins so consolidation's `MarkStale` proposals (T41) and the verifier share a coherent contract on what `stale` means.\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/` — `MemoryEvidence` from Phase 3 (`memory_evidence` table) is the input the verifier walks.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/` — `FileId`, `SymbolId`, `DocSectionId`, `TestId`; existence checks resolve evidence references through these.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/graph/` — graph snapshot API; the verifier asks the graph whether a referenced identity still resolves to a live node.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` — SQLite migration runner; `verification_jobs` table created here.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/proposal.rs` — the verifier emits `MarkStale` proposals through the T39 runtime, not direct writes.\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Hard limits, §Single source of truth, §Error handling, §Schema / model parity, §Observability; Lattice rules on doc-heading citation; spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties on stale-surfacing.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Verification Engine in full and §Phase 7 DoD. Copy the verification-checks list and the eight verification-output states into the top-of-file doc comment on `verification/mod.rs`.\n2. Add `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/mod.rs` re-exporting `existence`, `VerificationStatus`, `VerificationVerdict`, `VerifierCore`. Module doc comment cites `## 8. Verification Engine` and `## Storage Design`.\n3. Define `pub enum VerificationStatus { Verified, Unverified, InReview, Stale, Contradicted, Superseded, Expired, Invalidated }` in `verification/mod.rs`, mirroring spec verbatim. Derive serde + display so the SQLite column and the MCP tool surface both serialize the same wire names.\n4. Author `verification/schema.sql` defining the `verification_jobs` table (columns: `job_id PK`, `workspace_id`, `target_memory_id`, `check_kind`, `status` ∈ {`queued`, `running`, `completed`, `failed`}, `verdict` ∈ `VerificationStatus`, `reason TEXT`, `queued_at`, `started_at`, `finished_at`, indexes on `(workspace_id, status)` and `(target_memory_id, finished_at)`).\n5. In `verification/existence.rs`, implement `FileExistenceCheck`, `SymbolExistenceCheck`, `DocSectionExistenceCheck`, `TestExistenceCheck`. Each consumes a `MemoryEvidence` reference and the current graph snapshot, returns a `VerificationVerdict { status, reason: String }`. `Verified` when the identity resolves; `Invalidated` (file/symbol deletion) or `Stale` (graph snapshot is older than the evidence's anchor timestamp) otherwise. Test evidence resolves through the existing test-id index from Phase 1.\n6. Implement `VerifierCore::verify_memory(memory_id)`: load the memory's evidence rows, dispatch each to the matching existence check, aggregate verdicts (any `Invalidated` → memory status `invalidated`; any `Stale` and no `Invalidated` → `stale`; all `Verified` → `verified`). Persist the result by emitting a `MarkStale` / `MarkInvalidated` / `MarkVerified` proposal through the T39 runtime — never direct writes.\n7. Wire `mod verification;` into `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/lib.rs` (alphabetical) and register `verification/schema.sql` in the storage migration runner. Add `MarkVerified` and `MarkInvalidated` variants to `ProposalKind` if not already defined; migration covers the enum extension.\n8. Expose `VerifierCore::run_pending_jobs(workspace_id, budget: VerifierBudget)` so the daemon scheduler can drive the verifier under a per-call work budget (e.g. max N memories per call). Return a `VerifierReport { verified, stale, invalidated, expired, elapsed }` for observability.\n9. In `verification/existence_tests.rs`, write tests that: (a) a memory whose evidence cites a live file is `Verified`, (b) deleting the file makes the next verify return `Invalidated` (assert via a proposal emitted through T39, not via a direct memory mutation), (c) a memory whose evidence cites a deleted symbol returns `Invalidated`, (d) a memory whose evidence cites a still-existing doc section returns `Verified`, (e) a memory whose evidence cites a deleted test returns `Invalidated`, (f) the `verification_jobs` schema round-trips under the migration runner against a temp DB.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/mod.rs` — module root; exports `VerificationStatus`, `VerificationVerdict`, `VerifierCore`; doc comment cites spec §Verification Engine and §Storage Design.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/existence.rs` — per-anchor existence checks (file / symbol / doc-section / test) plus `VerifierCore::verify_memory`.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/schema.sql` — `verification_jobs` table.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/existence_tests.rs` — per-anchor existence verdicts, proposal emission through T39, migration round-trip.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/mod.rs` — confirms the module root exists.\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/existence.rs` — confirms the existence-check module exists.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib verification::existence_tests` — every existence-check unit test passes.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. `VerifierCore::verify_memory` is a dispatch loop — keep helpers small and named.\n- Single source of truth: status writes route through T39 proposals; do not introduce a parallel memory-mutation path. Existence resolution goes through the graph snapshot API, not ad-hoc filesystem scans.\n- Error handling: typed `VerificationError` (storage failure, missing memory, missing graph snapshot). No bare `unwrap`. Per-evidence failures emit a `tracing::warn!` and continue verifying the rest of the memory's evidence — never abort a whole job.\n- Naming: `VerifierCore::verify_memory`, `FileExistenceCheck`, `VerificationVerdict`. No `Manager`/`Helper` suffixes.\n- Schema parity: `VerificationStatus` matches the spec list verbatim; SQLite column uses the same string names.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Observability: every `verify_memory` call emits a `tracing::info_span!(\"verify_memory\", memory_id, evidence_count, verdict)`; aggregate runs emit `tracing::info!` with `VerifierReport` totals.\n- Doc citation: file-top comments cite `## 8. Verification Engine` and `## Phase 7: Verification And Freshness` (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` § Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content.\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: T49 (spans), T50 (scope), T51 (expiry + incremental), T52 (surfacing) are sibling tasks — but the eight-state output model, the existence checks, the `verification_jobs` table, and the proposal-through-T39 invariant all ship here.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed (the `ProposalKind` enum grows variants), the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed and the architecture doc was updated in the same task.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14824,"cache_read_input_tokens":72452,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":14824,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015qAoQeXM7HFtFDzBbPkUNq","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"7a49a190-695d-477d-ae40-be1f0dafa035","request_id":"req_011Cb7NFLFEWqZ2jGvDUmCkH","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 6+7+Gate task briefs"}
