{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"a163eb6f432e922f5","tool_use_id":"toolu_015qAoQeXM7HFtFDzBbPkUNq","description":"Writing docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T49.md","subagent_type":"general-purpose","usage":{"total_tokens":88055,"tool_uses":30,"duration_ms":568066},"last_tool_name":"Write","uuid":"3ae57631-fe36-46e6-bdd8-3baa10d77bd0","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01T8NoMY658whtcPyMrX3ZgZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PFHFfTQt2LjaCRn4szRPxz","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T49.md","content":"# T49 — Phase 7 — Exact-span evidence validation + content hashes\n\n**Phase:** 7\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T48\n**Spec anchor:** [§Verification Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#8-verification-engine), [§Phase 7: Verification And Freshness](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-7-verification-and-freshness)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task implements the second verification check from spec §Verification Engine: when a memory's evidence captured an exact text span (a byte range or `(start_line, end_line)`) at the time of creation, verification must confirm the current file content at that span still matches what was captured. If it does not, the verifier emits a `MarkStale` proposal (the assertion may still be true but the citation is stale) or `MarkInvalidated` (the evidence is gone). This is the difference between \"the file still exists\" (T48) and \"what the memory said about the file is still backed by the same bytes.\" It is the load-bearing mechanism for the spec's §Stale Memory Leakage risk control.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Verification checks: ... evidence text still matches when exact spans were captured ...\"\n\n> Phase 7 DoD: \"stale or contradicted memory cannot appear as normal trusted guidance\".\n\n> §Non-Negotiable Product Properties: \"Every stale or contradicted memory is surfaced as such, not hidden behind recency.\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: T48 — `VerifierCore`, `VerificationStatus`, `VerificationVerdict`, `verification_jobs` schema. Span validation slots in as one more check kind alongside existence.\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/` — `MemoryEvidence` carries optional `span: Option<EvidenceSpan>` and `evidence_content_hash: Option<[u8; 32]>` from Phase 3.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/` — `FileId` resolves to a current file path + content hash.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` — file content cache; span checks should not re-hash the whole file when only the span is needed.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/existence.rs` (T48) — pattern for one-check-per-evidence-row.\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Hard limits, §Error handling, §Schema / model parity, §Observability; Lattice rules on doc-heading citation; spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Verification Engine \"Verification checks\" list. Copy the span-validation bullet verbatim into the top-of-file doc comment on `verification/spans.rs`.\n2. Define `pub struct EvidenceSpan { file_id: FileId, byte_start: u32, byte_end: u32, line_start: u32, line_end: u32 }` (mirror the Phase 3 column shape) and `pub enum SpanMismatch { ContentChanged, FileShrunkBelowSpan, EncodingChanged, FileMissing }`.\n3. In `verification/spans.rs`, implement `SpanValidator::validate(evidence: &MemoryEvidence, current_file_bytes: &[u8]) -> VerificationVerdict`. Algorithm: (a) if `evidence.span` is `None`, return `Verified` (this check is no-op for evidence without an exact span — the existence check from T48 already covered the file), (b) if `byte_end > current_file_bytes.len()`, return `VerificationVerdict { status: Stale, reason: \"FileShrunkBelowSpan\" }`, (c) compute SHA-256 of `current_file_bytes[byte_start..byte_end]` and compare to `evidence.evidence_content_hash`; equal → `Verified`, unequal → `Stale { reason: ContentChanged }`, (d) handle encoding-mismatch (BOM appearance/removal, CRLF/LF flip) explicitly by recording `EncodingChanged` so the surfacing layer in T52 can distinguish noise from substantive change.\n4. Wire `SpanValidator` into `VerifierCore::verify_memory` (T48): after existence checks pass, run span validation on every evidence row that has a span. Aggregate verdicts so the final memory status downgrades to `stale` if any span mismatches but no anchor is missing.\n5. Provide a streaming read path: do NOT read the whole file when only a small span needs verifying. Use the existing storage layer's `read_range(file_id, start, end)` (or add one if absent, in the same task) so verification stays cheap on large files.\n6. Persist span-mismatch details: extend the verification-jobs `reason` column to carry a structured JSON payload `{ \"kind\": \"SpanMismatch\", \"subkind\": \"ContentChanged\" | \"FileShrunkBelowSpan\" | \"EncodingChanged\" | \"FileMissing\", \"evidence_id\": <id> }` so the Phase 10 inbox UI can render the exact reason.\n7. Emit the verdict as a `MarkStale` proposal through the T39 runtime (never direct memory writes), carrying the structured reason payload.\n8. In `verification/spans_tests.rs`, write tests that: (a) unchanged content at the span returns `Verified`, (b) modified content at the span returns `Stale { ContentChanged }`, (c) file truncated below `byte_end` returns `Stale { FileShrunkBelowSpan }`, (d) CRLF↔LF flip is reported as `EncodingChanged`, not `ContentChanged`, (e) evidence with `span = None` returns `Verified` (no-op), (f) span validation never reads the whole file (assert via a tracing-instrumented mock storage that counts bytes read).\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/spans.rs` — `EvidenceSpan`, `SpanMismatch`, `SpanValidator::validate`, streaming-range read path, structured-reason emission.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/spans_tests.rs` — unchanged / modified / truncated / encoding-flip / no-span / no-whole-file-read coverage.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/spans.rs` — confirms the spans module exists.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib verification::spans_tests` — every span-validation unit test passes.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. `SpanValidator::validate` is a guard cascade — keep it flat.\n- Single source of truth: span validation routes through `VerifierCore` (T48) and emits proposals through T39; no parallel memory writes; range reads go through the existing storage layer.\n- Error handling: typed `SpanValidationError` for I/O or hash failures. No bare `unwrap`. A missing file is a typed `SpanMismatch::FileMissing` verdict, not an error.\n- Naming: `SpanValidator::validate`, `EvidenceSpan`, `SpanMismatch::ContentChanged`. No `Manager`/`Helper`.\n- Schema parity: structured-reason JSON has matching Rust types so serde round-trips losslessly.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Observability: every span-validation call emits a `tracing::debug_span!(\"validate_span\", memory_id, file_id, byte_start, byte_end, verdict)`.\n- Doc citation: file-top doc comment cites `## 8. Verification Engine` \"evidence text still matches when exact spans were captured\" and the §Non-Negotiable Product Properties bullet on stale surfacing (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` § Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content.\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: encoding-flip handling, structured-reason payload, and the no-whole-file-read guarantee all ship in this task.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed (e.g. the `verification_jobs.reason` column becomes JSON-shaped), the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed and the architecture doc was updated in the same task.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":14824,"cache_read_input_tokens":72452,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":14824,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015qAoQeXM7HFtFDzBbPkUNq","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"cea2d986-4548-4426-ae83-8e6a27b6c07d","request_id":"req_011Cb7NFLFEWqZ2jGvDUmCkH","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 6+7+Gate task briefs"}
