{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01DJMqeMGbDfRSjsJXmwYv1Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WpZd6b2e1eHwNty7vsm98j","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T23.md","content":"# T23 — Phase 3 — Memory graph CRUD + verification status transitions + idempotent writes\n\n**Phase:** 3\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T19, T20\n**Spec anchor:** [§Memory Graph](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#4-memory-graph)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules.\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task implements the public memory store API: create, read, update, delete, and the state-machine transitions over `VerificationStatus` (`unverified → in_review → verified`, plus `stale`, `contradicted`, `superseded`, `expired`, `invalidated`). Writes are idempotent on a caller-provided idempotency key so retries do not double-insert. Every status transition emits the right event via the T13 writer (`MemoryCreated`, `MemoryUpdated`, `MemoryInvalidated`, `MemoryConsolidated`) and records an evidence row pointing at the triggering event. Without this task, the redesigned schema has no callable API and Phase 4 retrieval has nothing to read.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Verification outputs: `verified`, `unverified`, `in_review`, `stale`, `contradicted`, `superseded`, `expired`, `invalidated`.\"\n\n> \"Memory links should be first-class records … verification status.\"\n\n> \"No consolidation job may silently rewrite high-scope memory without preserving provenance and prior state.\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs:\n  - T19 — `MemoryRecord`, `MemoryClass`, `VerificationStatus`, `MemoryScope`, schema.\n  - T20 — `memory_links`, `memory_evidence`, `memory_accesses`, `memory_scores` tables and their CRUD APIs.\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/writer.rs` (T13) — `EventWriter` used to emit lifecycle events.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/scope.rs` (T21) — `ScopeFilter` used on every read API.\n  - Existing identity types from Phase 1.\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Error handling, §Naming, §Schema / model parity.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. In `memory_graph/store.rs`, define `pub struct MemoryStore { conn: Arc<Mutex<rusqlite::Connection>>, event_writer: Arc<EventWriter> }` with `MemoryStore::open(...)`.\n2. Define the create API: `pub fn MemoryStore::create(&self, draft: MemoryDraft, idempotency_key: IdempotencyKey) -> Result<MemoryRecord, MemoryStoreError>`. `MemoryDraft` is `MemoryRecord` minus `memory_id`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `usefulness_score`, `verification_status` (initial status is always `Unverified`). On insert, emit `MemoryCreated` event with payload `{ memory_id, class, stream, scope, idempotency_key }`. Insert evidence rows from `draft.initial_evidence`.\n3. Implement idempotency: store `idempotency_key` in a `memory_idempotency` table mapping key → `memory_id`. On `create` with a key that already exists, return the existing record without inserting; never raise an error.\n4. Define the read APIs (all take `&ScopeFilter` per T21):\n   - `get(memory_id, scope) -> Result<MemoryRecord, MemoryStoreError>`.\n   - `list_by_class(class, scope, limit) -> Result<Vec<MemoryRecord>, _>`.\n   - `list_by_stream(stream, scope, limit) -> Result<Vec<MemoryRecord>, _>`.\n   - `list_by_status(status, scope, limit) -> Result<Vec<MemoryRecord>, _>`.\n   - Reads with no scope refuse to compile (`ScopeFilter` is required).\n5. Define the update API: `pub fn update(&self, memory_id, patch: MemoryPatch, evidence: Option<MemoryEvidence>, idempotency_key: IdempotencyKey) -> Result<MemoryRecord, MemoryStoreError>`. `MemoryPatch` is the set of optional updatable fields (content, confidence, freshness_policy, validity_conditions, invalidation_triggers, scope) but NOT `verification_status` (use `transition_status`) and NOT `memory_id` (immutable). Emit `MemoryUpdated` event.\n6. Define the delete API: `pub fn delete(&self, memory_id, reason: &str) -> Result<(), MemoryStoreError>`. Delete is soft: set `verification_status = Invalidated` and write a tombstone row; the original record is kept for replay. Emit `MemoryInvalidated` event.\n7. In `memory_graph/transitions.rs`, define the verification state machine: `pub fn transition_status(store: &MemoryStore, memory_id: MemoryId, to: VerificationStatus, reason: &str, evidence: Option<MemoryEvidence>) -> Result<MemoryRecord, MemoryTransitionError>`. Allowed transitions per spec:\n   - `Unverified → InReview` (verification job started)\n   - `Unverified → Verified` (deterministic verification passed)\n   - `InReview → Verified` (human approval or job completion)\n   - `InReview → Stale` / `Contradicted` / `Expired` / `Invalidated` (review outcome)\n   - `Verified → Stale` (file changed since verification)\n   - `Verified → Contradicted` (counter-memory or contradicting link added)\n   - `Verified → Superseded` (newer memory supersedes; `superseded_by` column populated)\n   - `Verified → Expired` (TTL elapsed)\n   - `Verified → Invalidated` (manual or trigger-based invalidation)\n   - `Stale → Verified` (re-verification passed; evidence updated)\n   - `Stale → Invalidated` (re-verification failed and not recoverable)\n   - terminal: `Invalidated`, `Expired`, `Superseded` do not transition further.\n   Any disallowed transition returns `MemoryTransitionError::DisallowedTransition { from, to }`.\n8. Every transition writes an evidence row pointing at the triggering event and emits the right lifecycle event: `Verified`/`Stale`/`Contradicted`/`Superseded`/`Expired` use `MemoryUpdated`; `Invalidated` uses `MemoryInvalidated`; `MemoryConsolidated` is reserved for Phase 6 consolidation transitions.\n9. Define `MemoryStoreError` typed enum: `NotFound(MemoryId)`, `ScopeViolation(ScopeError)`, `ConstraintViolation { detail }`, `Storage(rusqlite::Error)`, `Identity(IdentityError)`, `EventEmit(EventWriteError)`. Define `MemoryTransitionError` separately so callers can pattern-match on transition issues specifically.\n10. In `memory_graph/store_tests.rs`, write tests covering: create → read round-trip; create with same idempotency key returns the existing record; update preserves immutable fields; soft-delete leaves the row readable as `Invalidated`; every legal transition is exercised; at least three illegal transitions are exercised and return `DisallowedTransition`; every transition emits the expected event (assert via `EventReader::tail`).\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/store.rs` — `MemoryStore`, `MemoryDraft`, `MemoryPatch`, `IdempotencyKey`, CRUD APIs, idempotency table integration, event emission.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/transitions.rs` — `transition_status`, allowed-transitions matrix, `MemoryTransitionError`.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/store_tests.rs` — CRUD round-trip, idempotency dedupe, immutable-field preservation, soft-delete, full legal-transition coverage, illegal-transition rejection, event-emission assertions.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory_graph/store.rs` — store module exists.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib memory_graph::store_tests` — every CRUD + transition test passes.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10.\n- Schema parity: `MemoryDraft` and `MemoryPatch` reference only fields that exist on `MemoryRecord`; mutability of each field is encoded in the patch type, not via runtime checks.\n- No silent error handling — every transition returns a typed error; event-emission failures roll back the SQL transaction (`?` from inside the txn).\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, commented-out code.\n- For SQLite: every write wrapped in a transaction; `rusqlite::params!`; no SQL formatting.\n- Use `tracing::info_span!(\"memory_store.transition\", from = ?, to = ?)`.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content.\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: CRUD, idempotency, soft-delete, every legal transition, illegal-transition rejection, event emission per lifecycle — all in this task.\n- [ ] Architecture doc updated in the same task if behavior is publicly observable — extend `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-graph-schema.md` (T19) with `## Lifecycle and transitions` section containing the allowed-transitions matrix; the code references this section by heading.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15982,"cache_read_input_tokens":85859,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":15982,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01KTEqX34f6x4nqNqXUnhApL","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"6b88070b-aa69-402d-81c5-aebedfeeefb2","request_id":"req_011Cb7NNhAmfrKHCVCozvQXS","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 2+3+Gate task briefs"}
