{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019ScAFhwj15KgrT4jB8Uvi8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XuuBfiW4BrZAovETLJov6f","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T80.md","content":"# T80 — Phase 11 — Large-repo performance tests\n\n**Phase:** 11\n**Type:** tests\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** R79\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 11: Hardening](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-11-hardening), [§Phase 1: Unified Identity Model](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-1-unified-identity-model), [§Phase 2: Event Log Substrate](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-2-event-log-substrate), [§Measurable Success Criteria](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#measurable-success-criteria)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task delivers the large-repo performance test suite that proves the hot-path budgets from Phases 1 and 2 hold at realistic scale, not only on the toy repo the unit tests use. Spec §Phase 1 sets identity resolution at ≤2ms P99; spec §Phase 2 sets event write at ≤5ms P99 on `prepare_change` and `get_context_capsule`; spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties bans \"unbounded graph traversal, payload growth, or event-log scans on hot paths.\" This task takes the fixture repos captured by T66 (large-repo fixtures from the benchmark suite — multiple languages, multiple repo sizes) and exercises every hot path against them, asserts the P99 budgets, and writes the results to `large_repo_results.json` for the metrics dashboard and R87 review.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 11 deliverables: large-repo performance tests; concurrency tests; recovery tests; corrupted-event handling; partial-index handling; workspace-boundary tests; migration tests; MCP schema compatibility tests; documentation for setup, operations, memory semantics, and workflow behavior.\"\n\n> \"Phase 11 definition of done: the system is production-grade for repeated agent use, not only successful on a toy repo.\"\n\n> \"Identity resolution adds no more than 2ms P99 to hot-path tool calls.\" (spec §Phase 1 DoD)\n\n> \"Event write adds no more than 5ms P99 to hot-path tool calls (`prepare_change`, `get_context_capsule`); large payloads spill to a side table rather than blocking the writer.\" (spec §Phase 2 DoD)\n\n> \"No unbounded graph traversal, payload growth, or event-log scans on hot paths.\" (spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: R79 (contract gate verdict) — confirms the daemon contract is stable so perf tests measure the shipping path, not in-flux APIs. Implicit upstream: T66 (large-repo fixture suite from Phase 9 benchmarking).\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/benchmark_tests.rs` and `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/query/benchmark_tests.rs` — existing benchmark patterns to mirror.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/benches/baseline_workflows.rs` (from T04) — baseline pattern.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/` (Phase 1 module) — identity resolver under test.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/` (Phase 2 module) — event writer under test.\n  - T66 large-repo fixture corpus (assumed at `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/fixtures/large_repos/` per the build context — verify at start of this task).\n- Standards files to honor: `coding.md` (hard limits, tests as documentation, observability); `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Phase 1 DoD (identity ≤2ms P99), §Phase 2 DoD (event write ≤5ms P99), §Non-Negotiable Product Properties (no unbounded scans), §Phase 11 deliverables, and §Measurable Success Criteria so the budgets and the targets are pinned before any code.\n2. Confirm the T66 fixture corpus exists; if absent, this task documents the gap and opens a follow-up. The harness assumes T66 ran; the fixture set must include at least: small-Rust (~5k files), medium-TypeScript (~25k files), large-polyglot (~100k files), and one extra-large fixture (~250k files) to stress event-log scans.\n3. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/large_repo_tests.rs` (new module under a new `hardening/` directory; register it from `lib.rs`). Annotate the tests with `#[ignore]` so default `cargo test --workspace` does not slow CI; the verification command uses `-- --include-ignored` to opt in.\n4. For each fixture, implement a test that:\n   - Spins up a daemon instance against a temp `.lattice/` directory rooted at the fixture.\n   - Performs a full incremental indexing pass and records the wall-clock duration.\n   - Runs N (≥1000) hot-path tool invocations for each of `prepare_change`, `get_context_capsule`, `expand_context`, `impact_from_diff`, `diagnose_failure`, `search_symbols`, `find_relevant_tests`.\n   - Computes per-tool P50, P95, P99 latency and asserts P99 ≤ the budget from the spec: identity resolution ≤2ms, event write ≤5ms, total tool latency must beat the baseline captured in T04 by the documented initial targets from §Measurable Success Criteria (30% fewer discovery calls is a quality metric, not latency — but the latency must not regress vs T04 baselines).\n   - Asserts no graph traversal scanned more than the documented neighborhood budget; assert no event-log query scanned more than the documented index slice; both via debug counters exposed by the daemon's tracing.\n5. Capture P50/P95/P99 per tool per fixture into a JSON report at `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/large_repo_results.json`. Schema mirrors `baseline_metrics.json` from T04 with an extra `fixture` field. The file is committed to the repo so R87 and R89 can diff against later runs.\n6. Add a test that exercises event-log compaction at large scale: write 1M events into the log, trigger compaction per spec §Storage Design \"event log compaction\", measure compaction wall-clock and assert the daemon remains responsive (hot-path P99 within budget while compaction runs).\n7. Add a test that exercises payload spillover: write a series of events whose payloads exceed the inline threshold from T13 (or wherever the threshold was defined in Phase 2), assert spillover row writes succeed and reads round-trip without breaking the hot-path budget.\n8. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release` then `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::large_repo_tests -- --include-ignored` and confirm every test passes. Capture the output and update the JSON report.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/large_repo_tests.rs` — `#[ignore]`d large-repo perf tests for every hot path against every fixture from T66, asserting the P99 budgets from spec §Phase 1 and §Phase 2.\n- `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/large_repo_results.json` — P50/P95/P99 per tool per fixture, plus indexing wall-clock and compaction wall-clock; committed to the repo for regression tracking.\n\n(Implicitly required: `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/mod.rs` registering the new module, and a `mod hardening;` line in `lib.rs`.)\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/large_repo_tests.rs` — confirms the test module exists at the path the harness expects.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::large_repo_tests -- --include-ignored` — runs every large-repo perf test (including the ones marked `#[ignore]` for default-skip) and confirms every P99 budget assertion passes.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines (split per fixture if it exceeds, e.g. `large_repo_tests/rust.rs`, `large_repo_tests/typescript.rs`).\n- Function length ≤50 lines per test; setup factored into helpers.\n- Tests as documentation: each test name describes the budget it asserts (e.g. `test_prepare_change_p99_under_5ms_on_large_polyglot_fixture`), per `coding.md` §Tests as documentation.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- No silent error handling — every measurement that fails the budget panics with a message naming the tool, fixture, observed P99, and budget.\n- Observability: tests emit `tracing` events under a dedicated target so the JSON report can be regenerated from the trace if needed.\n- Doc citation: comments cite `## Phase 1: Unified Identity Model` (DoD), `## Phase 2: Event Log Substrate` (DoD), and `## Non-Negotiable Product Properties` for the budget rules (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] All four (or more) fixture sizes covered; every hot path measured on every fixture; every P99 budget asserted.\n- [ ] Compaction + spillover stress tests included.\n- [ ] `large_repo_results.json` regenerated from the most recent run.\n- [ ] No deferred work: every hot path from spec §Phase 1 and §Phase 2 DoD covered in this task; concurrency (T81), recovery (T82), partial-index (T83), and migration (T84) are sibling Phase 11 tasks, not deferrals.\n- [ ] After build, deploy per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy procedure.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":101320,"cache_read_input_tokens":10845,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":101320,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XjrTa6YAS1dmMW989ZPauZ","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"9e82d955-3d5b-4136-a79d-f6189037af92","request_id":"req_011Cb7NGicAyFMeCwEAwKwU2","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 10+11+Final task briefs"}
