{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01FdMLjaXcZQEvJnpbkscPQS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012fr4bjgjxamqXhLwBA43HP","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R38.md","content":"# R38 — Backend review — Phase 5 working memory\n\n**Phase:** 5\n**Type:** review\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** T34, T35, T36, T37\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 5: Working Memory](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-5-working-memory), [§5. Working Memory](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#5-working-memory), [§3. Event Log](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#3-event-log)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis review certifies that Phase 5 — Working Memory — is complete, spec-faithful, and ships the excluded-context auditability that makes working memory trustworthy. The reviewer reads every file produced by T34–T37, runs the verification commands, and writes a structured findings report under `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R38-working-memory.md`. The report uses the headings required by the verification commands so the build harness can confirm it was actually written, not stubbed. Verdict is one of `Pass`, `Pass with follow-ups`, or `Fail with required rework`; `Fail` blocks the Phase 6 consolidation work from starting.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this review\n\n> \"Working memory contains: task statement; interpreted intent; active files and symbols; active hypotheses; active failures; current plan; selected memories; excluded memories and reasons; budget decisions; unresolved questions; verification status.\" (spec §5. Working Memory)\n\n> \"Required operations: retrieve; summarize; filter; pin; evict; expand; compress; checkpoint.\" (spec §5. Working Memory)\n\n> \"Phase 5: Working Memory — Deliverables: explicit per-task working memory state; operations for retrieve, summarize, filter, pin, evict, expand, compress, and checkpoint; MCP surface for inspecting current working memory; automatic event capture for included and excluded context; tests for token budgets, pinned context, eviction, and checkpoint restore. Definition of done: workflow tools can show what context is active, why it is active, and what was intentionally excluded; context management is no longer just prompt accumulation.\" (spec §Phase 5: Working Memory)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: every artifact produced by T34 (state + checkpoint table), T35 (operations), T36 (MCP tool + event hooks), T37 (test families).\n- Existing files this review reads:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/mod.rs`, `state.rs`, `schema.sql`, `state_tests.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/operations.rs`, `operations_tests.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/event_hooks.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/working_memory_tool.rs`, `working_memory_tool_tests.rs`\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/working_memory/budget_tests.rs`, `checkpoint_tests.rs`\n- Standards files to honor: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`; `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`; `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/AGENTS.md`.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §5. Working Memory, §Phase 5: Working Memory, and the relevant lines of §3. Event Log in full.\n2. Run every verification command from T34–T37 in sequence and record pass/fail with output excerpts in the review's `## Findings` section.\n3. Audit field coverage: open `WorkingMemoryState` and confirm every one of the eleven spec-named fields is present with the correct nullability and type; flag any field that was renamed or merged.\n4. Audit operation coverage: confirm each of the eight required operations exists as a callable, has a test in `operations_tests.rs`, honors the documented contract (idempotency, pin protection, no-op handling, etc.), and emits the appropriate event via T36's hook.\n5. Audit excluded-context auditability — the heart of this review:\n   - Confirm `ExcludedMemory.exclusion_reason` is non-optional and that every drop/skip path across T35 operations writes a populated reason (sample at least one entry from each of `filter`, `evict`, `compress`).\n   - Run the MCP `inspect_working_memory` tool against a synthetic state with mixed include/exclude entries; confirm `include_excluded=true` returns the excluded entries with reasons; confirm `include_excluded=false` does not silently leak them in a separate field.\n   - Confirm event hooks emit `MemoryRetrieved` / `MemoryExpanded` events whose payloads carry the included and excluded identity diffs with reasons. Sample at least three event payloads from the test capture.\n6. Audit checkpoint integrity: confirm `working_memory_checkpoints` schema has the documented columns and indexes; confirm save/load round-trip is byte-identical via canonical-JSON SHA-256; confirm version mismatch is rejected.\n7. Audit MCP surface compliance with spec §9: tool registration appears in `tools/list`; response supports compact and full modes; an `expansion_handle` is included; budget controls are respected.\n8. Audit coding-standard compliance across all produced files: file ≤800 lines, function ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, no TODOs/FIXMEs/commented-out code/unjustified `#[allow(...)]`, single source of truth (no parallel state loader, no parallel event writer, no fixtures duplicated with T32).\n9. Cross-check Phase 4 forward-compatibility actually held: confirm `RetrievalBundle` and `BundleResult` are embedded under `selected_memories` and `excluded_memories.result` unchanged from the Phase 4 schema; if a field was added or renamed, flag it as a Phase 4 rework requirement.\n10. Write the findings report under `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R38-working-memory.md` with the required headings; assign a verdict; list follow-ups (if any) as actionable items addressed to specific subsequent tasks.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R38-working-memory.md` — Phase 5 review report with required headings.\n\n## Required headings (verified by grep)\n\n- `## Spec alignment` — each spec deliverable and Definition-of-Done item mapped to the implementing task and file; deviations called out by name.\n- `## Coding-standard alignment` — per-file pass/fail against `coding.md` hard limits; any over-limit files flagged with the required justification.\n- `## Excluded-context auditability` — audit of `ExcludedMemory.exclusion_reason` population across all drop/skip paths, MCP `include_excluded` behaviour, and event-payload diffs containing inclusion/exclusion reasons.\n- `## Findings` — concrete observations, including verification-command output excerpts and any issues uncovered.\n- `## Verdict` — `Pass`, `Pass with follow-ups`, or `Fail with required rework`; if `Fail`, the report names the tasks that must be reopened before Phase 6 work can start.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R38-working-memory.md`\n- `grep -q '## Spec alignment' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R38-working-memory.md`\n- `grep -q '## Excluded-context auditability' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R38-working-memory.md`\n- `grep -q '## Verdict' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R38-working-memory.md`\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- The review report file ≤800 lines.\n- Function/nesting/cyclomatic limits not applicable (docs task).\n- Schema parity: not applicable directly, but the review confirms T34's schema parity between `working_memory_checkpoints` columns and `WorkingMemoryState` fields.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, or commented-out code in the report.\n- No broken windows: every follow-up is filed with a target task ID, never left as \"we'll come back to this.\"\n- Doc citation: the report cites the exact spec headings reviewed, per `/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md` \"Markdown Heading References\".\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Review report exists at the expected path with all four required headings.\n- [ ] Every verification command from T34–T37 was run and its result recorded.\n- [ ] Eleven spec-named state fields confirmed present.\n- [ ] Eight required operations confirmed present and contract-tested.\n- [ ] Excluded-context auditability audit covers all drop/skip paths, the MCP tool's `include_excluded` mode, and event-payload diffs.\n- [ ] Checkpoint round-trip byte-identical and version-rejection behaviour confirmed.\n- [ ] Phase 4 forward-compatibility check confirms `RetrievalBundle` shape was preserved.\n- [ ] Verdict is recorded; if not `Pass`, follow-ups name specific tasks to reopen.\n- [ ] No deferred work: every spec §Phase 5 Definition-of-Done item is asserted in the report.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3027,"cache_read_input_tokens":82079,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3027,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":50,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019RjXwCuf57BAKn88mWkE24","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"6e3f0850-0c5a-4677-99ad-a673470bd600","request_id":"req_011Cb7NQb1jiUJr7CRQTKm9E","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 4+5 task briefs"}
