{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019ScAFhwj15KgrT4jB8Uvi8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GiPK3xTN4G1waMDh8j9Yv3","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T81.md","content":"# T81 — Phase 11 — Concurrency tests (parallel sessions, write contention, replay-safe)\n\n**Phase:** 11\n**Type:** tests\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** R79\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 11: Hardening](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-11-hardening), [§3. Event Log](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#3-event-log), [§6. Consolidation Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#6-consolidation-engine), [§Testing Requirements](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#testing-requirements)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task delivers the concurrency test suite covering parallel sessions, write contention against the event log and memory store, and the replay-safe execution invariant for consolidation jobs. Spec §3 makes the event log append-only and replayable; spec §6 requires consolidation to be \"auditable, reversible, and test-covered\" with \"replay-safe job execution.\" Spec §Phase 11 deliverables list \"concurrency tests\" explicitly. Without this suite, race conditions in event ordering, double-applied consolidation jobs, or memory-link torn writes would only surface in production. This task forces those failure modes to happen in CI.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 11 deliverables: ... concurrency tests; recovery tests; ...\"\n\n> \"Required test families: ... concurrency tests; large fixture performance tests; ...\" (spec §Testing Requirements)\n\n> \"Replay-safe job execution.\" (spec §6 — consolidation engine deliverables)\n\n> \"The event log should be append-only and replayable.\" (spec §3)\n\n> \"Tests for ordering, replay, corruption handling, and workspace scoping.\" (spec §Phase 2 deliverables — concurrency is the contention side of ordering and replay.)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: R79 (contract gate) — confirms the daemon API the tests exercise is stable.\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/` (Phase 2 event writer/reader).\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/` (Phase 3 memory store + link + evidence tables).\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/` (Phase 6 consolidation jobs and proposal apply path).\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` (SQLite connection pool, WAL mode).\n- Standards files to honor: `coding.md`; `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §3 Event Log (append-only, replayable), §6 Consolidation Engine (replay-safe execution, proposal-only writes), §Phase 11 deliverables, and §Testing Requirements so the concurrency invariants are pinned.\n2. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/concurrency_tests.rs` (alongside `large_repo_tests.rs` from T80) and register it in the new `hardening/mod.rs`. Mark slow tests `#[ignore]` to opt in via the verification command's `--include-ignored` flag.\n3. Implement parallel-session tests:\n   - N (≥32) tokio tasks each open a separate daemon session, write a stream of events (`AssistantTaskStarted`, `ToolCalled`, `ToolResult`, `ContextBundleReturned`, …), and read them back. Assert per-session event ordering is preserved.\n   - Assert workspace scoping holds: events from session A do not appear in queries from session B except via cross-session queries that explicitly request them.\n   - Assert no event id collisions across sessions.\n4. Implement write-contention tests:\n   - N parallel writers each append events to the same `events` table; assert the daemon serializes writes without dropping any (count in = count out) and that ordering within each writer is preserved.\n   - N parallel writers each create memory records with overlapping classes/scopes; assert no duplicate stable ids; assert per-record invariants (confidence in [0,1], status valid) hold under contention.\n   - N parallel writers each create `memory_links` rows referencing the same source memory; assert no link drops, no torn writes (every row has both source and target set or neither), and that the access-history counter increments by exactly N.\n5. Implement replay-safe consolidation tests:\n   - Seed an event log with a deterministic trace; run consolidation jobs (episode summary, procedure extraction, contradiction detection); record the resulting memory state.\n   - Replay the same event log into a fresh daemon instance; run the same jobs; assert the resulting memory state is byte-identical (or, where LLM-driven, that the proposal records are identical aside from documented non-determinism placeholders such as `proposal_id`).\n   - Apply a proposal twice (simulating retry); assert the second apply is a no-op (idempotent) rather than producing a duplicate write.\n6. Implement reader-vs-writer tests: while N writers append events, a reader iterates the log and asserts it never observes a partial event, never observes events out of monotonic timestamp order within a single session, and that an iterator finishing observes a consistent snapshot.\n7. Implement compaction-during-write tests: trigger an event-log compaction snapshot (per spec §Storage Design) while writers are still appending; assert no events lost, no events duplicated, and that the snapshot + post-snapshot log together replay to the same state as the pre-compaction log.\n8. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release` then `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::concurrency_tests -- --include-ignored` and confirm every test passes.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/concurrency_tests.rs` — parallel-session, write-contention, replay-safe-consolidation, reader-vs-writer, and compaction-during-write tests covering events, memory store, links, and consolidation jobs.\n\n(Implicitly required: `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/mod.rs` declaring the new test module if not already present from T80.)\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/concurrency_tests.rs` — confirms the test module exists at the path the harness expects.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::concurrency_tests -- --include-ignored` — runs every concurrency test (including the slow ones marked `#[ignore]`) and confirms every invariant assertion passes.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines (split per concern if it exceeds, e.g. `concurrency_tests/events.rs`, `concurrency_tests/memory.rs`, `concurrency_tests/consolidation.rs`).\n- Function length ≤50 lines per test; setup factored into helpers (shared daemon-instance factory, event-stream generator, memory-record builder).\n- Tests as documentation: each test name describes the invariant it asserts (e.g. `test_parallel_writers_preserve_per_writer_ordering`, `test_consolidation_apply_is_idempotent`).\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- No silent error handling — every assertion failure panics with a message naming the scenario and the violated invariant.\n- Observability: tests emit `tracing` events under a dedicated target so race conditions can be diagnosed from logs even when not reproducible locally.\n- Doc citation: comments cite `## 3. Event Log`, `## 6. Consolidation Engine`, and `## Phase 11: Hardening` (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] Parallel-session, write-contention, replay-safe-consolidation, reader-vs-writer, and compaction-during-write scenarios all covered.\n- [ ] Idempotent apply test covers double-apply of a proposal.\n- [ ] No deferred work: every concurrency surface from spec §3 and §6 covered; recovery + corruption (T82), partial-index (T83), and migration (T84) are sibling Phase 11 tasks, not deferrals.\n- [ ] After build, deploy per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy procedure.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":101320,"cache_read_input_tokens":10845,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":101320,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XjrTa6YAS1dmMW989ZPauZ","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"cfad5a15-9f00-4000-bff5-0ab83b9da053","request_id":"req_011Cb7NGicAyFMeCwEAwKwU2","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 10+11+Final task briefs"}
