{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"a163eb6f432e922f5","tool_use_id":"toolu_015qAoQeXM7HFtFDzBbPkUNq","description":"Writing docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T51.md","subagent_type":"general-purpose","usage":{"total_tokens":102032,"tool_uses":32,"duration_ms":659584},"last_tool_name":"Write","uuid":"acad4ff5-7ff9-4d6e-ba28-abdbfec15c1d","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_015MDyAMJnW12qQpzjxve9XN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BjMbXEGZM9a37GGDX8KtBE","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T51.md","content":"# T51 — Phase 7 — Time-bound expiry + incremental verification triggered by graph changes\n\n**Phase:** 7\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T48, T49, T50\n**Spec anchor:** [§Verification Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#8-verification-engine), [§Phase 7: Verification And Freshness](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-7-verification-and-freshness)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task ships two spec-required Phase 7 mechanisms. First, time-bound expiry: memories with an `expires_at` reach the `expired` state automatically when their timestamp passes, and the verifier emits the corresponding `MarkExpired` proposal. Second, incremental verification: the verifier walks only memories whose evidence cites files/symbols that actually changed since the last graph snapshot, never a full rescan. The spec is explicit that \"large repos cannot tolerate full rescans for every memory\" — this is the mechanism that makes Phase 7 scalable.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Verification checks: ... time-bound memory has expired.\"\n\n> \"Verification outputs: ... `expired` ...\"\n\n> \"Verification must be incremental and tied to workspace changes. Large repos cannot tolerate full rescans for every memory.\"\n\n> Phase 7 DoD: \"stale or contradicted memory cannot appear as normal trusted guidance; verification results are explainable and queryable.\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: T48 (verifier core + `verification_jobs`), T49 (span validation), T50 (scope enforcement). Incremental verification dispatches to all three.\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/` — `Memory.expires_at: Option<DateTime<Utc>>` from Phase 3.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/graph/` — `GraphSnapshot` API; the incremental verifier asks for the file/symbol delta between two snapshot ids.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/indexer/` — hook point where the indexer announces file deltas so the verifier can subscribe.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` — `last_verified_at` and `last_verified_graph_snapshot_id` columns on memories (Phase 3); if absent, add via migration in this task.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/consolidation/proposal.rs` — `MarkExpired` proposal variant (add to `ProposalKind` if not present).\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Hard limits, §Single source of truth, §Error handling, §Observability; Lattice rules on doc-heading citation; spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties on no unbounded scans.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Verification Engine \"Verification checks\" + \"Verification outputs\" + the incremental constraint. Copy verbatim into the top-of-file doc comments on `verification/expiry.rs` and `verification/incremental.rs`.\n2. In `verification/expiry.rs`, implement `ExpiryScanner::scan(workspace_id, now: DateTime<Utc>) -> ExpiryReport`. Query memories with `expires_at IS NOT NULL AND expires_at <= ? AND verification_status != 'expired'`. For each match, emit a `MarkExpired` proposal through the T39 runtime carrying `prior_state.expires_at` and `proposed_state.verification_status = 'expired'`. Idempotent: re-running on a memory already `expired` is a no-op.\n3. Add `MarkExpired` to `ProposalKind` if not already present (T39 migration discipline) and ensure `VerificationStatus::Expired` from T48 round-trips into the memory store.\n4. In `verification/incremental.rs`, implement `IncrementalVerifier::on_graph_delta(prior_snapshot_id, new_snapshot_id, changed_files: Vec<FileId>)`. Algorithm: (a) compute the set of changed symbols by intersecting changed files with the graph's `Contains` edges from Phase 1, (b) query `memory_evidence` for every memory citing any changed file or symbol, (c) dispatch each impacted memory through `VerifierCore::verify_memory` (T48 + T49 + T50 in sequence — existence, span, scope), (d) update `last_verified_graph_snapshot_id` on memories whose verdict is now `Verified`, (e) return an `IncrementalReport { impacted, verified, stale, invalidated, expired, elapsed }`.\n5. Forbid full rescans on the incremental path: add a `cfg(debug_assertions)` invariant that `impacted.len() <= memory_evidence.rows_for_changed_files()` so a regression cannot silently widen the scan.\n6. Wire `IncrementalVerifier::on_graph_delta` into the indexer's existing `files-updated` callback (matches the wiring pattern T41's `StaleMarker::on_graph_change` uses). The verifier should run under a daemon-scheduled bounded work budget so a huge delta does not stall the daemon — overflow re-enqueues remaining memories for the next tick.\n7. Provide an explicit `IncrementalVerifier::run_pending_expiry(workspace_id, now)` periodic entry point that wraps `ExpiryScanner::scan` so expiry can run on a slow timer (e.g. every 5 minutes) without a graph delta.\n8. Update memory rows on successful verification: bump `last_verified_at = now` and `last_verified_graph_snapshot_id = new_snapshot_id` via T39 proposals (`Refresh` kind from T41) — never direct writes.\n9. In `verification/incremental_tests.rs`, write tests that: (a) a graph delta touching file `F` causes only memories whose evidence cites `F` (or symbols contained in `F`) to be re-verified; memories citing unrelated files are NOT scanned (assert via a counting test seam), (b) the `ExpiryScanner` flips `expires_at <= now` memories to `expired` via a `MarkExpired` proposal and is idempotent on re-run, (c) `last_verified_graph_snapshot_id` advances on success, (d) a memory whose evidence cites a deleted file goes from `verified` → `invalidated` on the next delta, (e) `IncrementalVerifier` respects the bounded work budget — given 1000 impacted memories and a budget of 50, exactly 50 are processed and the remainder is re-enqueued.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/expiry.rs` — `ExpiryScanner::scan`, `MarkExpired` proposal emission, idempotence.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/incremental.rs` — `IncrementalVerifier::on_graph_delta`, change-set narrowing, bounded work budget, snapshot-id bump on success.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/incremental_tests.rs` — incremental-scope narrowing, expiry idempotence, budget enforcement, snapshot-id propagation.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/expiry.rs` — confirms the expiry module exists.\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/incremental.rs` — confirms the incremental module exists.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib verification::incremental_tests` — every expiry + incremental unit test passes.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. `IncrementalVerifier::on_graph_delta` is a pipeline of small helpers (delta → impacted set → per-memory verify → report).\n- Single source of truth: per-memory verification routes through `VerifierCore::verify_memory` (T48); state writes route through T39 proposals; no parallel paths.\n- Error handling: typed `ExpiryError` / `IncrementalError`. No bare `unwrap`. Per-memory failures emit `tracing::warn!` and continue scanning.\n- Naming: `ExpiryScanner::scan`, `IncrementalVerifier::on_graph_delta`, `last_verified_graph_snapshot_id`. No `Manager`/`Helper`.\n- Schema parity: `last_verified_at`, `last_verified_graph_snapshot_id` migrations covered; nullable columns map to `Option<…>`.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Observability: `tracing::info_span!(\"incremental_verification\", workspace_id, prior_snapshot, new_snapshot, impacted, verified, stale, invalidated, expired, elapsed_ms)`.\n- Doc citation: cite `## 8. Verification Engine` \"Verification must be incremental and tied to workspace changes\" and \"time-bound memory has expired\" (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` § Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content.\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: expiry, incremental, snapshot-id propagation, bounded-budget re-enqueue, and the no-full-rescan guard all ship here.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed (memory schema gains `last_verified_graph_snapshot_id`), the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed and the architecture doc was updated in the same task.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13920,"cache_read_input_tokens":87276,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":13920,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":51,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015qAoQeXM7HFtFDzBbPkUNq","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"3986da32-a15d-467f-9415-3510b5593a60","request_id":"req_011Cb7NTyC4xxGsapJgX4yFX","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 6+7+Gate task briefs"}
