{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01DJMqeMGbDfRSjsJXmwYv1Q","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LfqJC9j2GeH4JtMsCgKo53","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R26.md","content":"# R26 — Contract gate — Identity ↔ Event Log ↔ Memory cross-layer contracts\n\n**Phase:** Contract gate\n**Type:** review\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** R10, R18, R25\n**Spec anchor:** [§Design Thesis](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#design-thesis)\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis gate certifies the cross-layer round-trip contracts between the three first-class substrates the spec names: workspace identity, event log, and memory graph. Each layer was reviewed in isolation by R10, R18, R25; this gate proves they compose. Specifically: stable identity references serialize cleanly into event payloads, those payloads round-trip back to the same identity targets, and memory records link to stable identities (not transient names) so memory survives identity refactors and event replays. This gate is the contract that the rest of the build (retrieval, working memory, consolidation, verification) can assume. A failed verdict here blocks T27 (Phase 4 start) because no later layer can be trustworthy on broken cross-layer contracts.\n\n## Inputs to read\n\n- Every artifact from R10 dependency tasks (Phase 1 identity): identity types, resolver, ambiguity diagnostics, serialization tests.\n- Every artifact from R18 dependency tasks (T11–T17): event model, store, writer, reader, capture, snapshot/compaction, tests.\n- Every artifact from R25 dependency tasks (T19–T24): memory classes, links, evidence, accesses, scores, streams, scope, migration, CRUD, transitions, contradiction/supersession/replay tests.\n- The R10, R18, R25 review markdown files themselves (verdicts must be APPROVED or APPROVED WITH FOLLOW-UPS — a REJECTED prior review blocks this gate).\n- Spec sections claimed satisfied:\n  - §Design Thesis (three substrates sharing identity, storage, and ranking primitives)\n  - §Phase 1: Unified Identity Model (DoD: every workflow output can be expanded through a stable identity)\n  - §Phase 2: Event Log Substrate (DoD: every workflow records task/retrieval/response/outcome events using stable identities)\n  - §Phase 3: Memory Graph Storage (DoD: every memory can explain its evidence and relationship state)\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Schema / model parity, §Tests as documentation.\n\n## Review procedure\n\n1. Verify identity references serialize cleanly into event payloads: pick each payload struct that embeds a `StableRef` (e.g. `FileRead`, `PatchApplied`, `MemoryRetrieved`, `ContextBundleReturned`, `DiagnosticObserved`); confirm serde output uses the canonical wire form from Phase 1 identity, not a path string or raw name.\n2. Verify event payloads round-trip back to identity targets: take a serialized event, deserialize via `EventReader`, resolve every `StableRef` through the Phase 1 resolver, and confirm the resolution returns the same identity object that was written.\n3. Verify memory links reference stable identities not transient names: take a `MemoryLink` with `target = MemoryLinkTarget::Symbol(SymbolId)`; rename or refactor the underlying symbol; confirm the link still resolves to the renamed symbol via the resolver, and that the link's `target_id` did not need to change.\n4. Verify memory evidence anchors carry stable identities: confirm `EvidenceAnchor::FileSpan` carries `FileId` (not a path string) and `EvidenceAnchor::DocSection` carries `DocSectionId` (not a heading string).\n5. Verify migration (T22) preserves identity references: pre-migration legacy memories that referenced files-by-path are post-migration memories that reference files-by-`FileId`; assert no path strings survive in `memory_evidence` or `memory_links` payloads.\n6. Verify event capture (T15) records identity-typed references: instrument a representative tool call, assert the emitted event's `references: Vec<StableRef>` contains the right typed variants (no strings).\n7. Verify replay preserves the contract: replay an event log from scratch (T17 + T24 fixtures) and assert that every reconstituted memory still has identity-resolvable evidence anchors after replay.\n8. Verify schema-level enforcement: every column that holds an identity (`provenance_event_ids_json`, `event_id`, `memory_id`, `target_id`) is constrained to the right shape; no schema drift between the identity, event, and memory layers permits raw strings where typed ids are expected.\n9. Add the cross-layer contract test file at `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/contract_tests/identity_event_memory.rs` (create `contract_tests/mod.rs` if absent and wire it into `lib.rs`). Tests in this file exercise the round-trip end-to-end: identity → event payload → event store → event reader → memory writer → memory store → memory reader → identity resolver, asserting equality at every boundary.\n10. Run `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib contract_tests::identity_event_memory` and confirm every test passes; record the test names in the review output.\n\n## Required sections in the review output file\n\n`docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R26-contract-identity-events-memory.md` with these mandatory headings:\n\n- `## Contract surfaces` — enumerate every cross-layer surface this gate covers: identity → event payload, event payload → identity resolution, identity → memory link target, identity → evidence anchor, event provenance on memory, replay-preserved identity, migration-preserved identity. For each surface, name the code module that defines it.\n- `## Round-trip evidence` — for each surface, the test name in `contract_tests/identity_event_memory.rs` that proves the round-trip, plus the assertion strategy (byte equivalence, resolver equivalence, or identity-id equivalence).\n- `## Schema regression coverage` — confirm no schema drift: list every column across `events`, `event_payloads`, `memories`, `memory_links`, `memory_evidence`, `memory_accesses` that holds an identity reference, and confirm it uses the typed identity shape (not a raw path/name). Include a golden-schema diff if any column type changed since the layer's own review.\n- `## Findings` — every defect, missing surface, or weak test, each with a severity (blocker / major / minor) and the owner.\n- `## Verdict` — `APPROVED` / `APPROVED WITH FOLLOW-UPS` / `REJECTED`. A `REJECTED` verdict blocks T27 (Phase 4 retrieval) from starting.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R26-contract-identity-events-memory.md` — review file exists.\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/contract_tests/identity_event_memory.rs` — contract test module exists.\n- `grep -q '## Contract surfaces' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R26-contract-identity-events-memory.md` — surfaces section present.\n- `grep -q '## Round-trip evidence' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R26-contract-identity-events-memory.md` — round-trip evidence section present.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib contract_tests::identity_event_memory` — every contract test passes; the verdict in the review may not be APPROVED if this command fails.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Review markdown file exists.\n- [ ] Every required section present with concrete content (no placeholder text).\n- [ ] Contract tests added (R26) and passing: `contract_tests::identity_event_memory` covers every surface listed in `## Contract surfaces`.\n- [ ] Verdict declared.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15982,"cache_read_input_tokens":85859,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":15982,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01KTEqX34f6x4nqNqXUnhApL","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"0694224a-1867-436e-8100-29cadefa6c74","request_id":"req_011Cb7NNhAmfrKHCVCozvQXS","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 2+3+Gate task briefs"}
