{"type":"system","subtype":"task_progress","task_id":"a163eb6f432e922f5","tool_use_id":"toolu_015qAoQeXM7HFtFDzBbPkUNq","description":"Writing docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T52.md","subagent_type":"general-purpose","usage":{"total_tokens":102083,"tool_uses":33,"duration_ms":702999},"last_tool_name":"Write","uuid":"aa9893cf-362d-4d88-9aa6-c36986ed3ea8","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_015MDyAMJnW12qQpzjxve9XN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WrFxVwt9Js58Ki46kL9WEi","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T52.md","content":"# T52 — Phase 7 — Stale surfacing in workflow bundles + label discipline (no trusted display of stale/contradicted)\n\n**Phase:** 7\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** T48, T49, T50, T51\n**Spec anchor:** [§Verification Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#8-verification-engine), [§Phase 7: Verification And Freshness](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-7-verification-and-freshness), [§Non-Negotiable Product Properties](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#non-negotiable-product-properties)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task enforces the non-negotiable from spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties: \"Every stale or contradicted memory is surfaced as such, not hidden behind recency.\" It implements the label-discipline layer that sits between the verifier (T48–T51) and every consumer that produces a workflow bundle (Phase 4 retrieval, Phase 8 workflow engine, Phase 10 review UI). A memory in `stale`, `contradicted`, `superseded`, `expired`, or `invalidated` MUST never appear as trusted guidance in any bundle; if surfaced at all, it must carry an unambiguous label and live in a separately-tagged section so an assistant cannot misread it as authoritative. Phase 7 DoD is binding: \"stale or contradicted memory cannot appear as normal trusted guidance.\"\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> §Non-Negotiable Product Properties: \"Every stale or contradicted memory is surfaced as such, not hidden behind recency.\"\n\n> Phase 7 DoD: \"stale or contradicted memory cannot appear as normal trusted guidance; verification results are explainable and queryable.\"\n\n> §Verification Engine: \"Verification outputs: `verified`; `unverified`; `in_review`; `stale`; `contradicted`; `superseded`; `expired`; `invalidated`.\"\n\n> §Risks — Stale Memory Leakage: \"Control: ... stale labels in all memory surfaces, and tests that stale memory cannot rank as trusted.\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: T48–T51 — the verifier produces the eight states; this task makes downstream bundle producers respect them.\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/intelligence/` — current workflow tools (`prepare_change`, `get_context_capsule`, `expand_context`) that assemble bundles. Phase 8 will redesign these; this task adds the label-discipline contract they must obey.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/` — `VerificationStatus` column from T48 is the input.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/query/` — ranking layer that must not promote stale memories.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/identity/` — `MemoryId` used in bundle entries.\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Single source of truth, §Naming, §Tests as documentation, §Observability; Lattice rules on doc-heading citation; spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties bullet on stale surfacing + §Verification Engine outputs + §Risks Stale Memory Leakage. Copy all three into the top-of-file doc comment on `verification/surfacing.rs`.\n2. In `verification/surfacing.rs`, define `pub enum BundleSection { Trusted, Stale, Contradicted, Superseded, Expired, Invalidated, InReview, Unverified }` and `pub struct LabeledMemory { memory_id, section: BundleSection, label_reason: String, content }`. The `Trusted` section is reserved for `Verified` memories only.\n3. Implement `pub fn classify(memory: &Memory) -> BundleSection` — a total, deterministic mapping from `VerificationStatus` to `BundleSection`. Exhaustive `match` (no `_` arm) so adding a new state forces an explicit decision.\n4. Implement `SurfacingPipeline::partition(memories: Vec<Memory>) -> SurfacedBundle` returning `SurfacedBundle { trusted: Vec<LabeledMemory>, advisory: Vec<LabeledMemory> }` where `advisory` carries every non-trusted memory tagged with its `BundleSection` and a one-line `label_reason` (e.g. \"File `src/foo.rs` line 42 content changed since 2026-04-01\"). The advisory list is what callers MAY display under an explicitly-labeled section; the trusted list is what they may treat as authoritative.\n5. Forbid stale memories from `trusted`: a debug-assertions invariant inside `partition` panics if any non-`Verified` memory leaks into the trusted list; release builds filter and emit `tracing::error!(\"stale_in_trusted_bundle\", memory_id, status)`.\n6. Suppress stale memories from ranking promotion: extend the existing ranker signal list (from Phase 4) to include `verification_status` as a hard precondition — only `Verified` enters the trusted bundle's top-N. Non-verified memories may still be returned in the advisory list, ranked separately.\n7. Add a `SurfacingPipeline::format_reason(memory, verdict) -> String` helper that produces the human-readable `label_reason` consistently across all callers. Single source of truth for label text — no caller composes its own string.\n8. Define the contract surface (`pub trait BundleProducer { fn surface(memories: Vec<Memory>) -> SurfacedBundle; }`) so Phase 4 retrieval (R33-era code) and Phase 8 workflow tools both implement the same interface and cannot diverge.\n9. In `verification/surfacing_tests.rs`, write tests that: (a) `Verified` memories land in `trusted`, every other state lands in `advisory` with the matching `BundleSection`, (b) the debug-assertions invariant fires if a test seam injects a `Stale` memory into `trusted`, (c) `label_reason` is non-empty and references the verifier's structured reason payload from T48/T49/T50/T51 (file id, span, scope, expiry), (d) the ranker top-N excludes every non-`Verified` memory regardless of score, (e) `classify` covers all eight `VerificationStatus` variants (exhaustiveness).\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/surfacing.rs` — `BundleSection`, `LabeledMemory`, `SurfacedBundle`, `SurfacingPipeline::partition`, `format_reason`, `BundleProducer` trait, debug-assertions invariant, ranker hard precondition.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/surfacing_tests.rs` — classification exhaustiveness, trusted/advisory partitioning, debug-assert guard, label-reason content, ranker exclusion.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/surfacing.rs` — confirms the surfacing module exists.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib verification::surfacing_tests` — every surfacing + label-discipline unit test passes.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10. `classify` is a flat `match`; `partition` is a single pass + invariant check.\n- Single source of truth: every bundle-producing surface implements `BundleProducer` and goes through `SurfacingPipeline::partition`; no caller composes a trusted-versus-advisory split manually. `format_reason` owns the label-text format.\n- Error handling: typed `SurfacingError` for the (small) failure modes (ranker integration not initialized). No bare `unwrap`. Stale-in-trusted is a `tracing::error!` + filter in release, panic in debug.\n- Naming: `BundleSection::Trusted`, `LabeledMemory`, `partition`, `format_reason`. No `Manager`/`Helper`.\n- Schema parity: `BundleSection` variants map 1:1 to `VerificationStatus` variants; if a new status is added, `classify` will fail to compile (exhaustive `match`).\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Observability: every release-mode stale-in-trusted filter emits `tracing::error!(\"stale_in_trusted_bundle\", memory_id, status, caller_module)`; partition counts emit a `tracing::debug!` per call.\n- Doc citation: file-top comment cites `## Non-Negotiable Product Properties` \"Every stale or contradicted memory is surfaced as such\", `## 8. Verification Engine` outputs list, and `## Risks — Stale Memory Leakage` (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` § Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content.\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: classifier, partitioner, debug-assertions invariant, ranker hard precondition, and the `BundleProducer` contract all ship in this task. Wiring into Phase 4 retrieval and Phase 8 workflow tools is the responsibility of those phases — but the contract surface they MUST implement is defined here.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed (existing bundle types now flow through `SurfacedBundle`), the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed and the architecture doc was updated in the same task.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13920,"cache_read_input_tokens":87276,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":13920,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":51,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015qAoQeXM7HFtFDzBbPkUNq","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"b4248f27-337c-463d-af81-48fca314e0ec","request_id":"req_011Cb7NTyC4xxGsapJgX4yFX","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 6+7+Gate task briefs"}
