{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01B3ExiWf97Ku1iLhAq6xya5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fv9dE6NHj9KinQYzsUTtWm","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T68.md","content":"# T68 — Phase 9 — Regression dashboard / CLI report\n\n**Phase:** 9\n**Type:** backend\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T65, T66\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-9-metrics-and-evaluation)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task ships the `lattice_report` binary and its supporting `metrics/report.rs` module so operators and CI can render the full Phase 9 metric set from the T65 collector and the T66 benchmark output. Spec §Phase 9 Deliverables names \"regression dashboard or CLI report\" as binding and the Phase 9 DoD requires that \"changes to retrieval, memory, and workflow behavior can be evaluated without relying on anecdote.\" The CLI is the surface that turns the metrics module into something a human or CI job can read.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 9 Deliverables: …regression dashboard or CLI report.\"\n\n> \"Definition of done: changes to retrieval, memory, and workflow behavior can be evaluated without relying on anecdote.\" (spec §Phase 9)\n\n> \"Initial targets: 30 percent fewer discovery tool calls on benchmark tasks; 40 percent fewer irrelevant file reads; 80 percent memory inclusion precision on curated memory benchmarks; zero trusted display of known contradicted memory; zero trusted display of known stale memory without stale label; 90 percent correct relevant-test recommendation on curated tasks.\" (spec §Measurable Success Criteria)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs:\n  - T65 — `MetricsCollector`, `MetricSignal`, `MetricValue`, `MetricScope`, `MetricSource`.\n  - T66 — `golden_anchors.json` and the JSON benchmark report from `cognitive_workspace_benchmark`.\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/bin/` — current daemon binary location; the new CLI binary lives alongside.\n  - `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/baseline_metrics.json` (from T04) — provides the baseline column for the report.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/` — the canonical metrics module.\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard `## Hard limits`, `## Single source of truth`, `## No broken windows`, `## Schema / model parity`, `## Observability`, `## Tests as documentation`.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Phase 9 and §Measurable Success Criteria in full.\n2. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/report.rs` exposing: (a) `ReportInput { current: Vec<MetricValue>, baseline: Option<Vec<MetricValue>>, benchmark_report_path: PathBuf, scope: MetricScope, success_criteria: SuccessCriteriaThresholds }`; (b) `RegressionReport` rendering per-signal current value, baseline value, delta, target threshold (from spec §Measurable Success Criteria), pass/fail per row; (c) renderers for human-readable text, machine-readable JSON, and a CI-friendly summary line; (d) per-signal evidence pointer back to the contributing event/memory IDs so any regression is investigable. `SuccessCriteriaThresholds` encodes the spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial targets explicitly (30%, 40%, 80%, 0, 0, 90%) so the report's pass/fail column is grounded in the spec.\n3. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/bin/lattice_report.rs` as the CLI binary. Argument surface: `--scope`, `--time-range`, `--signals`, `--baseline <path>`, `--benchmark <path>`, `--format text|json|ci-summary`, `--output <path>`, `--fail-on-regression`. The binary loads the current metrics via the T65 collector against the active workspace, optionally loads a baseline JSON, optionally loads the T66 benchmark JSON, and renders the `RegressionReport` to stdout or the `--output` path. With `--fail-on-regression`, exits non-zero when any signal fails its spec §Measurable Success Criteria target.\n4. Author `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md` describing: report architecture, signal definitions (referencing T65), thresholds (referencing spec §Measurable Success Criteria), input/output formats, CI integration guidance, regression-investigation runbook. The doc is the operator-facing reference.\n5. Implement `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/report_tests.rs` covering: (a) deterministic rendering across all three formats; (b) baseline-vs-current delta computation; (c) target threshold pass/fail logic for each spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial target; (d) honest reporting of `null` signals (renders as `n/a` with reason, never as zero); (e) exit-code behavior of `--fail-on-regression`; (f) per-signal evidence-pointer round-trip.\n6. Wire the binary into the workspace `Cargo.toml` so `cargo build --release --bin lattice_report` produces an installable binary. Document the build/deploy path in `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md`.\n7. Workspace boundary: the CLI honors the workspace it was invoked against — it never crosses workspace boundaries even if multiple `.lattice/` paths are reachable.\n8. Honor Cadres coding standard `## Observability`: the CLI emits structured `tracing` output to stderr so CI logs capture every signal collected and every threshold evaluated.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/bin/lattice_report.rs` — `lattice_report` CLI binary collecting current metrics, optionally loading baseline + T66 benchmark JSON, rendering the regression report in text/json/ci-summary, exiting non-zero on regression when requested.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/report.rs` — `RegressionReport`, `ReportInput`, `SuccessCriteriaThresholds`, three renderers, per-signal evidence pointers; encodes spec §Measurable Success Criteria initial targets explicitly.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/metrics/report_tests.rs` — unit tests covering deterministic rendering, baseline delta, threshold pass/fail, honest null handling, exit-code behavior, evidence-pointer round-trip.\n- `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md` — operator-facing reference: architecture, signal definitions, thresholds, formats, CI integration, regression runbook.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/bin/lattice_report.rs` — confirms the binary entry point exists at the harness path.\n- `test -f docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md` — confirms the operator doc exists at the harness path.\n- `cd daemon && cargo build --release --bin lattice_report` — the binary compiles cleanly with the rest of the workspace.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib metrics::report_tests` — every report test passes (rendering determinism, baseline delta, threshold logic, null handling, exit-code behavior, evidence-pointer round-trip).\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file (split `report.rs` per renderer if needed).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10.\n- Schema parity: `RegressionReport`, `ReportInput`, `SuccessCriteriaThresholds` derive `Serialize`, `Deserialize`, `Debug`, `Clone`; JSON output schema documented in `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md`.\n- No silent error handling — every IO/parse failure surfaces with a typed error and a non-zero exit code; honest `null` values render as `n/a` with reason, never zero.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code; no unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Public API names follow intent-over-mechanism naming (`SuccessCriteriaThresholds::memory_inclusion_precision`, not `Thresholds::mip`).\n- For SQLite: storage access goes through T65 `MetricsCollector`; no raw SQL in the binary or report module.\n- Observability: binary emits structured `tracing` to stderr with `scope`, `signal_count`, `pass_count`, `fail_count`, `format` fields per invocation.\n- Doc citation: cite spec headings `## Phase 9: Metrics And Evaluation` and `## Measurable Success Criteria` in `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-metrics-report.md` and the binary source.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command in tasks.json passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: all three render formats ship; `--fail-on-regression` is implemented; the operator doc is complete (no \"TBD\" sections).\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed; the existing `lattice` daemon binary is unaffected.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3269,"cache_read_input_tokens":103711,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3269,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":59,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_012n7S8LWZzY1cvitTHPzudV","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"279282f3-a4da-48f1-994d-a044bce886f7","request_id":"req_011Cb7NY8HNbB9Meugrxe9qx","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 8+9+Gate task briefs"}
