{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019ScAFhwj15KgrT4jB8Uvi8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y7bk4NhaqVDgskubuhfnSK","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T83.md","content":"# T83 — Phase 11 — Partial-index handling + workspace-boundary tests\n\n**Phase:** 11\n**Type:** tests\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** R79\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 11: Hardening](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-11-hardening), [§Non-Negotiable Product Properties](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#non-negotiable-product-properties), [§Scope Leakage](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#scope-leakage)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task delivers two test modules that enforce two of the spec's hardest invariants: partial indexes must degrade gracefully (no panics, no silent dropped results), and workspace boundaries must hold (no silent broad workspace reads bypassing ignore rules; no cross-workspace memory leakage). Spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties states \"no silent broad workspace reads that bypass ignore rules or workspace boundaries\"; spec §Scope Leakage names \"user/org/branch memories leak into wrong workspaces\" as a risk whose control is \"scope-aware queries, enforced filters in store APIs, and negative tests.\" This task provides those negative tests.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 11 deliverables: ... partial-index handling; workspace-boundary tests; ...\"\n\n> \"No silent broad workspace reads that bypass ignore rules or workspace boundaries.\" (spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties)\n\n> \"Risk: user/org/branch memories leak into wrong workspaces. Control: scope-aware queries, enforced filters in store APIs, and negative tests.\" (spec §Scope Leakage)\n\n> \"Tests for ordering, replay, corruption handling, and workspace scoping.\" (spec §Phase 2 deliverables)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: R79 (contract gate) — confirms the daemon API the tests exercise is stable.\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/indexer/` (incremental file → graph indexer).\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/parser/` (per-language parsers; partial parses on syntax errors).\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/` (memory store with scope filters).\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/` (event reader with workspace filters).\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/workspace/` (or wherever workspace boundary enforcement lives).\n- Standards files to honor: `coding.md` (tests as documentation, observability); `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties (workspace boundary rule), §Scope Leakage (negative tests required), §Phase 11 deliverables, and `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/workspace/` (or equivalent) so the boundary contract is pinned.\n2. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/partial_index_tests.rs` covering:\n   - **Syntax-error fixture**: a file containing valid code interleaved with sections that fail to parse; assert the indexer produces a partial graph (parsed sections present, failed sections marked as such), emits an `IndexFailure` event per file, and that queries against the partial graph return well-formed answers (no panics, no `unwrap` on missing nodes).\n   - **Mid-parse interrupt**: simulate a parser timeout or panic on a single file; assert the indexer continues with the remaining files and the partial index remains queryable.\n   - **Missing referenced file**: indexer encounters an `imports` reference whose target file is in the ignore list; assert the edge is created with a \"target-ignored\" marker, not silently dropped or attempted as a broad read.\n   - **Stale-on-read**: after a file is modified but before re-index completes, queries return results marked with the old freshness timestamp; assert the freshness label is correct and the operator can detect the staleness without seeing stale claims as `verified`.\n   - **Index-cold start**: query the daemon during the first incremental index pass; assert the partial-index responses include an explicit \"indexing in progress\" marker per spec §10 indexing-health view requirements.\n3. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/workspace_boundary_tests.rs` covering:\n   - **Ignore rule honored**: configure a workspace with `.gitignore`/`.latticeignore` rules; assert no file matched by the rules ever shows up in any query result. Repeat for `search_symbols`, `get_context_capsule`, `prepare_change`, `expand_context`, `impact_from_diff`, and `find_relevant_tests`.\n   - **No broad workspace read**: a query whose anchors don't resolve must not silently fall back to reading the entire workspace. Assert the daemon returns a \"no anchors resolved\" error or empty result with a documented marker, never a 10k-file scan dump per `## Non-Negotiable Product Properties`.\n   - **Cross-workspace memory scope leakage**: create memories in workspace A with scope `repo` and `user`; open workspace B and query for memories; assert `repo`-scoped memories from A do not leak into B, and that `user`-scoped memories appear only when explicitly opted in via the documented cross-workspace query parameter.\n   - **Branch scope leakage**: in workspace A on branch `main`, create memories scoped to `branch=main`; switch to branch `feature/x`; assert branch-scoped memories from `main` do not appear unless the query explicitly requests cross-branch.\n   - **Session scope leakage**: create memories scoped to session S1; in session S2 query for memories; assert session-scoped memories do not appear.\n   - **Event workspace scoping**: events emitted in workspace A do not appear in event-trace queries from workspace B (per spec §3 envelope `workspace_id` field).\n   - **Path-traversal attempt**: a query whose path argument contains `..` segments that resolve outside the workspace root must be rejected with an explicit error, not silently followed.\n4. Each test asserts the negative invariant: the leaked / forbidden item does NOT appear. Tests use direct store-API calls plus full-stack tool calls so both layers are validated.\n5. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release` then `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::partial_index_tests` and `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::workspace_boundary_tests` and confirm every test passes.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/partial_index_tests.rs` — syntax-error, mid-parse interrupt, missing-referenced-file, stale-on-read, and index-cold-start scenarios.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/workspace_boundary_tests.rs` — ignore-rule, no-broad-fallback, cross-workspace-memory, branch-scope, session-scope, event-workspace-scope, and path-traversal scenarios.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/partial_index_tests.rs` — confirms the partial-index test module exists.\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/workspace_boundary_tests.rs` — confirms the workspace-boundary test module exists.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::partial_index_tests` — runs every partial-index test.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::workspace_boundary_tests` — runs every workspace-boundary test.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file (split per scenario family if it exceeds).\n- Function length ≤50 lines per test.\n- Tests as documentation: each test name describes the negative invariant it asserts (e.g. `test_ignored_file_never_appears_in_search_symbols`, `test_branch_scoped_memory_does_not_leak_to_other_branch`).\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- No silent error handling — every assertion failure panics with the scenario and the leaked item.\n- Observability: workspace-boundary failures emit `tracing` events under a dedicated `security` target so production violations are alertable.\n- Doc citation: comments cite `## Non-Negotiable Product Properties`, `## Scope Leakage`, and `## Phase 11: Hardening` (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] Every partial-index and workspace-boundary scenario named above is covered with one test per behavior.\n- [ ] Negative-test coverage extends across both store APIs and tool calls (both layers validated).\n- [ ] No deferred work: every scope axis from spec §4 (session, branch, repo, user, organization) covered; migration (T84), docs (T85), runbook (T86) are sibling Phase 11 tasks, not deferrals.\n- [ ] After build, deploy per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy procedure.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":101320,"cache_read_input_tokens":10845,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":101320,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XjrTa6YAS1dmMW989ZPauZ","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"088d5452-0998-45e8-bcc5-f5a973823518","request_id":"req_011Cb7NGicAyFMeCwEAwKwU2","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 10+11+Final task briefs"}
