{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_015MDyAMJnW12qQpzjxve9XN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XUSNhUJXNrHsJJju4KrsW8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T53.md","content":"# T53 — Phase 7 — Verification tests (stale never displayed as trusted, scope leakage blocked)\n\n**Phase:** 7\n**Type:** tests\n**Model class:** balanced\n**Depends on:** T48, T49, T50, T51, T52\n**Spec anchor:** [§Verification Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#8-verification-engine), [§Phase 7: Verification And Freshness](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-7-verification-and-freshness), [§Non-Negotiable Product Properties](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#non-negotiable-product-properties), [§Risks — Stale Memory Leakage](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#stale-memory-leakage), [§Risks — Scope Leakage](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#scope-leakage)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task ships the cross-module integration suite that proves Phase 7's two non-negotiable invariants end-to-end: (1) stale, contradicted, superseded, expired, or invalidated memory NEVER appears in the trusted section of any bundle the system produces, and (2) scope-leak attempts (cross-branch, cross-workspace, cross-organization) are blocked at the store boundary, return zero leaked rows, and emit the audit event. Unit tests in T48–T52 cover each module in isolation; this task wires them together so the spec's stale-surfacing and scope-leakage risk controls are demonstrably enforced in the running system, not just in theory.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> §Non-Negotiable Product Properties: \"Every stale or contradicted memory is surfaced as such, not hidden behind recency.\"\n\n> §Risks — Stale Memory Leakage: \"Control: freshness indexes, graph-change-triggered verification, stale labels in all memory surfaces, and tests that stale memory cannot rank as trusted.\"\n\n> §Risks — Scope Leakage: \"Control: scope-aware queries, enforced filters in store APIs, and negative tests.\"\n\n> Phase 7 DoD: \"stale or contradicted memory cannot appear as normal trusted guidance\".\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: T48 (verifier core + existence checks), T49 (span validation), T50 (scope enforcement + negative tests), T51 (expiry + incremental), T52 (surfacing + label discipline).\n- Existing repo files this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/` — the full module shipped by T48–T52.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/` — memory store and Phase 3 evidence/scopes.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/` — `MemoryScopeFiltered` and `MemoryConsolidated` event payloads asserted on in tests.\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/graph/` — graph snapshot fixtures for incremental-verification tests.\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Tests as documentation, §Hard limits, §No broken windows; Lattice rules on doc-heading citation.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Phase 7 DoD + §Non-Negotiable Product Properties stale-surfacing bullet + §Risks Stale Memory Leakage + §Risks Scope Leakage. Copy all four into the top-of-file doc comment on `integration_tests.rs`.\n2. Build a `VerificationHarness` (top of file or sibling support module): seeds a temp SQLite store with the Phase 1/2/3/6/7 schemas, registers the indexer hook for incremental verification, sets up a fake LLM driver only where consolidation interplay is required, exposes a `bundle_through_surfacing` helper that takes raw memories and runs them through `SurfacingPipeline::partition` to assert on the trusted/advisory split.\n3. Write `test_stale_memory_never_appears_in_trusted_bundle` (covers T48/T49/T52): seed a memory whose evidence cites file `F`, modify the span content in `F`, run incremental verification, then call `bundle_through_surfacing(retrieved_memories)`; assert the memory is in `advisory` with `BundleSection::Stale` and NOT in `trusted`.\n4. Write `test_contradicted_memory_never_appears_in_trusted_bundle` (covers T48 + Phase 6 contradiction): seed two contradicting memories, trigger the Phase 6 contradiction job, apply the proposal flipping one to `contradicted`, then bundle and assert it is in `advisory` with `BundleSection::Contradicted`.\n5. Write `test_expired_memory_never_appears_in_trusted_bundle` (covers T51): seed a memory with `expires_at = now - 1s`, run `ExpiryScanner::scan`, then bundle and assert the memory is in `advisory` with `BundleSection::Expired`.\n6. Write `test_invalidated_memory_never_appears_in_trusted_bundle` (covers T48): seed a memory whose evidence cites file `F`, delete `F`, run incremental verification, bundle, assert `BundleSection::Invalidated`.\n7. Write `test_scope_leak_blocked_at_store_boundary_for_all_scopes` (covers T50): seed memories of each scope (session / branch / repo / organization), call `list_memories` with a non-matching `ScopeFilter` for each scope, assert zero leaked rows AND a `MemoryScopeFiltered` event per leak attempt.\n8. Write `test_ranker_excludes_non_verified_from_top_n` (covers T52 hard precondition): seed five memories, four `Stale` and one `Verified`, run the ranker with `top_n = 5`, assert only the `Verified` memory appears in the trusted list regardless of its raw score.\n9. Write `test_incremental_verification_narrows_to_changed_files_only` (covers T51): seed 100 memories citing 100 distinct files, modify only file `F_07`, trigger `IncrementalVerifier::on_graph_delta`, assert exactly one memory was re-verified (use the counting test seam from T51).\n10. Write `test_verifier_emits_explainable_label_reason_for_every_non_verified_state` (covers T48/T49/T50/T51/T52): produce one memory per non-verified state, bundle, assert each `LabeledMemory.label_reason` is non-empty AND mentions the verifier's structured reason field (file id, span byte range, scope mismatch, or expiry timestamp).\n11. Wire the suite via `mod integration_tests;` in `verification/mod.rs` under `#[cfg(test)]` (match the Phase 6 convention from T46).\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/integration_tests.rs` — `VerificationHarness` plus the named behavior-per-test functions covering trusted-bundle exclusion for every non-verified state, scope-leak blocking for all four scopes, ranker exclusion, incremental-scope narrowing, and explainable label reasons.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/integration_tests.rs` — confirms the integration test file exists.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib verification::integration_tests` — every Phase 7 integration test passes.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file (split harness into `integration_test_support.rs` if approaching the ceiling).\n- Test length ≤30 lines per `#[test]` function; setup factored into the harness.\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10 for harness helpers.\n- Single source of truth: tests exercise real `verification/` modules and the real memory store; no shadow re-implementation of surfacing partitioning.\n- Naming: tests follow `test_<behavior_description>` (e.g. `test_scope_leak_blocked_at_store_boundary_for_all_scopes`).\n- Error handling: tests assert on typed outcomes (`BundleSection::Stale`, `VerificationVerdict::Invalidated`, presence of `MemoryScopeFiltered` events) rather than free-form strings.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- Observability: tests capture `tracing` output via a test subscriber where the assertion is about a log line (e.g. `scope_leak_blocked`).\n- Doc citation: file-top comment cites the four spec invariants verbatim (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` § Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] `integration_tests.rs` exists with every test from steps 3–10 implemented.\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied (no individual test exceeds 30 lines; harness factored cleanly).\n- [ ] No deferred work: every Phase 7 invariant is covered end-to-end here; no \"leave for later\" placeholders.\n- [ ] If a backward-incompatible change was needed, the AGENTS.md \"Backward-compatibility and contract discipline\" section was followed and the architecture doc was updated in the same task.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13920,"cache_read_input_tokens":87276,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":13920,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":51,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015qAoQeXM7HFtFDzBbPkUNq","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"ae7c4100-5ab5-47cc-abba-b294bbedb9ae","request_id":"req_011Cb7NTyC4xxGsapJgX4yFX","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 6+7+Gate task briefs"}
