{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019ScAFhwj15KgrT4jB8Uvi8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TfnMe5KuHTgSrXysXGDcET","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T84.md","content":"# T84 — Phase 11 — Migration tests + MCP schema compatibility regression\n\n**Phase:** 11\n**Type:** tests\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** R79, T22, R64\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 11: Hardening](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-11-hardening), [§Phase 3: Memory Graph Storage](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-3-memory-graph-storage), [§Fork Strategy](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#fork-strategy), [§MCP Tool Contract Principles](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#mcp-tool-contract-principles)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task delivers two test modules that enforce the two long-term-compatibility surfaces of the fork: the storage migration path from the legacy Lattice schemas (Phase 3 memory rows, identity model, event-absent state) into the new schemas, and the MCP schema compatibility regression that confirms every backward-compat shim from R64 still functions. Spec §Phase 3 deliverables include \"migration/import path from existing Lattice memory rows\"; spec §Phase 11 deliverables list \"migration tests\" and \"MCP schema compatibility tests\" separately. Without these tests, an operator upgrading an existing Lattice deployment could silently lose memory or break a pinned assistant client.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Phase 11 deliverables: ... migration tests; MCP schema compatibility tests; ...\"\n\n> \"Migration/import path from existing Lattice memory rows.\" (spec §Phase 3 deliverables)\n\n> \"Required test families: ... storage migration tests; ... MCP schema tests; ...\" (spec §Testing Requirements)\n\n> \"Carry forward: ... structured memory groundwork; ... existing workflow tool vocabulary.\" (spec §Fork Strategy)\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: R79 (contract gate), T22 (memory migration path from legacy rows — Phase 3), R64 (MCP tool surface contract gate with backward-compat shims).\n- Existing files in the repo this task builds on:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/` (Phase 3 memory store, including the migration entry points from T22).\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/storage/` (SQLite migrations).\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp.rs` (MCP tool registry, including R64-era shims).\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-storage-migration-policy.md` (from T03 — the binding policy this test enforces).\n  - Legacy schema dumps captured during R10/R18 (assumed at `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/baselines/legacy_schemas/`).\n- Standards files to honor: `coding.md` (schema parity, observability); `AGENTS.md` (backward-compatibility discipline); `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Phase 3 deliverables (migration path), §Phase 11 deliverables (migration tests + MCP schema compat tests), §MCP Tool Contract Principles, and the T03 storage migration policy doc.\n2. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/migration_tests.rs` covering:\n   - **Legacy memory rows → new memory + links + evidence**: seed a temp SQLite database with the legacy `memories` table populated with representative rows (covering every memory class and every legacy verification status); run the migration entry point from T22; assert every legacy row maps to exactly one new memory record with the correct class, scope, and verification status; assert evidence and links are extracted from the legacy provenance JSON blob into the new `memory_evidence` and `memory_links` tables.\n   - **Legacy memory with malformed JSON evidence**: seed a row whose provenance JSON is malformed; assert the migration emits an event, quarantines the row in a `migration_quarantine` table, and does not abort the migration.\n   - **Idempotent migration**: run the migration twice; assert the second run is a no-op (no duplicate new rows, no version-table errors).\n   - **Forward migration order**: assert migrations apply in the order documented by `## Migration order` in `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-storage-migration-policy.md`; out-of-order application is rejected with a clear error.\n   - **Rollback path**: per `## Rollback` in the migration policy, assert each migration has a documented inverse; apply forward, then inverse, then forward again, and assert state is consistent.\n   - **Pre-event-log state**: seed a database that predates Phase 2 (no `events` table); assert the migration creates the events tables and bootstraps without requiring event-log data.\n   - **Large legacy dataset**: seed 100k legacy memory rows; assert the migration completes within a documented time budget and that no row is lost (count in == count out + count quarantined).\n3. Create `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp_compat_tests.rs` covering:\n   - **Every R64 shim still responds**: enumerate every legacy tool name from `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md` (T02) and assert that calling the legacy name returns a successful response shaped per the legacy schema. This is the backward-compat regression spec §MCP Tool Contract Principles requires.\n   - **Additive fields do not break legacy clients**: for every tool classified as `additive`, send a request omitting the new fields; assert the response is a valid superset (legacy fields present with original types).\n   - **Deprecated-with-deadline tools surface a warning**: for every tool classified as `deprecated-with-deadline`, assert the response includes a documented `deprecation_warning` field naming the removal date.\n   - **Compact and full render modes**: per spec §MCP Tool Contract Principles, every tool supports both modes; assert both modes return valid responses for every review-UI tool and every workflow tool.\n   - **Stable handles round-trip**: any context handle returned by a tool can be passed back via `expand_context` and resolves to the same content; assert this holds for every tool that returns handles.\n   - **Schema parity vs `mcp_schema` test**: cross-check against the existing `mcp_schema` test set so this module adds compat regression coverage without duplicating schema-shape assertions.\n4. Each test uses real daemon code paths (no mocks) and asserts both the response shape and the observable side effects (events emitted, audit rows written).\n5. Run `cd daemon && cargo build --release` then `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::migration_tests` and `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::mcp_compat_tests` and confirm every test passes.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/migration_tests.rs` — legacy-row → new-schema migration, idempotency, order, rollback, pre-event-log, and large-dataset scenarios; covers the backward-compat data path from T22.\n- `daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp_compat_tests.rs` — MCP compatibility regression covering every R64 shim, additive fields, deprecation warnings, compact/full render, and stable handles.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/hardening/migration_tests.rs` — confirms the migration test module exists.\n- `test -f daemon/crates/lattice-daemon/src/rpc/mcp_compat_tests.rs` — confirms the MCP compat test module exists.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib hardening::migration_tests` — runs every migration test.\n- `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-daemon --lib rpc::mcp_compat_tests` — runs every MCP compat test.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file (split per scenario family if needed).\n- Function length ≤50 lines per test.\n- Tests as documentation: each test name describes the migration or compatibility surface it asserts.\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, or unjustified `#[allow(...)]`.\n- No silent error handling — every assertion failure panics with the scenario and the violated invariant.\n- Schema parity: tests cross-check the migrated row count, the field-by-field mapping, and the round-trip render shapes per `coding.md` §Schema / model parity.\n- Observability: migration emits `tracing` events for each row migrated and each row quarantined; MCP compat tests assert deprecation-warning emission.\n- Doc citation: comments cite `## Phase 3: Memory Graph Storage` (migration), `## MCP Tool Contract Principles` (backward-compat), `## Phase 11: Hardening`, and the T02/T03 architecture docs by exact heading (per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Markdown Heading References).\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs).\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] Every migration scenario named above is covered; idempotency and rollback both exercised end-to-end.\n- [ ] Every MCP tool from the R64 compat matrix is exercised; deprecation warnings asserted.\n- [ ] No deferred work: every migration + compat surface from spec §Phase 3, §Phase 11, and §MCP Tool Contract Principles is covered; docs (T85) and runbook (T86) are sibling tasks, not deferrals.\n- [ ] After build, deploy per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy procedure.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":101320,"cache_read_input_tokens":10845,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":101320,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"pare