{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_015MDyAMJnW12qQpzjxve9XN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SX62PodxYTruLF7r8Lb8iA","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R54.md","content":"# R54 — Backend review — Phase 7 verification + freshness\n\n**Phase:** 7\n**Type:** review\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** T48, T49, T50, T51, T52, T53\n**Spec anchor:** [§Verification Engine](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#8-verification-engine), [§Phase 7: Verification And Freshness](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-7-verification-and-freshness), [§Non-Negotiable Product Properties](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#non-negotiable-product-properties), [§Risks](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#risks)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard; Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task is the Phase 7 backend review. It audits T48–T53 against the spec's verification contract, the §Non-Negotiable Product Properties bullets that verification directly touches (stale surfacing, no silent broad reads), the §Risks Stale Memory Leakage and Scope Leakage controls, and the coding standard. The review must produce a verdict on whether Phase 7 is ready to ship — every later phase (Phase 8 workflow engine, Phase 10 review UI) consumes the contract surfaces this phase defines, so a failed review blocks them. A pass/fail decision without cited evidence is not a review.\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> Phase 7 DoD: \"stale or contradicted memory cannot appear as normal trusted guidance; verification results are explainable and queryable.\"\n\n> §Verification Engine outputs: `verified`, `unverified`, `in_review`, `stale`, `contradicted`, `superseded`, `expired`, `invalidated`.\n\n> §Non-Negotiable Product Properties: \"Every stale or contradicted memory is surfaced as such, not hidden behind recency.\"\n\n> §Risks — Stale Memory Leakage: \"tests that stale memory cannot rank as trusted.\"\n\n> §Risks — Scope Leakage: \"scope-aware queries, enforced filters in store APIs, and negative tests.\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: T48 (verifier core + existence), T49 (span validation), T50 (scope enforcement), T51 (expiry + incremental), T52 (surfacing + label discipline), T53 (integration tests).\n- Existing repo files this task reviews:\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/` (all files)\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/memory/store.rs` (`ScopeFilter` enforcement at the store boundary, per T50)\n  - `daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/events/` (`MemoryScopeFiltered`, `MemoryConsolidated` payloads)\n- Standards: Cadres coding standard §Done means done; Lattice rules on doc-heading citation; spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties + §Risks.\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Run the full Phase 7 test suite from the repo root: `cd daemon && cargo test -p lattice-core --lib verification` and capture per-submodule pass / fail counts.\n2. Audit `T48.existence_tests`, `T49.spans_tests`, `T50.scope_leak_tests`, `T51.incremental_tests`, `T52.surfacing_tests`, `T53.integration_tests` for behavior coverage; list any spec verification-check bullet not exercised by at least one test.\n3. Audit `verification/scope_enforcement.rs` for the spec's §Scope Leakage control: confirm every store read path requires a `ScopeFilter`, confirm the debug-assertions guard exists, confirm `MemoryScopeFiltered` events are emitted on every release-build filter, confirm negative tests cover all four scopes.\n4. Audit `verification/surfacing.rs` for the stale-label discipline: confirm `classify` is exhaustive on `VerificationStatus`, confirm the debug-assertions invariant against stale-in-trusted, confirm the ranker hard precondition excludes non-`Verified` memories from `trusted`, confirm `label_reason` references the verifier's structured reason payload.\n5. Audit `verification/incremental.rs` for the no-full-rescan guarantee: confirm `on_graph_delta` walks only memories citing changed files/symbols, confirm the counting test seam from T51, confirm the bounded work budget re-enqueues overflow rather than stalling, confirm `last_verified_graph_snapshot_id` advances on success.\n6. Audit `verification/expiry.rs` for spec §Verification Engine \"time-bound memory has expired\": confirm `MarkExpired` proposal emission, idempotence on re-run, and routing through T39 (no direct writes).\n7. Audit coding-standard adherence across the verification module: file lengths via `wc -l`, function-length sampling, nesting depth on `VerifierCore::verify_memory`, `IncrementalVerifier::on_graph_delta`, `SurfacingPipeline::partition`. Record any exception and whether it carries the one-line justification per `coding.md` §Hard limits.\n8. Write the review at `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R54-verification.md` with the mandatory headings: `## Spec alignment`, `## Coding-standard alignment`, `## Stale-label discipline`, `## Scope-leak evidence`, `## Findings`, `## Verdict`. Each section cites concrete evidence (file paths, line ranges, test names, log lines). `## Verdict` states `pass` or `fail` with a one-paragraph justification; failures list the minimum-fix tasks needed before R55 / Phase 8 can begin.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R54-verification.md` — Phase 7 backend review with all six mandatory headings, concrete evidence per section, pass/fail verdict.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R54-verification.md` — confirms the review file exists.\n- `grep -q '## Spec alignment' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R54-verification.md` — `## Spec alignment` heading present.\n- `grep -q '## Stale-label discipline' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R54-verification.md` — `## Stale-label discipline` heading present.\n- `grep -q '## Scope-leak evidence' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R54-verification.md` — `## Scope-leak evidence` heading present.\n- `grep -q '## Verdict' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R54-verification.md` — `## Verdict` heading present.\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines (review doc; `wc -l` it).\n- Function length ≤50 lines, nesting ≤3, cyclomatic ≤10 — not applicable (review doc).\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code.\n- No unjustified suppressions.\n- Doc citation: every claim cites a code path (`daemon/crates/lattice-core/src/verification/...`) or a spec heading; vague phrases like \"looks fine\" are not evidence.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R54-verification.md` exists with all six mandatory headings.\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] No deferred work: every spec bullet under §Verification Engine, §Phase 7, the verification-touching §Non-Negotiable Product Properties bullets, and the §Risks Stale Memory Leakage / Scope Leakage controls is addressed in the review.\n- [ ] If the verdict is `fail`, the findings section lists the minimum-fix tasks needed before R55 / Phase 8 can begin.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13920,"cache_read_input_tokens":87276,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":13920,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":51,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015qAoQeXM7HFtFDzBbPkUNq","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"caf2b8e4-888e-498