{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_019ScAFhwj15KgrT4jB8Uvi8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012LWeY2EjcfBk7ufhaBmdDS","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/T85.md","content":"# T85 — Phase 11 — Documentation suite (all 11 required docs from spec §Documentation Requirements)\n\n**Phase:** 11\n**Type:** docs\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** R47, R54, R63, R70, R78\n**Spec anchor:** [§Documentation Requirements](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#documentation-requirements), [§Phase 11: Hardening](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-11-hardening)\n**Standards:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); Lattice project rules (`/home/pete/cadres/lattice/CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`).\n\n## Goal\n\nThis task delivers the complete documentation suite Phase 11 mandates. Spec §Documentation Requirements lists eleven required documents: successor architecture overview, MCP contract reference (which T61 was responsible for; this task collects/links it), memory model reference, event log design, consolidation design, retrieval/ranking design, verification/freshness design, operator guide, migration guide from Lattice, benchmark/evaluation guide, extension review UI guide. Spec §Phase 11 DoD includes \"documentation for setup, operations, memory semantics, and workflow behavior\"; this task closes the documentation surface area so the system is \"production-grade for repeated agent use, not only successful on a toy repo.\"\n\n## Spec excerpts that drive this task\n\n> \"Required docs: successor architecture overview; MCP contract reference; memory model reference; event log design; consolidation design; retrieval/ranking design; verification/freshness design; operator guide; migration guide from Lattice; benchmark/evaluation guide; extension review UI guide.\" (spec §Documentation Requirements)\n\n> \"Docs must be updated in the same change as public behavior changes.\" (spec §Documentation Requirements)\n\n> \"Phase 11 DoD: the system is production-grade for repeated agent use, not only successful on a toy repo.\"\n\n## Inputs\n\n- Dependency outputs: R47 (Phase 6 consolidation), R54 (Phase 7 verification), R63 (Phase 8 workflow + memory tools including the MCP contract reference from T61), R70 (Phase 9 metrics + benchmarks), R78 (Phase 10 review UI).\n- Existing architecture docs this suite must reference (not duplicate):\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-architecture.md` (T02)\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-compatibility-policy.md` (T02)\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-crate-boundary-plan.md` (T03)\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-storage-migration-policy.md` (T03)\n  - `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-event-log-compaction.md` (assumed from T16)\n  - Plus any MCP contract reference produced in Phase 8 from T61.\n  - Plus all `docs/architecture/2026-04-11-*.md` legacy docs (referenced by heading, not duplicated).\n- Standards files to honor: `coding.md` (no broken windows, single source of truth — every concept lives in exactly one doc); `lattice/CLAUDE.md` (Markdown heading references).\n\n## Steps\n\n1. Read spec §Documentation Requirements in full so the eleven required documents are pinned. Cross-reference each with the existing architecture docs to identify which ones are net-new vs. consolidation-of-existing.\n2. Create `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-successor-architecture-overview.md`. This is the front-door doc operators read first. Required headings: `## Overview`, `## Three substrates`, `## Identity model`, `## Storage layout`, `## Read paths`, `## Write paths`, `## Operational invariants`. Reference but do not duplicate the per-substrate design docs created below.\n3. Create `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-model-reference.md`. The authoritative reference for the memory graph. Required headings: `## Memory classes` (all classes from spec §4 including `CounterMemory`), `## Memory record fields` (every field from spec §4 with type, nullability, default), `## Memory link types` (all link types from spec §4 with reciprocity rules), `## Scope semantics` (session / branch / repo / user / organization), `## Verification status state machine`, `## Freshness policy`, `## Validity conditions and invalidation triggers`, `## Memory evidence`, `## Memory access history and usefulness scores`.\n4. Create `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-event-log-design.md`. The authoritative reference for the event log. Required headings: `## Append-only invariant`, `## Event kinds` (all 20 from spec §3), `## Event envelope` (every field from spec §3), `## Payload spillover`, `## Compaction snapshots`, `## Replay semantics`, `## Hot-path budgets`, `## Workspace and session scoping`.\n5. Create `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-design.md`. The authoritative reference for the consolidation engine. Required headings: `## Job types`, `## Modes` (synchronous / background / manual-review / replay), `## LLM-driven consolidation` (proposal-only, provenance, queue depth, cost budgets per spec §6), `## Proposal apply and reject flow`, `## Reversibility`, `## Replay-safe execution`.\n6. Create `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-retrieval-ranking-design.md`. The authoritative reference for retrieval. Required headings: `## Pipeline` (the ten-step pipeline from spec §7), `## Candidate sources`, `## Ranking signals` (all 13 from spec §7), `## Diagnostic mode`, `## Compact mode`, `## Inclusion reasons and expansion handles`, `## Forward compatibility with working memory`.\n7. Create `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-verification-freshness-design.md`. The authoritative reference for verification. Required headings: `## Verification checks` (every check from spec §8), `## Verification outputs` (all eight statuses from spec §8), `## Incremental verification`, `## Graph-change triggers`, `## Branch and workspace scope enforcement`, `## Time-bound expiry`.\n8. Create `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-operator-guide.md`. Operator-facing how-to. Required headings: `## Installation`, `## Initial setup`, `## Daily operations`, `## Review surface tour` (cross-link to the extension UI guide), `## Metrics dashboard`, `## Troubleshooting`. Include the `pkill -f lattice && cp daemon/target/release/lattice extension/bin/ && cp daemon/target/release/lattice ~/.vscode/extensions/lattice.lattice-0.1.0/bin/` deploy sequence from `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy.\n9. Create `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-migration-from-lattice.md`. Migration guide. Required headings: `## Overview`, `## Migration steps` (one ordered checklist), `## Pre-flight checks`, `## Data preservation guarantees`, `## Rollback procedure`, `## Post-migration verification`. Reference the storage migration policy from T03 by heading.\n10. Create `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-benchmark-evaluation-guide.md`. Benchmark how-to. Required headings: `## Overview`, `## Running baseline benchmarks`, `## Running large-repo benchmarks` (cross-link to T80 fixtures), `## Interpreting the metrics report`, `## Regression detection`, `## Initial targets` (the §Measurable Success Criteria initial targets verbatim).\n11. Create `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-extension-review-ui-guide.md`. Extension review UI walkthrough. Required headings: `## Overview`, `## Opening the review panel`, `## Memory inbox`, `## Promotion queue and contradiction queue`, `## Stale view and evidence inspector`, `## Event trace and retrieval explanation`, `## Consolidation, indexing, and graph health`, `## Accept/reject workflow`. Cross-link to T71–T76 file paths.\n12. For every doc, cite spec headings exactly per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Markdown Heading References. Do not duplicate spec content; cite the heading and add interpretation only.\n13. Confirm the MCP contract reference produced by T61 (Phase 8) is linked from the operator guide and the architecture overview. If T61 did not deliver a standalone file, this task documents the link to the relevant section in `mcp.rs` doc-comments or the inline tool documentation.\n\n## Files expected\n\n- `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-successor-architecture-overview.md` — top-level architecture overview.\n- `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-model-reference.md` — authoritative memory model reference.\n- `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-event-log-design.md` — authoritative event log design.\n- `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-design.md` — authoritative consolidation design.\n- `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-retrieval-ranking-design.md` — authoritative retrieval and ranking design.\n- `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-verification-freshness-design.md` — authoritative verification and freshness design.\n- `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-operator-guide.md` — operator how-to.\n- `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-migration-from-lattice.md` — migration guide.\n- `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-benchmark-evaluation-guide.md` — benchmark + evaluation how-to.\n- `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-extension-review-ui-guide.md` — extension review UI walkthrough.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f docs/architecture/2026-05-16-successor-architecture-overview.md`\n- `test -f docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-model-reference.md`\n- `test -f docs/architecture/2026-05-16-event-log-design.md`\n- `test -f docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-design.md`\n- `test -f docs/architecture/2026-05-16-retrieval-ranking-design.md`\n- `test -f docs/architecture/2026-05-16-verification-freshness-design.md`\n- `test -f docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-operator-guide.md`\n- `test -f docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-migration-from-lattice.md`\n- `test -f docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-benchmark-evaluation-guide.md`\n- `test -f docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-extension-review-ui-guide.md`\n- `grep -q '## Overview' docs/architecture/2026-05-16-successor-architecture-overview.md`\n- `grep -q '## Migration steps' docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-migration-from-lattice.md`\n\n## Coding-standard checks\n\n- File length ≤800 lines per file (`wc -l` every doc).\n- No `TODO`, `FIXME`, `XXX`, commented-out code, no placeholder sections (`coming soon`).\n- Single source of truth: each concept lives in exactly one doc; cross-references use exact `## Heading` anchors per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Markdown Heading References.\n- Naming: doc filenames follow the `YYYY-MM-DD-topic.md` convention already in use in `docs/architecture/`.\n- Doc citation: every doc that depends on the spec cites the spec heading by exact text; every doc that depends on another in this suite cites the target heading by exact text. No vague \"see the architecture docs\" prose.\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every file in \"Files expected\" exists with real content (no stubs, no placeholders).\n- [ ] Every verification command passes from repo root.\n- [ ] Coding-standard checks satisfied.\n- [ ] Every spec §Documentation Requirements item is covered by at least one doc in this suite. (The eleventh required item — \"MCP contract reference\" — is produced by T61 in Phase 8 and cross-linked from this suite; if T61 did not produce a standalone file, this task documents the inline location.)\n- [ ] Every doc cross-references the spec by exact heading; nothing duplicates spec content.\n- [ ] No deferred work: every required doc shipped; the runbook + recovery playbook (T86) are the sibling task pair, not deferrals.\n- [ ] After build, deploy per `lattice/CLAUDE.md` Build/Deploy procedure (docs do not require deploy, but if any embedded paths change, the binary copies must follow).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":101320,"cache_read_input_tokens":10845,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":101320,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XjrTa6YAS1dmMW989ZPauZ","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"2f3debf8-8e1b-4768-b9f2-5ed848461be9","request_id":"req_011Cb7NGicAyFMeCwEAwKwU2","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 10+11+Final task briefs"}
