{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01KGtXP2EMVTtVtg5QavRdVh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018fzsBcFMBkmEMDyc7m4ApV","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/pete/cadres/lattice/docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/tasks/R88.md","content":"# R88 — Definition-of-Done gate — shared checklist compliance for the whole fork\n\n**Phase:** Definition-of-Done gate\n**Type:** review\n**Model class:** advanced\n**Depends on:** R87\n**Spec anchor:** [§Phase 11: Hardening](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#phase-11-hardening), [§Non-Negotiable Product Properties](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#non-negotiable-product-properties), [§Measurable Success Criteria](../../2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-plan.md#measurable-success-criteria)\n**Standards reviewed:** Cadres coding standard (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md`); UI specification (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/ui-specification.md`); definition-of-done checklist (`/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md`); execution philosophy (`/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md`).\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis review walks every section of the shared `definition-of-done-checklist.md` against the whole cognitive-workspace fork and certifies that each applicable item is satisfied or explicitly deferred with reason, owner, and target date per the execution philosophy in `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md` (\"Never defer work you can do now\"). It is the second-to-last gate before R89 final readiness; passing this review means the whole-system delivery meets the cross-cutting \"done means done\" standard that applies regardless of which phase shipped a given artifact. Silent deferrals are not permitted — the `## Explicit Deferrals` section must either be empty (no deferrals) or list every deferral with reason, owner, and target date.\n\n## Inputs to read\n\n- Every artifact from every prior phase task and every prior review (R05 through R87).\n- Shared checklist: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md` — this review walks every section.\n- Shared coding standard: `/home/pete/cadres/shared/templates/coding.md` §Done means done.\n- Execution philosophy: `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md` §Execution Philosophy (\"Never defer work you can do now. ... Never implement a workaround when the real solution exists. ... Stop reasoning about time like a human.\").\n- Spec sections this review enforces: `## Phase 11: Hardening` DoD, `## Non-Negotiable Product Properties`, `## Measurable Success Criteria`.\n\n## Review procedure\n\n1. Open `definition-of-done-checklist.md` and walk it section by section against the fork delivery. Each section below is a heading in the output file and a procedure here.\n2. **Workflow Completion**: Confirm every primary operator workflow works end to end. For the fork, the primary workflows are: (a) the assistant calling MCP tools to plan and apply a change; (b) the operator reviewing the memory inbox, accepting/rejecting promotions and contradictions, inspecting evidence, and triggering on-demand verification; (c) the operator deploying a new daemon binary via the runbook. Confirm both backend and operator-facing UI are complete for every user-visible workflow. Confirm background jobs (consolidation, verification, compaction) are complete.\n3. **Failure Handling**: Confirm validation failures return actionable errors. Confirm permission-denied is not applicable (local-first, no per-user RBAC), but workspace-boundary enforcement is verified by T83. Confirm not-found and conflict states are truthful (e.g. proposal apply on an already-applied proposal returns a clear error per T81). Confirm partial-failure behavior is defined for async paths (consolidation queue, verification jobs). Confirm UI shows loading / empty / success / failure states per R78.\n4. **Security, Tenancy, and Audit**: Confirm access control is local-first; workspace scope is enforced per T83. Confirm destructive actions (memory invalidation, high-scope promotion) require explicit operator confirm per T73. Confirm meaningful state-changing actions create event-log records per Phase 2 + Phase 8. Confirm sensitive data (event payloads with file content) is local-only and not exposed externally.\n5. **Data Integrity and Workflow Controls**: Confirm invariants are enforced at the storage layer (foreign keys on `memory_links`, `memory_evidence`; constraints on verification status enum; uniqueness on event id). Confirm workflow statuses use explicit transition rules (verification status state machine, proposal state machine). Confirm invalid transitions are blocked and tested (T81 idempotency test).\n6. **Observability and Recovery**: Confirm logs and event records provide enough context to debug production failures (T82 recovery tests; T83 workspace-boundary tests emit `security` target events). Confirm critical async paths are idempotent (T81 replay-safe consolidation). Confirm recovery steps exist (T86 recovery playbook). Confirm rollback is defined (T84 migration rollback).\n7. **Performance and Scale**: Confirm the design avoids N+1 and broad scans per spec §Non-Negotiable Product Properties (T83 no-broad-fallback test). Confirm pagination / sortable headers are server-side capable for the review UI (R78). Confirm large-repo scale is exercised (T80). Confirm known scale limits are documented (T80 results in `large_repo_results.json`).\n8. **Documentation and Operator Readiness**: Confirm architecture documentation updated for every structural change (T02, T03, T16, T85). Confirm functional documentation reflects every behavior change. Confirm manual documentation (operator guide, runbook, recovery playbook) is updated per T85 + T86. Confirm operator-facing warnings (queue at bound, dropped jobs, broken references) are documented per T76 + T86.\n9. **Verification Evidence**: Confirm unit, integration, and E2E coverage exists. Confirm test commands were executed and results captured (R87 hardening evidence + R79 contract round-trip evidence). Confirm manual verification was captured for UI-heavy changes (R78).\n10. **Explicit Deferrals**: Walk every task brief T01–T86 and every review R05–R87. List every item explicitly deferred with reason, owner, and target date. Per `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md` execution philosophy, the expected state is an empty list. Any deferral must be justified or rejected back to the build.\n\n## Required sections in the review output file\n\nThe reviewer writes to `docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R88-definition-of-done.md` with these mandatory headings (one per checklist section from `shared/templates/definition-of-done-checklist.md`; each must contain real findings, not \"n/a\"):\n\n- `## Workflow Completion` — confirm assistant workflows, operator review workflows, deploy workflow, and background jobs are all complete end-to-end. Evidence column cites the phase + task that delivered each.\n- `## Failure Handling` — validation failures, permission-denied (not applicable here, document why), not-found / conflict, partial-failure, UI states. Evidence cites the tests + reviews that prove each.\n- `## Security, Tenancy, and Audit` — access control (local-first), workspace scope, destructive-action controls, audit (event log), sensitive data handling. Evidence cites T83 + T73 + Phase 2/8.\n- `## Data Integrity and Workflow Controls` — invariants in storage layer, transition rules, blocked transitions tests. Evidence cites Phase 3 schema + T81 + T82.\n- `## Observability and Recovery` — log/audit context, idempotency, recovery steps, rollback. Evidence cites T81 + T82 + T84 + T86.\n- `## Performance and Scale` — no broad scans, pagination/sort, large-repo scale, documented limits. Evidence cites T80 + T83 + R78.\n- `## Documentation and Operator Readiness` — architecture, functional, manual, operator-facing warnings. Evidence cites T02 + T03 + T16 + T85 + T86.\n- `## Verification Evidence` — unit, integration, E2E, commands executed, manual evidence. Evidence cites R87 + R79 + R78.\n- `## Explicit Deferrals` — MUST be either empty (state explicitly: \"No deferrals. Every spec item shipped in this build per the execution philosophy.\") or list each deferral with: deferred item, reason (must be technically valid, not \"time constraint\"), owner (named individual or role), target date (specific). Per `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md`: \"Never defer work you can do now. ... Offering to 'come back to this later' or 'leave this for a follow-up' is a failure mode.\"\n\n## Verification\n\n- `test -f docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R88-definition-of-done.md` — confirms the review markdown exists.\n- `grep -q '## Workflow Completion' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R88-definition-of-done.md`\n- `grep -q '## Failure Handling' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R88-definition-of-done.md`\n- `grep -q '## Security, Tenancy, and Audit' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R88-definition-of-done.md`\n- `grep -q '## Data Integrity and Workflow Controls' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R88-definition-of-done.md`\n- `grep -q '## Observability and Recovery' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R88-definition-of-done.md`\n- `grep -q '## Performance and Scale' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R88-definition-of-done.md`\n- `grep -q '## Documentation and Operator Readiness' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R88-definition-of-done.md`\n- `grep -q '## Verification Evidence' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R88-definition-of-done.md`\n- `grep -q '## Explicit Deferrals' docs/plans/2026-05-16-cognitive-workspace-fork-build/reviews/R88-definition-of-done.md`\n\n## Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Review markdown file exists at the path verification commands check.\n- [ ] Every one of the nine checklist sections above is present with concrete content (not \"n/a\").\n- [ ] `## Explicit Deferrals` is either empty (with the explicit \"No deferrals.\" statement) or every deferral lists reason + owner + target date — no silent deferrals, no vague \"to be revisited later\" prose.\n- [ ] Every section's evidence column cites the specific task/review/test that satisfies the checklist item.\n- [ ] If any section verdict is FAIL or any deferral cannot meet the reason+owner+date bar, the gate is BLOCK and a follow-up task is opened in this build (never deferred to a future session per `/home/pete/.claude/CLAUDE.md` execution philosophy).\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":135377,"cache_read_input_tokens":10845,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":135377,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XjrTa6YAS1dmMW989ZPauZ","session_id":"88204e0b-a61b-4ed7-ba98-4fcc53be0768","uuid":"983c4a68-a9df-4c12-8da3-3966610b92f6","request_id":"req_011Cb7Nnnq1PmkU6diUQFNyf","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Write Phase 10+11+Final task briefs"}
